/-!
# Canonical sheaves, ramified cyclic covers and the covering trick

This file collects three tools of the proof of [KollarMori, Theorem 2.64].

**Push-forward of the canonical sheaf.** Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a proper birational morphism of
smooth varieties over a field `k`, with `X` of dimension `n`. The canonical map
`Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}`, adjoint to the pull-back of forms, is an isomorphism, so
`f_* ω_Y ≅ ω_X`. It is injective on sections since `f` is an isomorphism over a dense open of
the integral `Y`; it is locally surjective since the biregular locus of `f` has complement of
codimension at least two in the normal scheme `X`, across which functions extend by `S₂`.

**Ramified cyclic covers.** Let `X` be a variety over `k`, `L` a line bundle on `X`, `m ≥ 2` and
`0 ≠ s ∈ H⁰(X, Lᵐ)` with zero scheme `D`, and `p : Z ⟶ X` the ramified cyclic cover. Locally
`Z = Spec 𝒪_U[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` with `f` an equation of `D`. Over an algebraically closed field of
characteristic zero and a normal `X`, `Z` is smooth iff `X` and `D` are: away from `D` the cover
is étale, and over `D` the three local rings are hypersurfaces in `𝒪_U[T]_{(𝔭, T)}`. If `X` and
`D` are smooth and `D ≠ ∅`, then `Z` is a smooth variety and `p` is finite, flat and surjective,
`Z` being connected since the fibre over a point of `D` is one point. The reduced preimage
`R = p⁻¹(D)_red` is cut out by `T`: it is smooth, an effective Cartier divisor with
`p⁻¹(D) = m R`, and `𝒪_Z(R) ≅ p^*L`, `T` being a regular section of `p^*L`. If `D + ∑ⱼ Dⱼ` is
snc with all coefficients `1`, so is `R + ∑ⱼ p⁻¹(Dⱼ)`, by a computation with regular parameters.

**The covering trick.** If `X` is smooth projective, `Δ` an snc `ℚ`-divisor with coefficients in
`[0, 1)` and `B ≡ M + Δ`, a composite `p : Z ⟶ X` of Bloch–Gieseker and cyclic covers and a
divisor `B_Z ≡ p^* M` make `H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` a direct summand of `H^i(Z, 𝒪(-B_Z))`; the proof is
an induction on the number of distinct coefficients of `Δ`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.isIso_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap_of_isBirationalMorphism`: the canonical
  map `ω_X ⟶ f_* ω_Y` is an isomorphism.
* `MMP.Mori.smooth_ramifiedCyclicCover_comp_iff`: `Z` is smooth over `k` iff `X` and `D` are.
* `MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective`: the cover of a
  smooth variety branched along a smooth non-empty divisor is a smooth variety, and `p` is
  finite, flat and surjective.
* `MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow`: `R` is smooth and an
  effective Cartier divisor, and `p⁻¹(D) = m R`.
* `MMP.Mori.nonempty_invertibleSheaf_radical_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_iso_pullback`:
  `𝒪_Z(R) ≅ p^*L`.
* `MMP.Mori.isSNC_ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_of_isSNC`: snc divisors pull back to snc divisors.
* `MMP.Mori.exists_isFinite_retract_cohomologyOverField_divisorialSheaf_neg`: the covering
  trick, the summand being a `CategoryTheory.Retract` in `ModuleCat k`.

## Implementation notes

The canonical sheaf of a smooth variety of dimension `n` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms` of its structure morphism in degree
`n`; the isomorphism is stated for the canonical map, the adjoint of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsMap`. The source writes
`ω_Y ≅ f^* ω_X ⊗ 𝒪_Y(K)` and uses algebraic Hartogs; the proof here does the same computation
on local trivializations.

As in `MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover`, the cover is written through `N = L⁻¹` and the pairing
`σ = ⟨·, s⟩ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X`, so `s ≠ 0` reads `σ ≠ 0` and `L` is the dual `N^∨`. The scheme
`p⁻¹(D)` has ideal `p^*I_D` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap`), its reduction
has the radical ideal, and `𝒪_Z(R)` is `Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'`. The
characteristic-zero hypothesis in the smoothness criterion cannot be dropped: in characteristic
`p ≥ 3` the cover `tᵖ = x² - 1` of `𝔸¹` is singular at `x = 0`.

In the covering trick the source's smooth `D₁, …, D_s` and coefficients `a₁, …, a_s` enter only
through `Δ = ∑ᵢ aᵢ Dᵢ`, so the datum is a `ℚ`-divisor `Δ` with snc support and coefficients in
`[0, 1)`; the pull-back `p^* M` is a `ℚ`-divisor `M_Z` with `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.IsPullback`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori], 2.47, 2.51,
  Theorem 2.64 (Step 4), Claim 2.65, Corollary 5.77
-/

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace MMP.Mori

section CanonicalSheaf

open MMP.Intersection

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The adjoint `L ⟶ f_* M` of `j : f^* L ⟶ M` sends a section `t` of `L` over `V` to
`j (f^* t)`. -/
private lemma homEquiv_app_apply (f : Y ⟶ X) {L : X.Modules} {M : Y.Modules}
    (j : (Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L ⟶ M) (V : X.Opens) (t : Γ(L, V)) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _ j).app V t =
      j.app (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app L).app V t) := by
  simp only [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit]; rfl

/-- For a birational morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of integral schemes with `f` quasi-compact and
`Ω^n_{X/k}` invertible, the adjoint `Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}` of the Jacobian section is
injective on the sections over every open: locally a section is `r • e` for a trivializing
generator `e`, its image is `f^♯ r • j_f(f^* e)`, and on the open where `f` is an open immersion
`j_f` is bijective and `f^* e` trivializes `f^* Ω^n_{X/k}`, so `f^♯ r` vanishes on a non-empty open,
hence `r = 0`. -/
private theorem injective_app_homEquiv_jacobianSection
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] (n : ℕ)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sX n)]
    (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsIntegral Y] [QuasiCompact f] (hfb : MMP.Mori.IsBirationalMorphism f)
    (U : X.Opens) :
    Function.Injective (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _
        (jacobianSection sX f n)).val.app (op U)) := by
  have : IsDominant f := hfb.isDominant
  obtain ⟨W, hWne, hW⟩ := hfb.exists_isOpenImmersion
  let L := Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sX n
  let j := jacobianSection sX f n
  let ε := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app L
  let α := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _ j
  change Function.Injective (α.app U)
  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
  intro s hs
  choose U₀ hU₀ a hxU₀ ha using fun x : U => exists_isTrivializingGenerator L x.2
  refine TopCat.Sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq' ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).obj L)
    U₀ U (fun x => homOfLE (hU₀ x))
    (fun y hy => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, hxU₀ _⟩) _ _ fun x => ?_
  change L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hU₀ x)).op s = L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hU₀ x)).op 0
  rw [map_zero]
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (ha x).bijective.2 (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hU₀ x)).op s)
  simp only at hr
  let g : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L, f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x) := ε.app (U₀ x) (a x)
  have hga : IsTrivializingGenerator ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L) (f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x) g :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.pullbackGenerator f L
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_tensorInvertible (X := X.toRingedSpace) L) (U₀ x)
      ⟨a x, ha x⟩).2
  have hnat := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (α.mapPresheaf.naturality (homOfLE (hU₀ x)).op) s
  simp only [Scheme.Modules.mapPresheaf_app, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at hnat
  have h1 : j.app (f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x) (f.app (U₀ x) r • g) = 0 := by
    have := Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul ε r (a x)
    rw [hr] at this
    rwa [homEquiv_app_apply, hs, map_zero, this] at hnat
  have hne : ((f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x : Y.Opens) : Set Y).Nonempty := by
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := f.denseRange.exists_mem_open (U₀ x).isOpen ⟨x, hxU₀ x⟩
    exact ⟨y, hy⟩
  obtain ⟨y, hyV, hyW⟩ : ((f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x ⊓ W : Y.Opens) : Set Y).Nonempty :=
    nonempty_preirreducible_inter (f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x).isOpen W.isOpen hne hWne
  have hle : f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x ⊓ W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x := inf_le_left
  have h2 := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (j.mapPresheaf.naturality (homOfLE hle).op)
    ((f.app (U₀ x) r) • g)
  simp only [Scheme.Modules.mapPresheaf_app, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at h2
  rw [h1, map_zero] at h2
  have h3 := (bijective_jacobianSection_app_of_le sX f W n
    (inf_le_right : f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ x ⊓ W ≤ W)).1 (h2.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  rw [Scheme.Modules.map_smul] at h3
  have h4 : Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op (f.app (U₀ x) r) = 0 := by
    apply (hga _ hle).1
    simpa only [zero_smul] using h3
  have h5 : f.app (U₀ x) r = 0 := by
    apply germ_injective_of_isIntegral Y y hyV
    rw [map_zero, ← Y.presheaf.germ_res (homOfLE hle) y ⟨hyV, hyW⟩, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
      h4, map_zero]
  have := IsSchemeTheoreticallyDominant.of_isDominant f
  have hr0 : r = 0 := (f.app_injective (U₀ x)) (h5.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  rw [← hr, hr0, zero_smul]

/-- The canonical map `Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}` is injective on the sections over every open. -/
private theorem injective_app_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsVariety k sX]
    [MMP.Mori.IsVariety k sY] (n : ℕ) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n sX] [Smooth sY]
    (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsProper f] (hfb : MMP.Mori.IsBirationalMorphism f) (hfs : f ≫ sX = sY)
    (U : X.Opens) :
    Function.Injective
      (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _
        (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsMap f sX sY (𝟙 _)
          (by rw [hfs, Category.comp_id]) n)).val.app (op U)) := by
  subst hfs
  have : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sX n) :=
    Stacks.Discriminant.isInvertible_relativeDifferentialForms sX n
  exact injective_app_homEquiv_jacobianSection sX n f hfb U

/-- Restriction maps of a module with trivializing generators near every point (a line bundle) on
an integral scheme are injective towards non-empty opens. -/
private theorem injective_presheaf_map_of_isTrivializingGenerator [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    (hL : ∀ x : X, ∃ U₀ : X.Opens, x ∈ U₀ ∧ ∃ a : Γ(L, U₀), IsTrivializingGenerator L U₀ a)
    {U V : X.Opens} (hVU : V ≤ U) (hV : (V : Set X).Nonempty) :
    Function.Injective (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op) := by
  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
  intro s hs
  choose W hxW a ha using fun x : U => hL x.1
  refine TopCat.Sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq' ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).obj L)
    (fun x : U => U ⊓ W x) U (fun x => homOfLE inf_le_left)
    (fun y hy => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, ⟨hy, hxW _⟩⟩) _ _ fun x => ?_
  change L.presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s = L.presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op 0
  rw [map_zero]
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (ha x (U ⊓ W x) inf_le_right).2 (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s)
  simp only at hr
  obtain ⟨y, hyV, hyW⟩ : (V ⊓ W x : Set X).Nonempty :=
    nonempty_preirreducible_inter V.isOpen (W x).isOpen hV ⟨x, hxW x⟩
  have hle : V ⊓ W x ≤ U ⊓ W x := inf_le_inf_right _ hVU
  have e1 : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : V ⊓ W x ≤ W x)).op (a x) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_right).op (a x)) := by
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]; rfl
  have e2 : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left : V ⊓ W x ≤ V)).op
        (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op s) := by
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
      ← Functor.map_comp]; rfl
  have h0 : X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op r = 0 := by
    apply (ha x (V ⊓ W x) inf_le_right).1
    simp only
    rw [zero_smul, e1, ← Scheme.Modules.map_smul, hr, e2, hs, map_zero]
  have hr0 : r = 0 := by
    apply germ_injective_of_isIntegral X y (show y ∈ U ⊓ W x from ⟨hVU hyV, hyW⟩)
    rw [map_zero, ← X.presheaf.germ_res (homOfLE hle) y ⟨hyV, hyW⟩, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
      h0, map_zero]
  rw [← hr, hr0, zero_smul]

/-- A normal locally Noetherian scheme satisfies Serre's condition `S₂`. -/
private lemma satisfiesS2_of_isNormal (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] :
    MMP.Flips.SatisfiesS2 X :=
  MMP.Flips.satisfiesS2_iff_forall_min_le_depth.mpr
    ((isNormal_iff_hasPropertySk_two_and_isRegularInCodimension_one X).mp inferInstance).1

/-- If `g` restricts to an isomorphism over `W`, then `𝒪_X(W) ⟶ 𝒪_Y(g⁻¹ W)` is an
isomorphism. -/
private lemma isIso_app_of_isIso_morphismRestrict {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) {W : X.Opens}
    (hW : IsIso (g ∣_ W)) : IsIso (g.app W) := by
  have h := morphismRestrict_appTop g W
  have : IsIso (g.app (W.ι ''ᵁ ⊤) ≫
      Y.presheaf.map (eqToHom (image_morphismRestrict_preimage g W ⊤)).op) := by
    rw [← h]; exact Scheme.Hom.instIsIsoCommRingCatApp _ ⊤
  have := IsIso.of_isIso_comp_right (g.app (W.ι ''ᵁ ⊤))
    (Y.presheaf.map (eqToHom (image_morphismRestrict_preimage g W ⊤)).op)
  rwa [Scheme.Opens.ι_image_top] at this

/-- A scheme smooth of relative dimension `n` over a field, and irreducible, has dimension `n`. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension (n : ℕ)
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsVariety k f] [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n f] :
    topologicalKrullDim X = n := by
  obtain ⟨x⟩ : Nonempty X := inferInstance
  let e : f.fiber (f x) ≃ₜ X := (f.fiberHomeo (f x)).trans
    ((Homeomorph.setCongr (Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun y => Subsingleton.elim (f y) (f x))).trans
      (Homeomorph.Set.univ X))
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt_of_irreducible k X f x,
    ← f.fiberι_asFiber x, ← fiberDimensionAt_eq_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension f n x]
  exact (topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_of_homeomorph e (f.asFiber x)).symm

/-- The canonical map `Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}` is locally surjective: near every point of
an open `U ⊆ X`, a section of `f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}` over `U` is the image of a section of
`Ω^n_{X/k}`. -/
private theorem exists_app_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap_eq
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsVariety k sX]
    [MMP.Mori.IsVariety k sY] (n : ℕ) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n sX] [Smooth sY]
    (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsProper f] (hfb : MMP.Mori.IsBirationalMorphism f) (hfs : f ≫ sX = sY)
    (U : X.Opens) (σ : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj
      (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sY n), U)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ (U₀ : X.Opens) (hU₀ : U₀ ≤ U), x ∈ U₀ ∧
      ∃ s₀ : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sX n, U₀),
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _
          (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsMap f sX sY (𝟙 _)
            (by rw [hfs, Category.comp_id]) n)).app U₀ s₀ =
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj
            (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sY n)).presheaf.map (homOfLE hU₀).op σ := by
  subst hfs
  let L := Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms sX n
  let M := Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms (f ≫ sX) n
  have : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L :=
    Stacks.Discriminant.isInvertible_relativeDifferentialForms sX n
  have hnX := topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension n sX
  have hnY : topologicalKrullDim Y = n :=
    (MMP.Intersection.topologicalKrullDim_eq_of_isBirationalMorphism sX (f ≫ sX) hfb).symm.trans
      hnX
  have := smoothOfRelativeDimension_of_isVariety (f ≫ sX) n hnY
  have : Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule Y M :=
    Stacks.Discriminant.isInvertible_relativeDifferentialForms (f ≫ sX) n
  have : IsDominant f := hfb.isDominant
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sX
  have : Smooth sX := SmoothOfRelativeDimension.smooth (n := n) (f := sX)
  have : IsNormal (Spec (.of k)) :=
    isNormal_spec_of_isNormalRing (IsNormalRing.of_isIntegrallyClosed k)
  have : IsNormal X := isNormal_of_smooth sX
  obtain ⟨U₀, hU₀, a, hxU₀, ha⟩ := exists_isTrivializingGenerator L hx
  let V := U₀ ⊓ MMP.Mori.biregularLocus f
  have hVbi : IsIso (f ∣_ V) := MMP.Mori.isBiregular_iff_le_biregularLocus.mpr inf_le_right
  have : IsOpenImmersion ((f ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ f) := by rw [← morphismRestrict_ι]; infer_instance
  have hfapp : IsIso (f.app V) := isIso_app_of_isIso_morphismRestrict f hVbi
  let ε := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app L
  let j := jacobianSection sX f n
  let g : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L, f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀) := ε.app U₀ a
  have hga : IsTrivializingGenerator ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj L) (f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀) g :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.pullbackGenerator f L
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_tensorInvertible (X := X.toRingedSpace) L) U₀
      ⟨a, ha⟩).2
  have hVU₀ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U₀ := f.preimage_mono inf_le_left
  have hcodim : ∀ z ∈ U₀, z ∉ V → 2 ≤ ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk z) := by
    intro z hz hzV
    by_contra h2
    refine hzV ⟨hz, MMP.Mori.mem_biregularLocus_of_ringKrullDim_stalk_le_one
      (sX := sX) ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩ f (inferInstance : MMP.Mori.IsVariety k (f ≫ sX))
      hfb ?_⟩
    rw [not_le] at h2
    generalize ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk z) = d at h2 ⊢
    induction d using WithBot.recBotCoe with
    | bot => exact bot_le
    | coe d =>
      have h2' : d < 2 := WithBot.coe_lt_coe.mp h2
      have h1 : d ≤ 1 := Order.le_of_lt_add_one (by simpa [one_add_one_eq_two] using h2')
      exact WithBot.coe_le_coe.mpr h1
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := (bijective_jacobianSection_app_of_le sX f (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) n le_rfl).2
    (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hVU₀.trans (f.preimage_mono hU₀))).op σ)
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ⟩ := (hga (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) hVU₀).2 t
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (f.app V)).2 ψ
  obtain ⟨φ', hφ'⟩ := (MMP.Flips.bijective_presheaf_map_of_satisfiesS2 (satisfiesS2_of_isNormal X)
    (inf_le_left : V ≤ U₀) hcodim).2 φ
  refine ⟨U₀, hU₀, hxU₀, φ' • a, ?_⟩
  have hne : ((f ⁻¹ᵁ V : Y.Opens) : Set Y).Nonempty := by
    have hη : genericPoint X ∈ U₀ :=
      ((genericPoint_spec X).mem_open_set_iff U₀.isOpen).mpr ⟨x, trivial, hxU₀⟩
    have hηV : genericPoint X ∈ V := by
      by_contra hη'
      have h2 := hcodim _ hη hη'
      have h0 : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) = 0 :=
        ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_field X.functionField
      rw [h0] at h2
      exact absurd h2 (by decide)
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := f.denseRange.exists_mem_open V.isOpen ⟨_, hηV⟩
    exact ⟨y, hy⟩
  apply injective_presheaf_map_of_isTrivializingGenerator M
    (fun y => by
      obtain ⟨U', -, e', hy, he'⟩ :=
        exists_isTrivializingGenerator M (show y ∈ (⊤ : Y.Opens) from trivial)
      exact ⟨U', hy, e', he'⟩) hVU₀ hne
  rw [homEquiv_app_apply, Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul]
  have hnat := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (j.mapPresheaf.naturality (homOfLE hVU₀).op)
    ((f.app U₀ φ') • g)
  simp only [Scheme.Modules.mapPresheaf_app, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at hnat
  refine hnat.symm.trans ?_
  refine (congrArg _ ?_).trans (ht.trans ?_)
  · rw [Scheme.Modules.map_smul, ← hψ, ← hφ, ← hφ']
    congr 1
    exact (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (f.naturality (homOfLE (inf_le_left : V ≤ U₀)).op) φ').symm
  · exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (M.presheaf.map_comp _ _) σ

end CanonicalSheaf

/-- **Push-forward of the canonical sheaf along a proper birational morphism.** Let
`f : Y ⟶ X` be a proper birational morphism of smooth varieties over `k`, with `X` smooth of
relative dimension `n` over `k`. Then the canonical map `Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ f_* Ω^n_{Y/k}`, adjoint to
the pull-back of forms `f^* Ω^n_{X/k} ⟶ Ω^n_{Y/k}`, is an isomorphism; that is, `f_* ω_Y ≅ ω_X`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_birational_pushforward_canonical"]
public theorem isIso_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap_of_isBirationalMorphism
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k sX] [IsVariety k sY]
    (n : ℕ) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n sX] [Smooth sY]
    (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsProper f] (hfb : IsBirationalMorphism f) (hfs : f ≫ sX = sY) :
    IsIso ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _
      (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsMap f sX sY (𝟙 _)
        (by rw [hfs, Category.comp_id]) n)) := by
  set α := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).homEquiv _ _
    (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialFormsMap f sX sY (𝟙 _) (by rw [hfs, Category.comp_id]) n)
  have := (Sheaf.isLocallyBijective_iff_isIso ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).map α)).mp
    ⟨Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _ fun V =>
        injective_app_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap sX sY n f hfb hfs V.unop,
      (TopCat.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff _).2 fun V σ x hx => by
        obtain ⟨U₀, hU₀, hxU₀, s₀, hs₀⟩ :=
          exists_app_homEquiv_relativeDifferentialFormsMap_eq sX sY n f hfb hfs V σ hx
        exact ⟨U₀, hU₀, ⟨s₀, hs₀⟩, hxU₀⟩⟩
  exact MMP.Flips.isIso_of_bijective_app _ fun U => ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (((SheafOfModules.toSheaf X.ringCatSheaf).map α).hom.app (op U))

section SmoothIff

/-- Over a perfect field, a scheme locally of finite type is smooth if and only if all of its
local rings are regular. -/
private theorem smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing (k : Type u) [Field k] [PerfectField k]
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] :
    Smooth g ↔ ∀ y, IsRegularLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation g :=
    LocallyOfFinitePresentation.iff_locallyOfFiniteType.mpr inferInstance
  have hset := smoothAt_locus_eq_regular_locus k g
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.smoothLocus_eq_top_iff, eq_top_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h y => (Set.ext_iff.mp hset y).mp ?_, fun h y _ => ?_⟩
  · exact InfinitesimalLifting.formallySmooth_stalkMap_smoothAt g y
      (Scheme.Hom.mem_smoothLocus.mp (h trivial))
  · exact Scheme.Hom.mem_smoothLocus.mpr
      (InfinitesimalLifting.SmoothAt.formallySmooth_stalkMap g y
        ((Set.ext_iff.mp hset y).mpr (h y)))

/-- Regularity of a local ring is invariant under ring isomorphism. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_congr {S S' : Type*} [CommRing S] [CommRing S'] (e : S ≃+* S') :
    IsRegularLocalRing S ↔ IsRegularLocalRing S' :=
  ⟨fun _ => .of_ringEquiv e, fun _ => .of_ringEquiv e.symm⟩

/-- The local ring of a scheme at a point of an affine open `V` is regular if and only if the
localization of `Γ(V)` at the corresponding prime is. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff {Y : Scheme.{u}} {V : Y.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    {y : Y} (hy : y ∈ V) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩).asIdeal) := by
  letI := Y.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨y, hy⟩
  have := hV.isLocalization_stalk ⟨y, hy⟩
  exact isRegularLocalRing_congr (IsLocalization.algEquiv
    (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl (Y.presheaf.stalk y)
    (Localization.AtPrime (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩).asIdeal)).toRingEquiv

/-- For `g : Y ⟶ X` and an affine open `U ∋ x` of `X` with affine preimage, the local rings of
`Y` at the points over `x` are the localizations of `Γ(Y, g⁻¹U)` at the primes over the prime
of `x`. -/
private theorem forall_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (hV : IsAffineOpen (g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U.1) :
    (∀ y, g y = x → IsRegularLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) ↔
      ∀ Q : PrimeSpectrum Γ(Y, g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1), Q.asIdeal.comap (g.app U.1).hom =
        (U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal →
          IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal) := by
  have key : ∀ y (hy : y ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1),
      (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩).asIdeal.comap (g.app U.1).hom =
        (U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨g y, hy⟩).asIdeal := fun y hy => by
    have := congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal
      (IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE (f := g) U.1 U.2 _ hV le_rfl hy)
    rwa [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app] at this
  constructor
  · intro h Q hQ
    obtain ⟨y, hmem, hQ'⟩ : ∃ y, ∃ hy : y ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, hV.primeIdealOf ⟨y, hy⟩ = Q := by
      let Q' : Spec Γ(Y, g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := Q
      have hmem : hV.fromSpec Q' ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 := by
        have : hV.fromSpec Q' ∈ Set.range hV.fromSpec := ⟨Q', rfl⟩
        rwa [hV.range_fromSpec] at this
      exact ⟨_, hmem, hV.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.injective
        (hV.fromSpec_primeIdealOf ⟨_, hmem⟩)⟩
    subst hQ'
    have hgx : g y = x := by
      have h1 : U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨g y, hmem⟩ = U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩ :=
        PrimeSpectrum.ext (by rw [← key _ hmem, hQ])
      have h2 := congrArg U.2.fromSpec h1
      rwa [U.2.fromSpec_primeIdealOf, U.2.fromSpec_primeIdealOf] at h2
    exact (isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff hV hmem).1 (h _ hgx)
  · rintro h y rfl
    exact (isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff hV hx).2 (h _ (key y hx))

section Algebra

variable {R B D : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [CommRing D] {m : ℕ} {f : R}

/-- In `B = R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` the class of `T` is an `m`-th root of `f`. -/
private theorem pow_eq_algebraMap_of_ker_eq_span (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) :
    φ Polynomial.X ^ m = algebraMap R B f := by
  have h : Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f ∈ RingHom.ker φ := hker ▸ Ideal.subset_span rfl
  rwa [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, map_pow, ← Polynomial.algebraMap_eq (R := R), φ.commutes,
    sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- Every prime of `R` has a prime of `R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` over it, for `m > 0`: the extension is
integral and injective. -/
private theorem exists_comap_eq_of_ker_eq_span (hm : 0 < m) (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) (P : Ideal R)
    [P.IsPrime] : ∃ Q : PrimeSpectrum B, Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap R B) = P := by
  have : Nontrivial R := by
    by_contra h
    rw [not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton] at h
    exact ‹P.IsPrime›.ne_top (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  have hmon : (Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f).Monic := Polynomial.monic_X_pow_sub_C f hm.ne'
  have hφX : ∀ q, φ q = Polynomial.aeval (φ Polynomial.X) q := fun q => by
    rw [Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, Polynomial.aeval_X_left_apply]
  have hint : IsIntegral R (φ Polynomial.X) := ⟨_, hmon, by
    change Polynomial.aeval (φ Polynomial.X) _ = 0
    rw [← hφX, ← RingHom.mem_ker, hker]; exact Ideal.subset_span rfl⟩
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral R B := ⟨fun b => by
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := hφ b
    have : φ q ∈ Algebra.adjoin R {φ Polynomial.X} := by
      rw [hφX q]
      exact Polynomial.aeval_mem_adjoin_singleton R (φ Polynomial.X)
    exact adjoin_le_integralClosure hint this⟩
  have hinj : (⊥ : Ideal B).comap (algebraMap R B) ≤ P := by
    intro r hr
    have hr' : Polynomial.C r ∈ RingHom.ker φ := by
      change φ (Polynomial.C r) = 0
      rwa [← Polynomial.algebraMap_eq (R := R), φ.commutes]
    rw [hker, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hr'
    by_contra h0
    have hr0 : r ≠ 0 := fun h => h0 (h ▸ P.zero_mem)
    refine hmon.not_dvd_of_natDegree_lt (Polynomial.C_ne_zero.2 hr0) ?_ hr'
    rwa [Polynomial.natDegree_C, Polynomial.natDegree_X_pow_sub_C]
  obtain ⟨Q, -, hQ, hQP⟩ := Ideal.exists_ideal_over_prime_of_isIntegral P ⊥ hinj
  exact ⟨⟨Q, hQ⟩, hQP⟩

/-- Regularity of `Localization.AtPrime I` only depends on the ideal `I`. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_congr {S : Type*} [CommRing S] {I J : Ideal S}
    [I.IsPrime] [J.IsPrime] (h : I = J) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime I) ↔ IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime J) := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- For `m` invertible in `R`, the localization of `R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` away from `T` is standard
étale over `R`: it is the standard étale algebra of the pair `(Tᵐ - f, T)`. -/
private theorem etale_localization_away_of_ker_eq_span (hm : 0 < m) (hmu : IsUnit (m : R))
    (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) :
    Algebra.Etale R (Localization.Away (φ Polynomial.X)) := by
  let P : StandardEtalePair R :=
    { f := Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f, monic_f := Polynomial.monic_X_pow_sub_C f hm.ne'
      g := Polynomial.X
      cond := ⟨Polynomial.C (↑hmu.unit⁻¹ : R) * Polynomial.X, 0, m, by
        rw [Polynomial.derivative_sub, Polynomial.derivative_C, sub_zero,
          Polynomial.derivative_X_pow, mul_zero, add_zero]
        calc Polynomial.C (m : R) * Polynomial.X ^ (m - 1) *
              (Polynomial.C (↑hmu.unit⁻¹ : R) * Polynomial.X)
            = Polynomial.C ((m : R) * ↑hmu.unit⁻¹) * (Polynomial.X ^ (m - 1) * Polynomial.X) := by
              rw [Polynomial.C_mul]; ring
          _ = Polynomial.X ^ m := by
              rw [IsUnit.mul_val_inv, Polynomial.C_1, one_mul, pow_sub_one_mul hm.ne']⟩ }
  let e₀ : AdjoinRoot (Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f) ≃ₐ[R] B :=
    (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R hker.symm).trans (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hφ)
  have he₀ : e₀ (AdjoinRoot.mk P.f P.g) = φ Polynomial.X := rfl
  have H : Submonoid.map e₀.toRingEquiv.toMonoidHom (.powers (AdjoinRoot.mk P.f P.g)) =
      .powers (φ Polynomial.X) := by
    rw [Submonoid.map_powers]
    exact congrArg Submonoid.powers he₀
  let e₂ : Localization.Away (AdjoinRoot.mk P.f P.g) ≃ₐ[R] Localization.Away (φ Polynomial.X) :=
    { __ := IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv _ _ _ H,
      commutes' r := by
        simp [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R (AdjoinRoot P.f) (Localization.Away _),
          IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R B (Localization.Away (φ Polynomial.X))]
        rw [← AdjoinRoot.algebraMap_eq, e₀.commutes] }
  exact Algebra.Etale.of_equiv (P.equivAwayAdjoinRoot.trans e₂)

/-- **Away from the zero locus.** Over a prime `P ∌ f` the extension `R → R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)`
becomes standard étale after inverting `T` (whose `m`-th power is `f`), so regularity goes up
and down. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff_of_notMem (hm : 0 < m)
    (hmu : IsUnit (m : R)) (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) (P : Ideal R)
    [P.IsPrime] (hfP : f ∉ P) (Q : PrimeSpectrum B)
    (hQ : Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap R B) = P) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime P) := by
  have := etale_localization_away_of_ker_eq_span hm hmu φ hφ hker
  set t := φ Polynomial.X
  have htQ : t ∉ Q.asIdeal := fun h => hfP (by
    rw [← hQ, Ideal.mem_comap, ← pow_eq_algebraMap_of_ker_eq_span φ hker]
    exact Q.asIdeal.pow_mem_of_mem h m hm)
  have hdisj : Disjoint (Submonoid.powers t : Set B) Q.asIdeal :=
    (Ideal.disjoint_powers_iff_notMem t Q.isPrime.isRadical).2 htQ
  let Q' := Q.asIdeal.map (algebraMap B (Localization.Away t))
  have : Q'.IsPrime := IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint (Submonoid.powers t) _ _
    Q.isPrime hdisj
  have hQ' : Q'.comap (algebraMap B (Localization.Away t)) = Q.asIdeal :=
    IsLocalization.comap_map_of_isPrime_disjoint (Submonoid.powers t) _ Q.isPrime hdisj
  have : Q'.LiesOver P := ⟨by
    rw [Ideal.under, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq R B (Localization.Away t), ← Ideal.comap_comap,
      hQ', hQ]⟩
  rw [isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff_of_etale P Q', isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_congr hQ'.symm]
  exact isRegularLocalRing_congr
    (IsLocalization.localizationLocalizationAtPrimeIsoLocalization (Submonoid.powers t)
      Q').toRingEquiv

/-- Regularity of the localization at a prime is transported along a ring isomorphism. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_comap_ringEquiv {S S' : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [CommRing S'] (e : S ≃+* S') (Q : Ideal S') [Q.IsPrime] :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime (Q.comap e)) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q) := by
  have H : Submonoid.map e.toMonoidHom (Q.comap e).primeCompl = Q.primeCompl := by
    ext y
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩; exact hx
    · intro hy; exact ⟨e.symm y, by simpa [Ideal.primeCompl] using hy, by simp⟩
  exact isRegularLocalRing_congr (IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv
    (Localization.AtPrime (Q.comap e)) (Localization.AtPrime Q) e H)

/-- For `I ≤ 𝔭`, the localization of `A ⧸ I` at `𝔭 / I` is `A_𝔭 ⧸ I A_𝔭`. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_map_mk_iff {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (I 𝔭 : Ideal A)
    [𝔭.IsPrime] [(𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).IsPrime] (h : I ≤ 𝔭) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime (𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing
        (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭))) := by
  have hM : Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (A ⧸ I) 𝔭.primeCompl =
      (𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).primeCompl := by
    ext y
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
    have hmem : ∀ z, Ideal.Quotient.mk I z ∈ 𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) ↔ z ∈ 𝔭 := fun z =>
      Ideal.mem_quotient_iff_mem h
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨z, hz, hzx⟩
      change _ ∉ _
      rw [← hzx]
      exact fun h' => hz ((hmem z).1 h')
    · intro hx
      exact ⟨x, (hmem x).not.1 hx, rfl⟩
  haveI : IsLocalization (𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).primeCompl
      (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭))) := hM ▸ inferInstance
  exact isRegularLocalRing_congr (IsLocalization.algEquiv (𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).primeCompl
    (Localization.AtPrime (𝔭.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭 ⧸ I.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭)))).toRingEquiv

/-- For a surjection `ψ : A → C` and a prime `Q` of `C` over `𝔮`, the local ring `C_Q` is
`A_𝔮 ⧸ (ker ψ) A_𝔮`. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_iff_of_surjective {A C : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing C] (ψ : A →+* C) (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) (Q : Ideal C) [Q.IsPrime]
    (𝔮 : Ideal A) [𝔮.IsPrime] (h𝔮 : Q.comap ψ = 𝔮) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime 𝔮 ⧸
        (RingHom.ker ψ).map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime 𝔮))) := by
  subst h𝔮
  let e := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hψ
  have hle : RingHom.ker ψ ≤ Q.comap ψ := Ideal.comap_mono bot_le
  have hc : (Q.comap ψ).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ψ)) = Q.comap e := by
    have : (Q.comap e).comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ψ)) = Q.comap ψ := by
      ext x; exact Iff.rfl
    rw [← this, Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective]
  haveI : ((Q.comap ψ).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ψ))).IsPrime := hc ▸ inferInstance
  rw [← isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_comap_ringEquiv e Q, ← isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_congr hc]
  exact isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_map_mk_iff _ _ hle

/-- In a domain, a nonzero element lies in no minimal prime. -/
private theorem notMem_of_mem_minimalPrimes {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [IsDomain S] {x : S}
    (hx : x ≠ 0) : ∀ p ∈ minimalPrimes S, x ∉ p := fun p hp hxp =>
  hx ((Ideal.mem_bot).1 (hp.2 ⟨(inferInstance : (⊥ : Ideal S).IsPrime), bot_le⟩ bot_le hxp))

/-- Over a prime `P ∋ f`, the prime of `R[T]` under a prime of `R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` over `P` is
`(P, T)`. -/
private theorem comap_eq_comap_constantCoeff_of_mem (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) (P : Ideal R)
    (hfP : f ∈ P) (Q : PrimeSpectrum B) (hQ : Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap R B) = P) :
    Q.asIdeal.comap (φ : Polynomial R →+* B) = P.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff := by
  have hXQ : φ Polynomial.X ∈ Q.asIdeal := Q.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem m <| by
    rwa [pow_eq_algebraMap_of_ker_eq_span φ hker, ← Ideal.mem_comap, hQ]
  ext x
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : Polynomial.X ∣ x - Polynomial.C (x.coeff 0) :=
    Polynomial.X_dvd_iff.2 (by simp)
  have h1 : φ x = algebraMap R B (x.coeff 0) + φ Polynomial.X * φ y := by
    rw [← φ.commutes, Polynomial.algebraMap_eq, ← map_mul, ← map_add, ← hy]
    ring_nf
  change φ x ∈ Q.asIdeal ↔ Polynomial.constantCoeff x ∈ P
  rw [h1, Ideal.add_mem_iff_left _ (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hXQ), ← Ideal.mem_comap, hQ,
    Polynomial.constantCoeff_apply]

/-- `T` does not lie in the square of the maximal ideal of `R[T]_(P, T)`. -/
private theorem algebraMap_X_notMem_maximalIdeal_sq [IsDomain R] (P : Ideal R)
    (𝔭 : Ideal (Polynomial R)) [𝔭.IsPrime] (h𝔭 : P.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff = 𝔭) :
    algebraMap (Polynomial R) (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) Polynomial.X ∉
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) ^ 2 := by
  have h𝔭' : ∀ x, x ∈ 𝔭 ↔ x.coeff 0 ∈ P := fun x => by
    rw [← h𝔭, Ideal.mem_comap, Polynomial.constantCoeff_apply]
  have sq1 : ∀ a ∈ 𝔭 ^ 2, a.coeff 1 ∈ P := by
    intro a ha
    rw [pow_two] at ha
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on ha (fun x hx y hy => ?_) (fun x y hx hy => ?_)
    · rw [h𝔭'] at hx hy
      rw [Polynomial.coeff_mul, Finset.Nat.antidiagonal_succ]
      simp only [Finset.Nat.antidiagonal_zero, Finset.map_singleton, Finset.sum_cons,
        Finset.sum_singleton]
      exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hx) (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hy)
    · rw [Polynomial.coeff_add]
      exact Ideal.add_mem _ hx hy
  intro h
  rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal, ← Ideal.map_pow,
    IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff 𝔭.primeCompl] at h
  obtain ⟨⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨s, hs⟩⟩, h⟩ := h
  rw [← map_mul] at h
  have h' := congrArg (fun p => p.coeff 1)
    (IsLocalization.injective (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) 𝔭.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors h)
  simp only [Polynomial.coeff_X_mul_zero] at h'
  rw [show (1 : ℕ) = 0 + 1 from rfl, Polynomial.coeff_X_mul] at h'
  exact hs ((h𝔭' s).2 (h' ▸ sq1 a ha))

/-- For `m ≥ 2`, `Tᵐ - f` lies in the square of the maximal ideal of `R[T]_(P, T)` if and only if
`f` lies in the square of the maximal ideal of `R_P`. -/
private theorem algebraMap_X_pow_sub_C_mem_maximalIdeal_sq_iff [IsDomain R] (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (P : Ideal R) [P.IsPrime] (𝔭 : Ideal (Polynomial R)) [𝔭.IsPrime]
    (h𝔭 : P.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff = 𝔭) :
    algebraMap (Polynomial R) (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) (Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f) ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) ^ 2 ↔
      algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime P) f ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime P) ^ 2 := by
  have h𝔭' : ∀ x, x ∈ 𝔭 ↔ x.coeff 0 ∈ P := fun x => by
    rw [← h𝔭, Ideal.mem_comap, Polynomial.constantCoeff_apply]
  have hcc : Function.Surjective (Polynomial.constantCoeff : Polynomial R →+* R) := fun r =>
    ⟨Polynomial.C r, by simp⟩
  have hm' : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) ^ 2 =
      (𝔭 ^ 2).map (algebraMap (Polynomial R) (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭)) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal]
  have sqTm : algebraMap (Polynomial R) (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) (Polynomial.X ^ m) ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) ^ 2 := by
    rw [hm']
    apply Ideal.mem_map_of_mem
    obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k, m = k + 2 := ⟨m - 2, by omega⟩
    rw [pow_add]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.pow_mem_pow ((h𝔭' _).2 (by simp)) 2)
  rw [map_sub, Submodule.sub_mem_iff_right _ sqTm, hm', ← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal,
    ← Ideal.map_pow, IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff 𝔭.primeCompl,
    IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff P.primeCompl]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨s, hs⟩⟩, h⟩
    rw [← map_mul] at h
    have h' := congrArg (fun p => p.coeff 0)
      (IsLocalization.injective (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) 𝔭.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors h)
    simp only [Polynomial.mul_coeff_zero, Polynomial.coeff_C_zero] at h'
    refine ⟨⟨⟨a.coeff 0, ?_⟩, ⟨s.coeff 0, fun hs' => hs ((h𝔭' s).2 hs')⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    · have hle : (𝔭 ^ 2).map Polynomial.constantCoeff ≤ P ^ 2 := by
        rw [Ideal.map_pow, ← h𝔭, Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ hcc]
      have := hle (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
      rwa [Polynomial.constantCoeff_apply] at this
    · simp only
      rw [← map_mul, h']
  · rintro ⟨⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨s, hs⟩⟩, h⟩
    rw [← map_mul] at h
    have h' := IsLocalization.injective (Localization.AtPrime P) P.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors h
    have hle : (P ^ 2).map Polynomial.C ≤ 𝔭 ^ 2 := by
      rw [Ideal.map_pow]
      refine Ideal.pow_right_mono (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun x hx => ?_) 2
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, h𝔭']
      simpa using hx
    refine ⟨⟨⟨Polynomial.C a, hle (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)⟩,
      ⟨Polynomial.C s, fun hs' => hs (by simpa [h𝔭'] using hs')⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    simp only
    rw [← map_mul, ← map_mul Polynomial.C, h']

/-- **On the zero locus.** Over a prime `P ∋ f`, with `R' = R[T]_(P, T)`, the local ring of
`R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` is `R'/(Tᵐ - f)`, `R'/(T) = R_P` and the local ring of `R/(f)` is `R_P/(f)`;
three applications of `MMP.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_iff` give the
equivalence. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff_of_mem [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (hm : 2 ≤ m) (hf : f ≠ 0) (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) (ψ : R →+* D)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) (hψker : RingHom.ker ψ = Ideal.span {f}) (P : Ideal R)
    [P.IsPrime] (hfP : f ∈ P) (Q : PrimeSpectrum B)
    (hQ : Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap R B) = P) (Q' : PrimeSpectrum D)
    (hQ' : Q'.asIdeal.comap ψ = P) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime P) ∧
        IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q'.asIdeal) := by
  classical
  let 𝔭 : Ideal (Polynomial R) := P.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
  have h𝔭 : ∀ x, x ∈ 𝔭 ↔ x.coeff 0 ∈ P := fun x => by
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Polynomial.constantCoeff_apply]
  have hcc : Function.Surjective (Polynomial.constantCoeff : Polynomial R →+* R) := fun r =>
    ⟨Polynomial.C r, by simp⟩
  have hX𝔭 : (Polynomial.X : Polynomial R) ∈ 𝔭 := by
    rw [h𝔭]
    simp
  have hB := isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_iff_of_surjective (φ : Polynomial R →+* B) hφ Q.asIdeal
    𝔭 (comap_eq_comap_constantCoeff_of_mem φ hker P hfP Q hQ)
  rw [show RingHom.ker (φ : Polynomial R →+* B) = RingHom.ker φ from rfl, hker, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton] at hB
  have hRP := isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_iff_of_surjective
    (Polynomial.constantCoeff : Polynomial R →+* R) hcc P 𝔭 rfl
  rw [Polynomial.ker_constantCoeff, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton] at hRP
  have hD := isRegularLocalRing_atPrime_iff_of_surjective ψ hψ Q'.asIdeal P hQ'
  rw [hψker, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton] at hD
  have inj' := IsLocalization.injective (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) 𝔭.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have injP := IsLocalization.injective (Localization.AtPrime P) P.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have mem' : ∀ x ∈ 𝔭, algebraMap (Polynomial R) (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) x ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime 𝔭) := fun x hx => by
    rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hx
  -- the three hypersurface equivalences
  have hT := MMP.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_iff (mem' _ hX𝔭)
    (notMem_of_mem_minimalPrimes ((map_ne_zero_iff _ inj').2 Polynomial.X_ne_zero))
  have hG := MMP.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_iff
    (mem' (Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f) (by
      rw [h𝔭, Polynomial.coeff_sub, Polynomial.coeff_X_pow, Polynomial.coeff_C_zero,
        if_neg (by omega), zero_sub]
      exact P.neg_mem hfP))
    (notMem_of_mem_minimalPrimes ((map_ne_zero_iff _ inj').2
      (Polynomial.monic_X_pow_sub_C f (by omega)).ne_zero))
  have hF := MMP.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_iff
    (show algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime P) f ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ by
      rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal]; exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hfP)
    (notMem_of_mem_minimalPrimes ((map_ne_zero_iff _ injP).2 hf))
  have sqT := algebraMap_X_notMem_maximalIdeal_sq P 𝔭 rfl
  rw [hB, hD, hF, hRP, hG, hT, algebraMap_X_pow_sub_C_mem_maximalIdeal_sq_iff hm P 𝔭 rfl]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨h1, h2⟩ => ⟨⟨h1, sqT⟩, ⟨h1, sqT⟩, h2⟩, fun ⟨_, ⟨h1, _⟩, h2⟩ => ⟨h1, h2⟩⟩

end Algebra

/-- **Algebraic core.** Let `R` be a Noetherian domain in which `m ≥ 2` is invertible, `0 ≠ f ∈ R`,
`B = R[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` and `D = R/(f)`. Over a prime `P` of `R`, the localizations of `B` at the primes
over `P` are regular if and only if `R_P` is regular and so are the localizations of `D` at the
primes over `P`. -/
private theorem forall_isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff {R B D : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [CommRing B] [Algebra R B] [CommRing D] {m : ℕ}
    (hm : 2 ≤ m) (hmu : IsUnit (m : R)) {f : R} (hf : f ≠ 0) (φ : Polynomial R →ₐ[R] B)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C f}) (ψ : R →+* D)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) (hψker : RingHom.ker ψ = Ideal.span {f}) (P : Ideal R)
    [P.IsPrime] :
    (∀ Q : PrimeSpectrum B, Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap R B) = P →
        IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal)) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime P) ∧
        ∀ Q : PrimeSpectrum D, Q.asIdeal.comap ψ = P →
          IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime Q.asIdeal) := by
  have hD : ∀ Q : PrimeSpectrum D, Q.asIdeal.comap ψ = P → f ∈ P := fun Q hQ => by
    have hf0 : ψ f = 0 := by
      rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, hψker]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f
    rw [← hQ, Ideal.mem_comap, hf0]; exact Q.asIdeal.zero_mem
  have hD' : f ∈ P → ∃ Q : PrimeSpectrum D, Q.asIdeal.comap ψ = P := fun hfP => by
    have hle : RingHom.ker ψ ≤ P := by
      rwa [hψker, Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ⟨⟨P.map ψ, Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective hψ hle⟩,
      (Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective' ψ hψ P).trans (sup_eq_left.2 hle)⟩
  obtain ⟨Q₀, hQ₀⟩ := exists_comap_eq_of_ker_eq_span (by omega) φ hφ hker P
  by_cases hfP : f ∈ P
  · obtain ⟨Q₁, hQ₁⟩ := hD' hfP
    have H := fun Q hQ Q' hQ' => isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff_of_mem hm hf φ hφ hker
      ψ hψ hψker P hfP Q hQ Q' hQ'
    exact ⟨fun h => ⟨((H Q₀ hQ₀ Q₁ hQ₁).1 (h Q₀ hQ₀)).1,
        fun Q' hQ' => ((H Q₀ hQ₀ Q' hQ').1 (h Q₀ hQ₀)).2⟩,
      fun ⟨hR, hDr⟩ Q hQ => (H Q hQ Q₁ hQ₁).2 ⟨hR, hDr Q₁ hQ₁⟩⟩
  · have H := fun Q hQ => isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff_of_notMem (by omega) hmu φ hφ
      hker P hfP Q hQ
    exact ⟨fun h => ⟨(H Q₀ hQ₀).1 (h Q₀ hQ₀), fun Q' hQ' => absurd (hD Q' hQ') hfP⟩,
      fun ⟨hR, _⟩ Q hQ => (H Q hQ).2 hR⟩

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]

/-- The cyclic cover is locally of finite type: on a chart its ring is a quotient of a
polynomial ring in one variable. -/
private theorem locallyOfFiniteType_cyclicCoverToBase (m : ℕ)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) :
    LocallyOfFiniteType (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ) := by
  have := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  rw [HasRingHomProperty.iff_exists_appLE (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType)
    (RingHom.finiteType_stableUnderComposition.stableUnderCompositionWithLocalizationAway
      RingHom.finiteType_holdsForLocalizationAway).1]
  intro z
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, -, φ, hφ, hφC, -, -⟩ := exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ z)
  refine ⟨U, ⟨_, U.2.preimage _⟩, hxU, le_rfl, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app, ← hφC]
  exact RingHom.FiniteType.comp (RingHom.FiniteType.of_surjective φ hφ)
    (RingHom.finiteType_algebraMap.mpr inferInstance)

/-- On an integral scheme, the zero scheme of a nonzero `σ` is nowhere dense: its ideal is
nonzero on every nonempty affine open. -/
private theorem zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_ne_bot [IsIntegral X] {m : ℕ}
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (U : X.affineOpens) [Nonempty U.1] :
    (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).ideal U ≠ ⊥ := by
  intro hU
  apply hσ
  have hsub : (U.1 : Set X) ⊆ (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support := fun x hx =>
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := U) hx).2 (by rw [hU]; simp)
  have hd : Dense (U.1 : Set X) := U.1.isOpen.dense (Set.nonempty_coe_sort.1 ‹_›)
  have hsupp : (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support = ⊤ := by
    ext x
    simp only [TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_top, Set.mem_univ, iff_true]
    exact (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support.isClosed.closure_subset_iff.2 hsub (hd x)
  have hI := Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_eq_top_iff.1 hsupp
  have hV : ∀ (V : X.affineOpens) s, σ.val.app (Opposite.op V.1) s = 0 := fun V s => by
    have h := zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_eq_span_range N m σ V
    rw [hI] at h
    have hs : σ.val.app (Opposite.op V.1) s ∈
        (Ideal.span (Set.range (σ.val.app (Opposite.op V.1))) : Ideal Γ(X, V.1)) :=
      Ideal.subset_span ⟨s, rfl⟩
    rw [← h] at hs
    exact (Ideal.mem_bot (R := Γ(X, V.1))).1 hs
  apply SheafOfModules.hom_ext
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro W
  ext s
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.section_ext X.sheaf W.unop _ _ fun x hx => ?_
  obtain ⟨V, hV', hxV, hVW⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.1 X.isBasis_affineOpens hx
  have h1 := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply σ.val (homOfLE hVW).op s
  have h2 := hV ⟨V, hV'⟩ (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map
    (homOfLE hVW).op s)
  have key : X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op (σ.val.app W s) = 0 := h1.symm.trans h2
  show X.presheaf.germ _ x hx (σ.val.app W s) = X.presheaf.germ _ x hx 0
  rw [map_zero]
  have h3 := congrArg (X.presheaf.germ V x hxV) key
  rw [map_zero] at h3
  exact (X.presheaf.germ_res_apply (homOfLE hVW) x hxV _).symm.trans h3

/-- **Pointwise criterion.** The local rings of the cyclic cover over a point `x` are regular
if and only if `𝒪_{X,x}` is regular and so are the local rings of the zero scheme over `x`;
there is at least one point over `x`. -/
private theorem forall_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_iff (k : Type u) [Field k] [CharZero k]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] [LocallyOfFiniteType f] {m : ℕ} (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (x : X) :
    (∀ z, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ z = x →
        IsRegularLocalRing ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z)) ↔
      IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∧
        ∀ y, (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι y = x →
          IsRegularLocalRing ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subscheme.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, a, φ, hφ, hφC, hker, hI⟩ := exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ x
  have := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  rw [forall_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff _ U (U.2.preimage _) hxU,
    forall_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff _ U (U.2.preimage _) hxU,
    isRegularLocalRing_stalk_iff U.2 hxU]
  have : Nonempty U.1 := ⟨⟨x, hxU⟩⟩
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
  letI := ((cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).app U.1).hom.toAlgebra
  have ha : a ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    exact zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_ne_bot N σ hσ U (hI.trans (by simp))
  have hmu : IsUnit (m : Γ(X, U.1)) := by
    let ρ : k →+* Γ(X, U.1) := (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom.comp
      ((f.app ⊤).hom.comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv.hom)
    have h : IsUnit (m : k) := (Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 (by omega)).isUnit
    exact map_natCast ρ m ▸ h.map ρ
  exact forall_isRegularLocalRing_localization_iff hm hmu ha
    { φ with commutes' := fun r => RingHom.congr_fun hφC r } hφ hker
    ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.app U.1).hom
    ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι_app_surjective U)
    (((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).ker_subschemeι_app U).trans hI) _

end SmoothIff

/-- **Smoothness of a ramified cyclic cover.** For an algebraically closed field `k` of
characteristic zero, a normal variety `X` over `k`, a line bundle `N = L⁻¹` on `X`, `m ≥ 2` and
a nonzero `σ = ⟨·, s⟩ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X`, the ramified cyclic cover `Z = cyclicCover N m σ` is
smooth over `k` if and only if `X` is smooth over `k` and the zero scheme `D = zeroScheme N m σ`
of `s` is smooth over `k`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_cyclic_cover_smooth_iff"]
public theorem smooth_ramifiedCyclicCover_comp_iff (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (hX : IsNormalVariety k f)
    (N : X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N] {m : ℕ}
    (hm : 2 ≤ m) (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) :
    Smooth (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) ↔
      Smooth f ∧ Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f) := by
  obtain ⟨hint, -, hft, -⟩ := (isVariety_iff k f).1 hX.1
  have := locallyOfFiniteType_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  have H := forall_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_iff N k f hm σ hσ
  rw [smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing k, smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing k,
    smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing k]
  refine ⟨fun h => ⟨fun x => ((H x).1 fun z _ => h z).1,
    fun y => ((H _).1 fun z _ => h z).2 y rfl⟩, fun ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ z => ?_⟩
  exact (H _).2 ⟨h₁ _, fun y _ => h₂ y⟩ z rfl

section SmoothVariety

/-- A map that is open and closed onto a preconnected space, with a point whose fibre is a
non-empty subsingleton, has a connected source. -/
private theorem connectedSpace_of_isOpenMap_of_isClosedMap {Z X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Z]
    [TopologicalSpace X] [PreconnectedSpace X] {p : Z → X} (hpo : IsOpenMap p)
    (hpc : IsClosedMap p) (x : X) (hx : (p ⁻¹' {x}).Nonempty) (hx' : (p ⁻¹' {x}).Subsingleton) :
    ConnectedSpace Z := by
  obtain ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ := hx
  refine connectedSpace_iff_clopen.2 ⟨⟨z₀⟩, fun s hs => ?_⟩
  have himage : ∀ w : Set Z, IsClopen w → w.Nonempty → x ∈ p '' w := fun w hw hne => by
    rcases isClopen_iff.1 (⟨hpc _ hw.1, hpo _ hw.2⟩ : IsClopen (p '' w)) with h | h
    · exact absurd (Set.image_eq_empty.1 h) hne.ne_empty
    · exact h ▸ Set.mem_univ x
  by_contra h
  have h₁ : s.Nonempty := Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.2 fun h' => h (Or.inl h')
  have h₂ : sᶜ.Nonempty := Set.nonempty_compl.2 fun h' => h (Or.inr h')
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hax⟩ := himage s hs h₁
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hbx⟩ := himage sᶜ hs.compl h₂
  exact hb (hx' (show p b = x from hbx) (show p a = x from hax) ▸ ha)

/-- Over an affine open `U` with affine preimage, `p` maps the point `Spec Γ(p⁻¹U) ⟶ p⁻¹U` of a
prime `q` to the point of its contraction `q ∩ Γ(U)`. -/
private theorem fromSpec_comap {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ X) {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen (p ⁻¹ᵁ U)) (q : Spec Γ(Z, p ⁻¹ᵁ U)) :
    hU.fromSpec (PrimeSpectrum.comap (p.app U).hom q) = p (hV.fromSpec q) := by
  rw [← Spec.map_apply, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply,
    Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE, IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec p hU hV]

private theorem primeIdealOf_map {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ X) {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen (p ⁻¹ᵁ U)) (z : p ⁻¹ᵁ U) :
    hU.primeIdealOf ⟨p z.1, z.2⟩ = PrimeSpectrum.comap (p.app U).hom (hV.primeIdealOf z) := by
  apply hU.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.injective
  refine (hU.fromSpec_primeIdealOf _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (fromSpec_comap p hU hV _).symm
  rw [hV.fromSpec_primeIdealOf]

/-- If over an affine open `U ∋ x` with affine preimage at most one prime of `Γ(p⁻¹U)` contracts
to the prime of `x`, the fibre of `p` over `x` has at most one point. -/
private theorem subsingleton_preimage_of_isAffineOpen {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ X)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen (p ⁻¹ᵁ U)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (h : ∀ q₁ q₂ : PrimeSpectrum Γ(Z, p ⁻¹ᵁ U),
      PrimeSpectrum.comap (p.app U).hom q₁ = hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩ →
      PrimeSpectrum.comap (p.app U).hom q₂ = hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩ → q₁ = q₂) :
    (p.base ⁻¹' {x}).Subsingleton := by
  rintro z₁ (rfl : p z₁ = x) z₂ (hz : p z₂ = p z₁)
  have h₂ : z₂ ∈ p ⁻¹ᵁ U := show p z₂ ∈ U by rwa [hz]
  have key := h (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨z₁, hx⟩) (hV.primeIdealOf ⟨z₂, h₂⟩)
    (primeIdealOf_map p hU hV ⟨z₁, hx⟩).symm
    (by rw [← primeIdealOf_map p hU hV ⟨z₂, h₂⟩]; congr 2)
  have := congrArg hV.fromSpec key
  rwa [hV.fromSpec_primeIdealOf, hV.fromSpec_primeIdealOf] at this

open Polynomial in
/-- In a quotient `A` of `R[T]` in which `Tᵐ = f`, a prime `q` whose contraction contains `f` is
generated by its contraction and the image of `T`. -/
private theorem eq_map_comap_sup_span_of_mem {R A : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A]
    (ψ : R[X] →+* A) (hs : Function.Surjective ψ) {m : ℕ} {f : R}
    (hf : ψ (Polynomial.X ^ m) = ψ (C f))
    (q : Ideal A) [q.IsPrime] (hfq : f ∈ q.comap (ψ.comp C)) :
    q = Ideal.map (ψ.comp C) (q.comap (ψ.comp C)) ⊔ Ideal.span {ψ Polynomial.X} := by
  have hX : ψ Polynomial.X ∈ q := by
    refine (‹q.IsPrime›).mem_of_pow_mem m ?_
    rwa [← map_pow, hf]
  refine le_antisymm (fun a ha => ?_) (sup_le Ideal.map_comap_le
    ((Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).2 hX))
  obtain ⟨P, rfl⟩ := hs a
  have hP : P = C (P.coeff 0) + Polynomial.X * P.divX := by
    rw [add_comm, X_mul_divX_add]
  rw [hP, map_add, map_mul] at ha ⊢
  have h0 : ψ (C (P.coeff 0)) ∈ q := by
    have := q.sub_mem ha (q.mul_mem_right (ψ P.divX) hX)
    simpa using this
  exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mem_sup_left (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (show P.coeff 0 ∈ _ from h0)))
    (Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)))

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N] {m : ℕ}
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

/-- Over a point `x` of the zero scheme `D`, the fibre of the cyclic cover is
`Spec κ(x)[T]/(Tᵐ)`, a single point: a prime of `A[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` over `𝔭 ∋ f` contains `T`. -/
private theorem subsingleton_fibre_of_mem_zeroScheme (x : X)
    (hx : x ∈ Set.range (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.base) :
    ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).base ⁻¹' {x}).Subsingleton := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, f, φ, hs, hC, hk, hI⟩ := exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ x
  haveI := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U.1 := U.2
  have hV : IsAffineOpen (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := hU.preimage _
  set 𝔭 := hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have hf𝔭 : f ∈ 𝔭.asIdeal := by
    have hxD : x ∈ ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support : Set X) ∩ U.1 :=
      ⟨(Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι _) ▸ hx, hxU⟩
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_inter, ← hU.fromSpec_image_zeroLocus] at hxD
    obtain ⟨𝔮, h𝔮, h𝔮x⟩ := hxD
    have : 𝔮 = 𝔭 := hU.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.injective
      (h𝔮x.trans (hU.fromSpec_primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).symm)
    subst this
    rw [hI] at h𝔮
    exact h𝔮 (Ideal.subset_span rfl)
  have hfX : φ (Polynomial.X ^ m) = φ (Polynomial.C f) := by
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← map_sub, ← RingHom.mem_ker, hk]
    exact Ideal.subset_span rfl
  refine subsingleton_preimage_of_isAffineOpen _ hU hV hxU fun q₁ q₂ h₁ h₂ => ?_
  have key : ∀ q : PrimeSpectrum Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ U.1),
      PrimeSpectrum.comap ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).app U.1).hom q = 𝔭 →
      q.asIdeal = Ideal.map (φ.comp Polynomial.C) 𝔭.asIdeal ⊔ Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X} := by
    intro q hq
    have hq' : q.asIdeal.comap (φ.comp Polynomial.C) = 𝔭.asIdeal := by
      rw [hC, ← hq]; rfl
    rw [← hq']
    exact eq_map_comap_sup_span_of_mem φ hs hfX q.asIdeal (hq' ▸ hf𝔭)
  exact PrimeSpectrum.ext ((key q₁ h₁).trans (key q₂ h₂).symm)

/-- A ramified cyclic cover of a connected scheme with `0 < m` and non-empty zero scheme is
connected: the cover is finite and flat, hence open and closed, and its fibre over a point of the
zero scheme is a single point. -/
private theorem connectedSpace_cyclicCover [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [PreconnectedSpace X]
    (hm : 0 < m) (hD : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) : ConnectedSpace (cyclicCover N m σ) := by
  have := isFinite_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm
  have := flat_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm
  have : UniversallyOpen (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) := UniversallyOpen.of_flat _
  obtain ⟨d⟩ := hD
  have := surjective_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm
  exact connectedSpace_of_isOpenMap_of_isClosedMap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).isOpenMap
    (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).isClosedMap _ ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).surjective _)
    (subsingleton_fibre_of_mem_zeroScheme N σ _ ⟨d, rfl⟩)

end SmoothVariety

/-- **A ramified cyclic cover of a smooth variety, branched along a smooth non-empty divisor, is a
smooth variety**: for a smooth variety `f : X ⟶ Spec k` over an algebraically closed field
of characteristic zero, an invertible sheaf `N = L⁻¹`, `m ≥ 2`
and a non-zero `σ = ⟨·, s⟩ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X` whose zero scheme is smooth over `k` and non-empty,
the cover `p : Z ⟶ X` is finite, flat and surjective and `p ≫ f : Z ⟶ Spec k` is a smooth
variety. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_cyclic_cover_smooth_variety"]
public theorem ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsVariety k f] [Smooth f] (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hD : Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) :
    IsVariety k (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) ∧ Smooth (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) ∧
      IsFinite (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) ∧ Flat (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) ∧
      Surjective (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) := by
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by omega
  have hfin := isFinite_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm0
  have hnorm : IsNormal X :=
    (MMP.Threefold.Resolution.isLocallyNoetherian_and_isNormal_of_isSmoothScheme
      ((isSmoothScheme_iff f).2 ‹_›)).2
  have hsm : Smooth (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) :=
    (smooth_ramifiedCyclicCover_comp_iff k f ⟨‹_›, hnorm⟩ N hm σ hσ).2 ⟨‹_›, hD⟩
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  have : PreconnectedSpace X :=
    ⟨(IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ X).2.isPreconnected⟩
  have := connectedSpace_cyclicCover N σ hm0 hDne
  have : IsIntegral (cyclicCover N m σ) :=
    Stacks.Chow.isIntegral_of_connectedSpace_of_smooth (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f)
  exact ⟨(isVariety_iff k _).2 ⟨this, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩, hsm, hfin,
    flat_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm0,
    surjective_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ hm0⟩

section BranchPullback

open Polynomial

section Algebra

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] {m : ℕ} {f : A} {φ : A[X] →+* B}

private theorem map_C_eq_pow (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C f}) :
    φ (C f) = φ Polynomial.X ^ m := by
  have h : Polynomial.X ^ m - C f ∈ RingHom.ker φ := hker ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, map_pow, sub_eq_zero] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- A constant whose image lies in `(t)` lies in `(f)`. -/
private theorem mem_span_of_map_C_mem (hm : 0 < m) (hsurj : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C f}) {a : A}
    (ha : φ (C a) ∈ Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X}) : a ∈ Ideal.span {f} := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 ha
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hsurj b
  have hmem : C a - g * Polynomial.X ∈ RingHom.ker φ := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, map_mul, hb, sub_self]
  rw [hker, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hmem
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hmem
  have := congrArg (eval 0) hh
  simp only [eval_sub, eval_C, eval_mul, eval_X, mul_zero, sub_zero, eval_pow,
    zero_pow hm.ne', zero_sub] at this
  rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
  exact ⟨-(h.eval 0), by rw [this]; ring⟩

/-- The ideal `(t)` is radical when `(f)` is. -/
private theorem isRadical_span_X (hm : 0 < m) (hsurj : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C f}) (hf : (Ideal.span {f}).IsRadical) :
    (Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X}).IsRadical := by
  have hC : ∀ g : A[X], φ g - φ (C (g.coeff 0)) ∈ Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X} := fun g => by
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := (X_dvd_sub_C (p := g))
    rw [← map_sub, hq, map_mul]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  rintro b ⟨n, hn⟩
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hsurj b
  have hq : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X}) (φ g) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X}) (φ (C (g.coeff 0))) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq.2 (hC g)
  have hn' : φ (C (g.coeff 0 ^ n)) ∈ Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X} := by
    rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem] at hn ⊢
    rw [map_pow, map_pow, map_pow, ← hq, ← map_pow, hn]
  have ha : g.coeff 0 ∈ Ideal.span {f} := hf ⟨n, mem_span_of_map_C_mem hm hsurj hker hn'⟩
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, hq, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 ha
  rw [← hc, map_mul, map_mul, map_C_eq_pow hker]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.pow_mem_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _) _ hm)

/-- The radical of `(tᵐ)` is `(t)` when `(f)` is radical. -/
private theorem radical_span_pow (hm : 0 < m) (hsurj : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C f}) (hf : (Ideal.span {f}).IsRadical) :
    (Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X ^ m}).radical = Ideal.span {φ Polynomial.X} := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · refine (isRadical_span_X hm hsurj hker hf).radical_le_iff.2 ?_
    rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact Ideal.pow_mem_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _) _ hm
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ⟨m, Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _⟩

/-- The class `t` of `T` is a non-zero-divisor when `f` is. -/
private theorem isRegular_map_X (hm : 0 < m) (hsurj : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C f}) (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) :
    IsRegular (φ Polynomial.X) := by
  have key : ∀ b : B, φ Polynomial.X * b = 0 → b = 0 := by
    intro b hb
    obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hsurj b
    have hmem : Polynomial.X * g ∈ RingHom.ker φ := by rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_mul, hb]
    rw [hker, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hmem
    obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hmem
    have h0 : h.coeff 0 = 0 := by
      have := congrArg (eval 0) hh
      simp only [eval_mul, eval_X, zero_mul, eval_sub, eval_pow, zero_pow hm.ne', eval_C,
        zero_sub, neg_mul] at this
      rw [coeff_zero_eq_eval_zero]
      exact (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.1 hf).1 _ (neg_eq_zero.1 this.symm)
    obtain ⟨h', rfl⟩ := X_dvd_iff.2 h0
    have hg : g = (Polynomial.X ^ m - C f) * h' := by
      ext n
      have := congrArg (coeff · (n + 1)) hh
      simp only [mul_left_comm _ Polynomial.X, coeff_X_mul] at this
      exact this
    rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, hker, hg]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  exact (Commute.isRegular_iff (Commute.all _)).2 (isLeftRegular_iff_right_eq_zero_of_mul.2 key)

end Algebra

section Schemes

/-- On an affine open, the ideal of a reduced closed subscheme is radical. -/
private theorem isRadical_ideal_of_isReduced {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    [IsReduced I.subscheme] (U : X.affineOpens) : (I.ideal U).IsRadical := by
  rw [Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced]
  exact isReduced_of_injective (I.subschemeObjIso U).inv.hom
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (I.subschemeObjIso U).inv).1

/-- Let `p : Z ⟶ X` be affine, `I` an ideal sheaf on `X` and `R` the radical of `p⁻¹I`. If `X` is
covered by affine opens `U` with `Γ(Z, p⁻¹U) = Γ(X, U)[T]/(Tᵐ - f)`, `I = (f)` on `U` and `R = (T)`
on `p⁻¹U`, then `p` restricts to an isomorphism `V(R) ≅ V(I)`. -/
private theorem isIso_subschemeMap_of_charts {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ X) [IsAffineHom p]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (hle : I ≤ (I.comap p).radical.map p) {m : ℕ} (hm0 : 0 < m)
    (U : X → X.affineOpens) (hxU : ∀ x, x ∈ (U x : X.Opens)) (g : ∀ x, Γ(X, (U x).1))
    (φ : ∀ x, Γ(X, (U x).1)[X] →+* Γ(Z, p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1))
    (hsurj : ∀ x, Function.Surjective (φ x))
    (hC : ∀ x, (φ x).comp C = (p.app (U x).1).hom)
    (hker : ∀ x, RingHom.ker (φ x) = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - C (g x)})
    (hIU : ∀ x, I.ideal (U x) = Ideal.span {g x})
    (hRV : ∀ x, (I.comap p).radical.ideal ⟨p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage p⟩ =
      Ideal.span {φ x Polynomial.X}) :
    IsIso (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap (I.comap p).radical I p hle) := by
  set R := (I.comap p).radical
  let V : X → Z.affineOpens := fun x => ⟨p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage p⟩
  set G := Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap R I p hle
  have hsq : G ≫ I.subschemeι = R.subschemeι ≫ p :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι R I p hle
  haveI : IsAffineHom (G ≫ I.subschemeι) := by rw [hsq]; infer_instance
  haveI : IsAffineHom G := IsAffineHom.of_comp G I.subschemeι
  refine IsZariskiLocalAtTarget.of_iSup_eq_top (P := MorphismProperty.isomorphisms Scheme)
    (fun x => I.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1) (eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ =>
      TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨_, hxU (I.subschemeι z)⟩) fun x => ?_
  change IsIso _
  rw [isIso_morphismRestrict_iff_isIso_app _ ((U x).2.preimage _),
    ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
  have happ := Scheme.Hom.congr_app hsq (U x).1
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_app, Scheme.Hom.comp_app] at happ
  obtain ⟨hh, hsqa⟩ : ∃ hh, ∀ a, G.app (I.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1) (I.subschemeι.app (U x).1 a) =
      R.subscheme.presheaf.map (eqToHom hh).op
        (R.subschemeι.app (p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1) (p.app (U x).1 a)) :=
    ⟨_, fun a => ConcreteCategory.congr_hom happ a⟩
  have hαI : ∀ a, I.subschemeι.app (U x).1 a =
      (I.subschemeObjIso (U x)).inv (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a) := fun a => by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeι_app]; rfl
  have hαR : ∀ b, R.subschemeι.app (p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1) b =
      (R.subschemeObjIso (V x)).inv (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b) := fun b => by
    erw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeι_app R (V x)]; rfl
  have hpC : ∀ a, p.app (U x).1 a = φ x (C a) := fun a =>
    (RingHom.congr_fun (hC x) a).symm
  have he : ∀ {W W' : R.subscheme.Opens} (h : W = W'),
      Function.Bijective (R.subscheme.presheaf.map (eqToHom h).op) := fun h => by
    subst h
    rw [eqToHom_refl, op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
    exact Function.bijective_id
  refine ⟨(injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun y hy => ?_, fun y => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ : ∃ a, I.subschemeι.app (U x).1 a = y := by
      obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ :=
        (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (I.subschemeObjIso (U x)).inv).2 y
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective q
      exact ⟨a, hαI a⟩
    rw [hsqa, map_eq_zero_iff _ (he hh).1, hαR,
      map_eq_zero_iff _ (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _).1,
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, hRV x, hpC] at hy
    have ha : a ∈ I.ideal (U x) := by
      rw [hIU x]; exact mem_span_of_map_C_mem hm0 (hsurj x) (hker x) hy
    rw [hαI, (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem).2 ha, map_zero]
  · obtain ⟨y', rfl⟩ := (he hh).2 y
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ :=
      (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (R.subschemeObjIso (V x)).inv).2 y'
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective q
    obtain ⟨P, rfl⟩ := hsurj x b
    refine ⟨I.subschemeι.app (U x).1 (P.coeff 0), ?_⟩
    have hq : Ideal.Quotient.mk (R.ideal (V x)) (φ x (C (P.coeff 0))) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (R.ideal (V x)) (φ x P) := by
      obtain ⟨q', hq'⟩ := X_dvd_sub_C (p := P)
      rw [Ideal.Quotient.eq, hRV x, ← map_sub, ← neg_sub, hq', map_neg, map_mul]
      exact (Ideal.neg_mem_iff _).2 (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _))
    rw [hsqa, hαR, hpC, hq]

end Schemes

end BranchPullback

/-- **The branch divisor of a ramified cyclic cover.** Let `X` be a smooth variety over `k`, `N`
an invertible sheaf on `X` (the inverse `L⁻¹` of a line bundle `L`), `m ≥ 2` and
`σ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X` a nonzero pairing `⟨·, s⟩` with `s ∈ H⁰(X, Lᵐ)`, whose zero scheme `D` is
smooth over `k` and non-empty. Let `p : Z ⟶ X` be the ramified cyclic cover and `R` the reduced
subscheme of `p⁻¹(D)`. Then `R` is smooth over `k`, it is an effective Cartier divisor on `Z`,
and the ideal of `p⁻¹(D)` is the `m`-th power of the ideal of `R`, that is `p⁻¹(D) = m R`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_cyclic_cover_branch_pullback"]
public theorem ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f]
    (hX : IsSmoothScheme f) (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0)
    (hD : IsSmoothScheme ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) :
    IsSmoothScheme
        (((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical.subschemeι ≫
          ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) ∧
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
        ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical ∧
      (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) =
        ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical ^ m := by
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by omega
  haveI : IsAffineHom (MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) :=
    MMP.Mori.isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  haveI hDred : IsReduced (MMP.Mori.zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subscheme :=
    MMP.Resolution.Aux.isReduced_subscheme_of_isSmoothScheme f _ hD
  set p := MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ
  set I := MMP.Mori.zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ
  set R := (I.comap p).radical with hR
  choose U hxU g φ hsurj hC hker hIU using MMP.Mori.exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ
  let V : X → (MMP.Mori.cyclicCover N m σ).affineOpens := fun x =>
    ⟨p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage p⟩
  have hcomap : ∀ x, (I.comap p).ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {φ x Polynomial.X ^ m} := fun x => by
    rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I p (U x) (V x) le_rfl,
      Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app, hIU x, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, ← hC x,
      RingHom.comp_apply, map_C_eq_pow (hker x)]
  have hrad : ∀ x, (Ideal.span {g x}).IsRadical := fun x =>
    hIU x ▸ isRadical_ideal_of_isReduced I (U x)
  have hRV : ∀ x, R.ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {φ x Polynomial.X} := fun x => by
    rw [hR, Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal, hcomap,
      radical_span_pow hm0 (hsurj x) (hker x) (hrad x)]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hle : I ≤ R.map p :=
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le.2 (Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_radical _)
    haveI := isIso_subschemeMap_of_charts p I hle hm0 U hxU g φ hsurj hC hker hIU hRV
    have hsm : Smooth (I.subschemeι ≫ f) := hD.smooth
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι _ _ _ hle,
      Category.assoc]
    exact MMP.Mori.isSmoothScheme_of_smooth inferInstance
  · refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen R fun z =>
      ⟨_, (V (p z)).2, hxU (p z), φ (p z) Polynomial.X, ?_, hRV (p z)⟩
    refine isRegular_map_X hm0 (hsurj _) (hker _) ?_
    haveI : Nonempty ((U (p z)) : X.Opens) := ⟨⟨p z, hxU (p z)⟩⟩
    have hg : g (p z) ≠ 0 := fun h0 => zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_ne_bot N σ hσ _
      (by rw [hIU, h0, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot])
    exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hg
  · refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top V
      (eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨p z, hxU (p z)⟩) fun x => ?_
    rw [hcomap, show (R ^ m).ideal (V x) = R.ideal (V x) ^ m from
      Submodule.toSubMulAction_inj.mp rfl, hRV, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]

section BranchLineBundle

open Polynomial

section Charts

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]

private theorem algebraSheafIncl_cast (U : X.Opens) {n n' : ℤ} (h : n = n')
    (z : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece n).val.obj (op U)) :
    (cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl n' U
      ((eqToHom (congrArg (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece h)).val.app (op U) z) =
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl n U z := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- Every positive power of a degree-one section of `Sym(N)` comes from `Symⁿ(N)`. -/
private theorem exists_algebraSheafIncl_eq_pow (W : X.Opens)
    (g : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece 1).val.obj (op W)) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n →
      ∃ u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op W),
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl n W u =
        (cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl 1 W g ^ n := by
  intro n hn
  induction n with
  | zero => exact absurd hn (lt_irrefl 0)
  | succ n ih =>
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hn'
    · refine ⟨(eqToHom (congrArg (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece
        (by norm_num : (1 : ℤ) = ((0 + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)))).val.app (op W) g, ?_⟩
      rw [pow_one]
      exact algebraSheafIncl_cast N W (by norm_num) g
    · obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := ih hn'
      refine ⟨(eqToHom (congrArg (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece
        (Nat.cast_succ n).symm)).val.app (op W)
          (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.mul (n : ℤ) 1).app (op W) u g), ?_⟩
      rw [algebraSheafIncl_cast N W (Nat.cast_succ n).symm,
        ← Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.algebraSheafIncl_mul, hu, pow_succ]

/-- A trivialization of `N` over `W` gives a section `t` with `a ↦ a • t|_{W'}` bijective on
every open `W' ⊆ W`. -/
private theorem exists_bijective_smul (W : X.Opens)
    (e : N.over W ≅ SheafOfModules.unit (X.ringCatSheaf.over W)) :
    ∃ t : N.val.obj (op W), ∀ (W' : X.Opens) (hW : W' ≤ W),
      Function.Bijective fun a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W') =>
        a • (N.val.map (homOfLE hW).op t : N.val.obj (op W')) := by
  let t : N.val.obj (op W) :=
    e.inv.val.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 W))) (1 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))
  have key : ∀ (W' : X.Opens) (hW : W' ≤ W) (a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W')),
      a • (N.val.map (homOfLE hW).op t : N.val.obj (op W')) =
        e.inv.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hW))) a := by
    intro W' hW a
    have h1 := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply e.inv.val (X := op (Over.mk (𝟙 W)))
      (Y := op (Over.mk (homOfLE hW)))
      (Over.homMk (homOfLE hW) : Over.mk (homOfLE hW) ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 W)).op
      (1 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))
    erw [PresheafOfModules.unit_map_one] at h1
    have h2 := (e.inv.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hW)))).hom.map_smul a
      (1 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W'))
    exact (congrArg (fun z : N.val.obj (op W') => a • z) h1).symm.trans
      (h2.symm.trans (congrArg _ (mul_one a)))
  refine ⟨t, fun W' hW => ?_⟩
  have : (fun a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W') =>
      a • (N.val.map (homOfLE hW).op t : N.val.obj (op W'))) =
        e.inv.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hW))) :=
    funext (key W' hW)
  rw [this]
  exact ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _ ⋙
    (CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hW))) ⋙ forget _).mapIso
      ((SheafOfModules.forget _).mapIso e.symm)).toEquiv.bijective

/-- On the chart over an affine open `W` of the base on which `t` trivializes the line bundle, the
image of the zero section of the total space is cut out by the fibre coordinate of `t`. -/
private theorem ideal_ker_zeroSection (D : Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.{u}) (W : D.X.affineOpens)
    (t : D.L.val.obj (op W.1))
    (ht : Function.Bijective fun a : D.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W.1) => a • t) :
    D.zeroSection.ker.ideal ⟨D.totalSpaceToBase ⁻¹ᵁ W.1, W.2.preimage _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(D.chartRingEquiv W
        (D.algebraSheafIncl 1 W.1 (D.symmetricAlgebraGen.val.app (op W.1) t)))} := by
  let b : Module.Basis (Fin 1) Γ(D.X, W.1) Γ(D.L, W.1) :=
    (Module.Basis.singleton (Fin 1) Γ(D.X, W.1)).map
      (LinearEquiv.ofBijective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton Γ(D.X, W.1) Γ(D.L, W.1) t) ht)
  have hb : b 0 = t := by
    simp [b]
    exact one_smul _ _
  rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_apply]
  refine (D.ker_zeroSectionChartMap_eq W).symm.trans ?_
  rw [D.ker_zeroSectionChartMap W b]
  congr 2
  rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, ← D.chartEquiv_genToPushforward W b 0]
  congr 1
  rw [hb]
  exact (D.chartRingEquiv_algebraSheafIncl W t).symm

end Charts

/-- **The zero section meets the cyclic cover in the reduced branch divisor.** Let
`ι : Z ⟶ Spec_X Sym(N)` be the closed immersion of the cyclic cover into the total space of `N`.
The preimage under `ι` of the zero section `o(X)` is `p⁻¹(D)_red`. On a chart
`Z|_U = Spec 𝒪_U[T]/(Tᵐ - f)` the ideal of `o(X)` restricts to `(T)`, which contains `(f) = (Tᵐ)`
and has quotient `𝒪_U/(f)`, the coordinate ring of `D ∩ U`; that ring is reduced because `D` is
reduced, so `(T)` is the radical of `(f)`. -/
private lemma comap_ker_zeroSection_eq_radical {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    [IsReduced (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subscheme] :
    (cyclicCoverSituation N).zeroSection.ker.comap (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι =
      ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical := by
  set p := ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ
  set I := zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ
  set D := cyclicCoverSituation N
  set ι := (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι
  haveI : IsAffineHom p := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  choose U hxU he using fun x : X => D.exists_trivializing_affineOpen x
  let V : X → (cyclicCover N m σ).affineOpens := fun x => ⟨p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage p⟩
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top V
    (eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨p z, hxU (p z)⟩) fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_bijective_smul N (U x).1 (he x).some
  have htW : N.val.map (homOfLE (le_refl (U x).1)).op t = t := by
    simp <;> rfl
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_algebraSheafIncl_eq_pow N (U x).1
    (D.symmetricAlgebraGen.val.app (Opposite.op (U x).1) t) m hm
  have hloc := cyclicCover_local_equation N m hm σ (U x).1 t ht u hu _ rfl
  obtain ⟨hsurj, hker⟩ := hloc.1 (U x).1 le_rfl
  have hI := hloc.2 (U x) le_rfl
  rw [htW] at hsurj hker
  set ψ := Polynomial.eval₂RingHom ((cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).app (U x).1).hom
    (cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ 1 (U x).1 (D.symmetricAlgebraGen.val.app (Opposite.op (U x).1) t))
  have hC : ψ.comp Polynomial.C = (p.app (U x).1).hom := by
    ext a; simp [ψ, p]
  have hrad := hI ▸ isRadical_ideal_of_isReduced I (U x)
  have ht' : Function.Bijective fun a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (Opposite.op (U x).1) => a • t :=
    htW ▸ ht (U x).1 le_rfl
  have hL : (D.zeroSection.ker.comap ι).ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {ψ Polynomial.X} := by
    rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE _ ι
      ⟨symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage _⟩ (V x) le_rfl,
      ideal_ker_zeroSection D (U x) t ht', Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
    simp only [ψ, Polynomial.coe_eval₂RingHom, Polynomial.eval₂_X]
    erw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
    rfl
  have hR : (I.comap p).radical.ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {ψ Polynomial.X} := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal,
      Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I p (U x) (V x) le_rfl,
      Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app, hI, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, ← hC,
      RingHom.comp_apply, map_C_eq_pow hker, radical_span_pow hm hsurj hker hrad]
  rw [hL, hR]

end BranchLineBundle

/-- **The branch divisor of a ramified cyclic cover cuts out the pulled-back line bundle.** Let
`X` be a smooth variety over `k`, `N` an invertible sheaf on `X` (the inverse `L⁻¹` of a line
bundle `L`), `m ≥ 2` and `σ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X` a nonzero pairing `⟨·, s⟩` with `s ∈ H⁰(X, Lᵐ)`,
whose zero scheme `D` is smooth over `k` and non-empty. Let `p : Z ⟶ X` be the ramified cyclic
cover and `R` the reduced subscheme of `p⁻¹(D)`. Then `𝒪_Z(R) ≅ p^*L`, where `L = N^∨`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_cyclic_cover_branch_line_bundle"]
public theorem nonempty_invertibleSheaf_radical_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_iso_pullback
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f]
    (hX : IsSmoothScheme f) (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0)
    (hD : IsSmoothScheme ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) :
    Nonempty ((Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf'
        ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical :
          (cyclicCover N m σ).Modules) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).obj
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.dualSheaf X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
          N)) := by
  let D := cyclicCoverSituation N
  let ι := (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι
  let M' := (Scheme.Modules.pullback ι).obj D.basePullbackInverse
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (cyclicCover N m σ).sheaf.obj
      (cyclicCover N m σ).ringCatSheaf.property M' :=
    Stacks.AmpleRestrict.isInvertible_pullback _ _
  let τ' : Γ(M', ⊤) := pullbackGlobalSections ι D.basePullbackInverse
    (D.tautologicalSectionBaseSections.eval (Opposite.op ⊤))
  have hZ : AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme (cyclicCover N m σ) M' τ' =
      ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical := by
    refine (Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme_pullbackGlobalSections ι
      D.basePullbackInverse 1 _).trans ?_
    have h : Stacks.RegularSectionSequence.zeroScheme D.totalSpace D.basePullbackInverse
        (D.tautologicalSectionBaseSections.eval (Opposite.op ⊤)) = D.zeroSection.ker :=
      D.zeroScheme_tautologicalSectionBase_eq_ker_zeroSection
    rw [h]
    haveI := MMP.Resolution.Aux.isReduced_subscheme_of_isSmoothScheme f _ hD
    exact comap_ker_zeroSection_eq_radical N m (by omega) σ
  let s := Stacks.Divisors.sectionsOfTop M' τ'
  have hs : s.eval (Opposite.op ⊤) = τ' := by
    rw [Stacks.Divisors.sectionsOfTop_eval]
    simp only [homOfLE_refl, op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
    rfl
  have hreg : AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegularSection (cyclicCover N m σ).sheaf.obj
      (cyclicCover N m σ).ringCatSheaf.property s := by
    refine (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection _ M' s).mp ?_
    rw [hs, hZ]
    exact (MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow f hX N m hm σ hσ hD
      hDne).2.1
  have hinj : ∀ U : (cyclicCover N m σ).Opens, Function.Injective fun r : Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, U) =>
      r • M'.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op τ' := by
    intro U
    have h := Scheme.Modules.injective_unitHomEquiv_symm_app_of_isRegularSection M' s hreg U
    have he : ∀ r : Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, U),
        ((M'.unitHomEquiv.symm s).val.app (op U)).hom r =
        r • M'.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op τ' := by
      intro r
      rw [Scheme.Modules.unitHomEquiv_symm_app_apply, hs]
    exact fun a b hab => h (by rwa [he, he])
  let e₀ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorInverseIsoDualSheaf X.presheaf
    X.ringCatSheaf.2 N _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.mulNegOneIso X.presheaf X.ringCatSheaf.2 N)
  exact ⟨eqToIso (congrArg Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' hZ.symm) ≪≫
    (invertibleSheafIsoZeroScheme M' τ' hinj).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback ι).mapIso ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (symSpecToBase N)).mapIso e₀) ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp ι (symSpecToBase N)).app _⟩

/-! ### Divisors cut out by products of regular parameters -/

/-- The quotient of a ring by the unit ideal has length zero. -/
public lemma length_quotient_top (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    Module.length R (R ⧸ (⊤ : Ideal R)) = 0 :=
  Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mpr (Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.mpr rfl)

/-- Off the support of `I`, the length of `𝒪_{Y,x} / I_x` vanishes. -/
private lemma length_stalk_quotient_eq_zero {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData) {x : Y}
    (hx : x ∉ I.support) :
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk x)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I x)).toNat : ℤ) = 0 := by
  rw [(Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mpr hx, length_quotient_top]
  rfl

/-- Parameters at `y` adapted to the family `G`: a regular system of parameters `w` of `𝒪_{Y,y}`
and pairwise disjoint sets `S o` of indices with `(G o)_y = (∏_{i ∈ S o} w i)`. -/
private def AdaptedParams {Y : Scheme.{u}} {κ : Type*} (G : κ → Y.IdealSheafData) (y : Y) :
    Prop :=
  ∃ (n : ℕ) (w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (S : κ → Finset (Fin n)),
    IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ (∀ o o', o ≠ o' → Disjoint (S o) (S o')) ∧
      ∀ o, IdealSheafData.stalk (G o) y = Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S o, w i}

/-- If the generic point of a prime divisor `Q` lies on `V(I)`, then at every point the stalk of
`I` lies in that of the ideal of `Q`. -/
private lemma stalk_le_stalk_idealSheaf {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    {Q : PrimeDivisor Y} (hQ : Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support) (y : Y) :
    IdealSheafData.stalk I y ≤ IdealSheafData.stalk Q.idealSheaf y := by
  refine MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.stalk_mono ?_ y
  rw [← MMP.Intersection.vanishingIdeal_support_idealSheaf Q,
    ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_support_iff_le_vanishingIdeal]
  change Q.support ⊆ I.support
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
  exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hQ) I.support.isClosed

/-- A component through `y` of `E = ∑ₒ G o` has, at `y`, a member of an adapted regular system of
parameters as local equation. -/
private lemma exists_stalk_eq_span_of_adapted {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ] (G : κ → Y.IdealSheafData) (E : Divisor Y)
    (hE : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor Y, E.coeff P = ∑ o, ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (G o) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ))
    {Q : PrimeDivisor Y} (hQ : Q ∈ E.support) {y : Y} (hy : y ∈ Q.support) {n : ℕ}
    {w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y} {S : κ → Finset (Fin n)} (hw : IsRegularSystemOfParameters w)
    (hS : ∀ o, IdealSheafData.stalk (G o) y = Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S o, w i}) :
    ∃ i, IdealSheafData.stalk Q.idealSheaf y = Ideal.span {w i} := by
  obtain ⟨o, ho⟩ : ∃ o, Q.genericPoint ∈ (G o).support := by
    by_contra! h
    exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ <| (hE Q).trans <|
      Finset.sum_eq_zero fun o _ => length_stalk_quotient_eq_zero _ (h o)
  obtain ⟨q, -, hqE, hq1⟩ := MMP.Intersection.exists_stalk_idealSheaf_eq_of_mem_support Q hy
  have := isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hw
  have := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain (Y.presheaf.stalk y)
  have hprod : (∏ i ∈ S o, w i) ∈ q.asIdeal := by
    rw [← hqE]
    refine stalk_le_stalk_idealSheaf _ ho y ?_
    rw [hS o]
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
  obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := (Ideal.IsPrime.prod_mem_iff (hp := q.isPrime)).mp hprod
  exact ⟨i, hqE.trans (Ideal.eq_span_singleton_of_height_eq_one hq1 hi
    (MMP.Intersection.prime_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hw _))⟩

/-- **Snc from adapted parameters.** If at every point of `Y` the ideals `G o` are generated by
products of pairwise disjoint sets of members of a regular system of parameters, then
`E = ∑ₒ G o` is snc with all coefficients `1`. -/
private lemma isSNC_of_forall_adaptedParams {k : Type u} [Field k] [CharZero k]
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType sY] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ]
    (G : κ → Y.IdealSheafData) (E : Divisor Y)
    (hE : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor Y, E.coeff P = ∑ o, ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (G o) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ))
    (hG : ∀ y, AdaptedParams G y) :
    E.IsSNC sY ∧ ∀ P ∈ E.support, E.coeff P = 1 := by
  classical
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sY
  have param : ∀ y : Y, ∃ (n : ℕ) (w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y)
      (j : {Q : PrimeDivisor Y // Q ∈ E.support ∧ y ∈ Q.support} → Fin n),
      IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ Function.Injective j ∧
        ∀ Q, IdealSheafData.stalk Q.1.idealSheaf y = Ideal.span {w (j Q)} := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨n, w, S, hw, -, hS⟩ := hG y
    choose j hj using fun Q : {Q : PrimeDivisor Y // Q ∈ E.support ∧ y ∈ Q.support} =>
      exists_stalk_eq_span_of_adapted G E hE Q.2.1 Q.2.2 hw hS
    refine ⟨n, w, j, hw, fun Q Q' h => Subtype.ext
      (MMP.Intersection.eq_of_stalk_idealSheaf_eq Q.2.2 Q'.2.2 ?_), hj⟩
    rw [hj Q, hj Q', h]
  refine ⟨⟨fun Q hQ => ?_, param⟩, fun P hP => ?_⟩
  · refine MMP.Resolution.isSmoothScheme_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_span_parameter sY _ fun y hy => ?_
    obtain ⟨n, w, j, hw, -, hI⟩ := param y
    exact ⟨n, w, j ⟨Q, hQ, hy⟩, hw, hI ⟨Q, hQ, hy⟩⟩
  set η := P.genericPoint
  obtain ⟨n, w, S, hw, hdisj, hS⟩ := hG η
  obtain rfl : n = 1 := by
    have h := hw.2
    rw [ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight, P.coheight_genericPoint] at h
    exact_mod_cast h.symm
  have hterm : ∀ o, ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk η)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk η ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (G o) η)).toNat : ℤ) =
        if (S o).Nonempty then 1 else 0 := by
    intro o
    rw [hS o]
    split_ifs with h
    · have hSo : S o = Finset.univ := by
        obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := h
        exact Finset.eq_univ_of_forall fun j => Subsingleton.elim i j ▸ hi
      rw [hSo, Fin.prod_univ_one, show (0 : Fin 1) = default from rfl, ← Set.range_unique, hw.1]
      have : IsSimpleModule (Y.presheaf.stalk η)
          (Y.presheaf.stalk η ⧸ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk η)) :=
        isSimpleModule_iff_isCoatom.mpr
          (Ideal.isMaximal_def.mp (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _))
      rw [Module.length_eq_one]; rfl
    · rw [Finset.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.mp h, Finset.prod_empty, Ideal.span_singleton_one]
      rw [length_quotient_top]; rfl
  have hsum := hE P
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun o _ => hterm o, Finset.sum_boole] at hsum
  have hle : (Finset.univ.filter fun o => (S o).Nonempty).card ≤ 1 := by
    refine Finset.card_le_one.mpr fun a ha b hb => ?_
    by_contra hab
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.mp ha).2
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hb).2
    exact Finset.disjoint_left.mp (hdisj a b hab) hi (Subsingleton.elim j i ▸ hj)
  have hne : (Finset.univ.filter fun o => (S o).Nonempty).card ≠ 0 := fun h0 =>
    Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hP (hsum.trans (by rw [h0]; rfl))
  rw [hsum, show (Finset.univ.filter fun o => (S o).Nonempty).card = 1 by omega]
  rfl

/-! ### Adapted parameters on the base -/

/-- On an integral scheme an effective Cartier divisor has, at every point, a nonzero local
equation. -/
private lemma exists_stalk_eq_span_singleton_ne_zero {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y]
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I] (y : Y) :
    ∃ g : Y.presheaf.stalk y, g ≠ 0 ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {g} := by
  obtain ⟨V, hyV, g, hg, hV⟩ :=
    Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_isRegular I inferInstance y
  haveI : Nonempty (V : Y.Opens) := ⟨⟨y, hyV⟩⟩
  refine ⟨Y.presheaf.germ V y hyV g, fun h0 => hg.ne_zero ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact germ_injective_of_isIntegral Y y hyV (h0.trans (map_zero _).symm)
  · rw [IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ y V hyV, hV, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

/-- On a normal integral locally Noetherian scheme, if the stalk of an effective Cartier divisor
`I` at the generic point of a prime divisor `Q` lies in the `e`-th power of the maximal ideal, the
length of `𝒪_{X,Q} / I` is at least `e`. -/
private lemma le_length_of_stalk_le_pow {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [IsNormal Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData) [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I]
    (Q : PrimeDivisor Y) (e : ℕ)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint) ^ e) :
    (e : ℤ) ≤ ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
  set η := Q.genericPoint
  haveI : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Y.presheaf.stalk η) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UnitsNormalProper.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk
      (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.coheight_genericPoint Q)
  obtain ⟨g, hg0, hg⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_singleton_ne_zero I η
  have hne : IdealSheafData.stalk I η ≠ ⊥ := by
    rwa [hg, Ne, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot]
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible (Y.presheaf.stalk η)
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.ideal_eq_span_pow_irreducible hne hϖ
  have hmax : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk η) = Ideal.span {ϖ} :=
    (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer ϖ).mp hϖ
  have hd' : IdealSheafData.stalk I η = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ ^ d := by
    rw [hd, hmax, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  rw [hd', IsDiscreteValuationRing.length_quotient_pow_maximalIdeal]
  rw [hd'] at h
  have hanti := Ideal.pow_right_strictAnti (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk η))
    (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field _) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).ne_top
  have : e ≤ d := (StrictAnti.le_iff_ge hanti).mp h
  simpa using this

/-- At a point of the support, the length at the generic point of a prime divisor is positive. -/
private lemma one_le_length_of_mem_support {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I] (Q : PrimeDivisor Y)
    (h : Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support) :
    (1 : ℤ) ≤ ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
  have := le_length_of_stalk_le_pow I Q 1 ?_
  · exact_mod_cast this
  rw [pow_one]
  refine IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal fun htop => ?_
  exact (Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mp htop h

/-- The point of `Y` corresponding to a prime of `𝒪_{Y,x}` is a generization of `x`. -/
private lemma fromSpecStalk_specializes {Y : Scheme.{u}} (x : Y)
    (q : PrimeSpectrum (Y.presheaf.stalk x)) : Y.fromSpecStalk x q ⤳ x := by
  have : Y.fromSpecStalk x q ∈ Set.range (Y.fromSpecStalk x) := ⟨q, rfl⟩
  rwa [Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk] at this

/-- The stalk at a generization `η` of `x`, corresponding to the prime `q` of `𝒪_{X,x}`, of an
ideal sheaf whose stalk at `x` lies in `qᵉ` lies in the `e`-th power of the maximal ideal. -/
private lemma stalk_le_maximalIdeal_pow {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData) {x : Y}
    (q : PrimeSpectrum (Y.presheaf.stalk x)) (e : ℕ)
    (h : IdealSheafData.stalk I x ≤ q.asIdeal ^ e) :
    IdealSheafData.stalk I (Y.fromSpecStalk x q) ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (Y.fromSpecStalk x q)) ^ e := by
  have hsp := fromSpecStalk_specializes x q
  letI := (Y.presheaf.stalkSpecializes hsp).hom.toAlgebra
  haveI := Stacks.Chow.isLocalization_stalk_of_specializes hsp q rfl
  rw [Stacks.Chow.idealStalk_eq_map_stalkSpecializes I hsp,
    ← IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal q.asIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (Y.fromSpecStalk x q)),
    ← Ideal.map_pow]
  exact Ideal.map_mono h

/-- **Adapted parameters on the base.** Let `X` be a smooth variety and `H o` finitely many
effective Cartier divisors whose sum `B` is snc with all coefficients `1`. At every point the
`H o` are cut out by products of pairwise disjoint sets of members of one regular system of
parameters: the local equation of `H o` at `x` is the product of the equations of the components
of `B` through `x` which are components of `H o`, each with multiplicity one. -/
private lemma adaptedParams_of_isSNC {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [hXv : IsVariety k f] [Smooth f] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ]
    (H : κ → X.IdealSheafData) [∀ o, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (H o)]
    (B : Divisor X)
    (hB : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor X, B.coeff P = ∑ o, ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
      (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (H o) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ))
    (hsnc : B.IsSNC f) (hB1 : ∀ P ∈ B.support, B.coeff P = 1) (x : X) : AdaptedParams H x := by
  classical
  haveI : IsIntegral X := hXv.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  haveI : ∀ y : X, IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk y) :=
    isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field f
  haveI : ∀ y : X, IsDomain (X.presheaf.stalk y) := fun y => IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain _
  haveI : ∀ y : X, UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk y) :=
    fun y => IsRegularLocalRing.uniqueFactorizationMonoid _
  haveI : IsNormal X :=
    { stalk_isDomain := fun _ => inferInstance, stalk_normal := fun _ => inferInstance }
  set τ : PrimeDivisor X → κ → ℤ := fun P o => ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
      (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (H o) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ)
    with hτ
  have hB' : ∀ P, B.coeff P = ∑ o, τ P o := hB
  have hτ0 : ∀ P o, 0 ≤ τ P o := fun P o => Int.natCast_nonneg _
  have hle_coeff : ∀ P o, τ P o ≤ B.coeff P := fun P o => by
    rw [hB' P]; exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun o _ => hτ0 P o) (Finset.mem_univ o)
  -- a prime divisor whose generic point lies on `H o` is a component of `B` lying on no other `H`
  have K0 : ∀ (P : PrimeDivisor X) o, P.genericPoint ∈ (H o).support →
      P ∈ B.support ∧ ∀ o', o' ≠ o → P.genericPoint ∉ (H o').support := by
    intro P o hP
    have h1 : 1 ≤ τ P o := one_le_length_of_mem_support (H o) P hP
    have hPB : P ∈ B.support := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr fun h0 => by
      have := hle_coeff P o
      have h0' : B.coeff P = 0 := h0
      omega
    refine ⟨hPB, fun o' ho' hP' => ?_⟩
    have h1' : 1 ≤ τ P o' := one_le_length_of_mem_support (H o') P hP'
    have hsum : τ P o' + τ P o ≤ B.coeff P := by
      rw [hB' P, ← Finset.sum_pair ho']
      exact Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg (Finset.subset_univ _) fun o _ _ => hτ0 P o
    have := hB1 P hPB
    omega
  obtain ⟨n, v, jB, hv, hjB, hQ⟩ := hsnc.2 x
  haveI : Finite {Q : PrimeDivisor X // Q ∈ B.support ∧ x ∈ Q.support} :=
    Finite.of_injective jB hjB
  haveI : Fintype {Q : PrimeDivisor X // Q ∈ B.support ∧ x ∈ Q.support} := Fintype.ofFinite _
  let T : κ → Finset {Q : PrimeDivisor X // Q ∈ B.support ∧ x ∈ Q.support} := fun o =>
    Finset.univ.filter fun Q => Q.1.genericPoint ∈ (H o).support
  have hprime : ∀ Q : {Q : PrimeDivisor X // Q ∈ B.support ∧ x ∈ Q.support},
      Prime (v (jB Q)) := fun Q =>
    MMP.Intersection.prime_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hv _
  refine ⟨n, v, fun o => (T o).image jB, hv, ?_, fun o => ?_⟩
  · intro o o' hoo'
    rw [Finset.disjoint_left]
    intro i hi hi'
    obtain ⟨Q, hQT, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hi
    obtain ⟨Q', hQT', hQQ'⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hi'
    rw [hjB hQQ'] at hQT'
    exact (K0 Q.1 o (Finset.mem_filter.mp hQT).2).2 o' (Ne.symm hoo') (Finset.mem_filter.mp hQT').2
  show _ = Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ (T o).image jB, v i}
  rw [Finset.prod_image fun Q _ Q' _ h => hjB h]
  obtain ⟨g, hg0, hg⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_singleton_ne_zero (H o) x
  have hsub : ∀ Q ∈ T o, IdealSheafData.stalk (H o) x ≤ Ideal.span {v (jB Q)} := by
    intro Q hQT
    rw [← hQ Q]
    exact stalk_le_stalk_idealSheaf _ (Finset.mem_filter.mp hQT).2 x
  have hdvd : (∏ Q ∈ T o, v (jB Q)) ∣ g := by
    have hinf : IdealSheafData.stalk (H o) x ≤ (T o).inf fun Q => Ideal.span {v (jB Q)} :=
      Finset.le_inf hsub
    rw [MMP.Intersection.finsetInf_span_singleton_eq_span_prod _ _ (fun Q _ => hprime Q), hg,
      Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton] at hinf
    · exact hinf
    · intro Q _ Q' _ hass
      refine Subtype.ext (MMP.Intersection.eq_of_stalk_idealSheaf_eq Q.2.2 Q'.2.2 ?_)
      rw [hQ Q, hQ Q']
      exact Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.mpr hass
  obtain ⟨h, rfl⟩ := hdvd
  rw [hg]
  suffices hu : IsUnit h from Ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_unit hu _
  by_contra hu
  have h0 : h ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; exact hg0 (mul_zero _)
  obtain ⟨π, hπirr, hπh⟩ := WfDvdMonoid.exists_irreducible_factor hu h0
  have hπ : Prime π := UniqueFactorizationMonoid.irreducible_iff_prime.mp hπirr
  have hqprime : (Ideal.span {π}).IsPrime := (Ideal.span_singleton_prime hπ.ne_zero).mpr hπ
  let q : PrimeSpectrum (X.presheaf.stalk x) := ⟨Ideal.span {π}, hqprime⟩
  haveI : Submodule.IsPrincipal q.asIdeal := ⟨⟨π, rfl⟩⟩
  have hq1 : q.asIdeal.height = 1 := by
    refine le_antisymm (Ideal.height_le_one_of_isPrincipal_of_mem_minimalPrimes q.asIdeal _ ?_) ?_
    · rw [Ideal.minimalPrimes_eq_subsingleton_self]; rfl
    · rw [ENat.one_le_iff_ne_zero, Ne, Ideal.height_eq_zero_iff_eq_bot]
      change ¬ Ideal.span {π} = ⊥
      rw [Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot]; exact hπ.ne_zero
  have hη1 : Order.coheight (X.fromSpecStalk x q) = 1 := by
    have := Stacks.Chow.coheight_fromSpecStalk_eq_height x q
    rwa [hq1] at this
  set Q₀ : PrimeDivisor X := AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.ofCoheightOne (X.fromSpecStalk x q) hη1
  have hQ₀η' : AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint Q₀ = X.fromSpecStalk x q :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_ofCoheightOne _ hη1
  have hQ₀η : Q₀.genericPoint = X.fromSpecStalk x q := hQ₀η'
  have hxQ₀ : x ∈ Q₀.support := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure, hQ₀η', ← specializes_iff_mem_closure]
    exact fromSpecStalk_specializes x q
  have hQ₀x : IdealSheafData.stalk Q₀.idealSheaf x = Ideal.span {π} := by
    obtain ⟨q', hq', hq'E, -⟩ := MMP.Intersection.exists_stalk_idealSheaf_eq_of_mem_support Q₀ hxQ₀
    rw [hQ₀η] at hq'
    have : q' = q := (X.fromSpecStalk x).isEmbedding.injective hq'
    rw [hq'E, this]
  have hgq : (∏ Q ∈ T o, v (jB Q)) * h ∈ q.asIdeal :=
    Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mpr hπh)
  have hηH : Q₀.genericPoint ∈ (H o).support := by
    rw [hQ₀η]
    refine (Stacks.Chow.le_iff_fromSpecStalk_mem_support (H o) x q).mp ?_
    rwa [hg, Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
  obtain ⟨hQ₀B, -⟩ := K0 Q₀ o hηH
  let Q₀' : {Q : PrimeDivisor X // Q ∈ B.support ∧ x ∈ Q.support} := ⟨Q₀, hQ₀B, hxQ₀⟩
  have hQ₀T : Q₀' ∈ T o := Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hηH⟩
  have hass : Associated π (v (jB Q₀')) :=
    (Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton.mp ((hQ Q₀').symm.trans hQ₀x)).symm
  have hπ2 : π ^ 2 ∣ (∏ Q ∈ T o, v (jB Q)) * h := by
    rw [pow_two]
    exact mul_dvd_mul (hass.dvd.trans (Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem _ hQ₀T)) hπh
  have hle2 : IdealSheafData.stalk (H o) x ≤ q.asIdeal ^ 2 := by
    rw [hg]
    change _ ≤ Ideal.span {π} ^ 2
    rwa [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton]
  have h2 : (2 : ℤ) ≤ τ Q₀ o :=
    le_length_of_stalk_le_pow (H o) Q₀ 2 (by
      rw [hQ₀η]; exact stalk_le_maximalIdeal_pow (H o) q 2 hle2)
  have := hle_coeff Q₀ o
  rw [hB1 Q₀ hQ₀B] at this
  omega

/-- On a variety, a finite family of effective Cartier divisors defines a Weil divisor whose
coefficient at `P` is the sum of the lengths of `𝒪_P / (Gⱼ)_P`: only finitely many prime divisors
have their generic point in the support of some `Gⱼ`, and off that support the summand vanishes. -/
private lemma exists_divisor_coeff_eq_sum_length {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k sY] {κ : Type*} [Fintype κ]
    (G : κ → Y.IdealSheafData) [hG : ∀ j, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (G j)] :
    ∃ E : Divisor Y, ∀ P : PrimeDivisor Y, E.coeff P =
      ∑ j, ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk (G j) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sY
  haveI : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sY
  haveI : IsNoetherian Y := ⟨⟩
  set c : PrimeDivisor Y → ℤ := fun P => ∑ j,
      ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (G j) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ)
  have hfin : (Function.support c).Finite := by
    refine (Set.finite_iUnion fun j => finite_setOf_genericPoint_mem
      (G j).support.isClosed fun s hs h0 => ?_).subset ?_
    · have hmax : IsMax s := Order.coheight_eq_zero.mp h0
      have hgen : genericPoint Y ⤳ s := (genericPoint_spec Y).specializes trivial
      have hgs : genericPoint Y = s :=
        (hgen.antisymm (hmax (show s ≤ genericPoint Y from hgen))).eq
      refine notMem_support_of_mem_genericPoints_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor (G j) (hG j)
        (x := genericPoint Y) ?_ (hgs ▸ hs)
      show closure ({genericPoint Y} : Set Y) ∈ irreducibleComponents Y
      rw [show closure ({genericPoint Y} : Set Y) = Set.univ from genericPoint_spec Y,
        irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]
      rfl
    · intro P hP
      obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero hP
      refine Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨j, ?_⟩
      by_contra hn
      exact hj (length_stalk_quotient_eq_zero _ hn)
  exact ⟨Finsupp.ofSupportFinite c hfin, fun P => rfl⟩

/-! ### Regular systems of parameters along the cover -/

/-- If `φ : A → B` is a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings with `𝔪_B = 𝔪_A B` and
`dim B = dim A`, the image of a regular system of parameters of `A` is one of `B`. -/
private lemma isRegularSystemOfParameters_comp_of_map_maximalIdeal {A B : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B] (φ : A →+* B) {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → A}
    (hv : IsRegularSystemOfParameters v)
    (hmax : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map φ = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim B = ringKrullDim A) : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (φ ∘ v) := by
  refine ⟨?_, hdim.trans hv.2⟩
  rw [Set.range_comp, ← Ideal.map_span, hv.1, hmax]

/-- Let `φ : A → B` be a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings, `v` a regular system of
parameters of `A`, and `t ∈ 𝔪_B` a non-zero-divisor such that `φ(v i₀) ∈ (t)`, every element of
`𝔪_B` is `φ(a) + (t)` with `a ∈ 𝔪_A`, and `dim B = dim A/(v i₀) + 1`. Then replacing `φ(v i₀)` by
`t` gives a regular system of parameters of `B`. -/
private lemma isRegularSystemOfParameters_update {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing B] (φ : A →+* B) [IsLocalHom φ] {n : ℕ}
    {v : Fin n → A} (hv : IsRegularSystemOfParameters v) (i₀ : Fin n) {t : B}
    (ht : t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
    (hgen : ∀ y ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B, ∃ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A,
      y - φ a ∈ Ideal.span {t})
    (hvi₀ : φ (v i₀) ∈ Ideal.span {t})
    (hdim : ringKrullDim B = ringKrullDim (A ⧸ Ideal.span {v i₀}) + 1) :
    IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Function.update (φ ∘ v) i₀ t) := by
  classical
  have := isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hv
  set w := Function.update (φ ∘ v) i₀ t
  have hw : ∀ i, w i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B := fun i => by
    by_cases hi : i = i₀
    · subst hi; simp only [w, Function.update_self]; exact ht
    · simp only [w, Function.update_of_ne hi, Function.comp_apply]
      have hvi : v i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := hv.1 ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
      exact map_nonunit φ _ hvi
  have htw : Ideal.span {t} ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range w) := by
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i₀, by simp [w]⟩
  have hφv : ∀ i, φ (v i) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range w) := fun i => by
    by_cases hi : i = i₀
    · subst hi; exact htw hvi₀
    · exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, by simp [w, Function.update_of_ne hi]⟩
  refine ⟨le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_) fun y hy => ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact hw i
  · obtain ⟨a, ha, hya⟩ := hgen y hy
    have hφa : φ a ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range w) := by
      rw [← hv.1] at ha
      obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun A).mp ha
      rw [map_sum]
      exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun i _ => by
        rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (hφv i)
    have := Ideal.add_mem _ (htw hya) hφa
    rwa [sub_add_cancel] at this
  · rw [hdim, MMP.Resolution.ringKrullDim_quotient_span_singleton_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters
      hv i₀]
    have h1 : 1 ≤ n := Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr fun h => (h ▸ i₀).elim0
    obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le h1
    simp only [Nat.add_sub_cancel_left]
    push_cast
    rw [add_comm]

/-- A member of a regular system of parameters, or a product over a nonempty set of them, lies in
the maximal ideal. -/
private lemma prod_mem_maximalIdeal {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] {n : ℕ}
    {v : Fin n → A} (hv : IsRegularSystemOfParameters v) {S : Finset (Fin n)} (hS : S.Nonempty) :
    (∏ i ∈ S, v i) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hS
  rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase S v hi]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (hv.1 ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)

/-- If the product of the members of a regular system of parameters indexed by `S` generates a
prime ideal, `S` is a singleton. -/
private lemma exists_eq_singleton_of_isPrime {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → A} (hv : IsRegularSystemOfParameters v)
    {S : Finset (Fin n)} (hP : (Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S, v i}).IsPrime) : ∃ i₀, S = {i₀} := by
  classical
  have := isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hv
  have := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain A
  rcases S.eq_empty_or_nonempty with rfl | ⟨i, hi⟩
  · exact absurd (by rw [Finset.prod_empty, Ideal.span_singleton_one]) hP.ne_top
  refine ⟨i, ?_⟩
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hji⟩ : ∃ j ∈ S, j ≠ i := by
    by_contra! h
    exact hne (Finset.eq_singleton_iff_unique_mem.mpr ⟨hi, h⟩)
  have h0 : (∏ i ∈ S, v i) ≠ 0 := Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun l _ =>
    (MMP.Intersection.prime_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters hv l).ne_zero
  have hprime : Prime (∏ i ∈ S, v i) := (Ideal.span_singleton_prime h0).mp hP
  rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase S v hi] at hprime
  rcases hprime.irreducible.isUnit_or_isUnit rfl with hu | hu
  · exact (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp (hv.1 ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩) hu
  · exact (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp
      (prod_mem_maximalIdeal hv ⟨j, Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hji, hj⟩⟩) hu

/-- The zero scheme of a non-zero `σ` on an integral scheme is an effective Cartier divisor: on
a chart its ideal is generated by one non-zero function. -/
private lemma isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroSchemeIdeal {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) := by
  refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen _ fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, g, -, -, -, -, hIU⟩ := exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ x
  haveI : Nonempty U.1 := ⟨⟨x, hxU⟩⟩
  refine ⟨U.1, U.2, hxU, g, IsRegular.of_ne_zero ?_, hIU⟩
  rintro rfl
  exact zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_ne_bot N σ hσ U (hIU.trans (by simp))

/-- In `B = A[T]/(Tᵐ - g)` with `m` invertible in `A`, every localization `S` of `B` away from the
class `t` of `T` is formally unramified over `A`. -/
private lemma formallyUnramified_of_isLocalization_away {A B S : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing S] {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) (hmu : IsUnit (m : A)) {g : A}
    (φ : Polynomial A →+* B) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : RingHom.ker φ = Ideal.span {Polynomial.X ^ m - Polynomial.C g}) (ρ : B →+* S)
    (hρ : letI := ρ.toAlgebra; IsLocalization.Away (φ Polynomial.X) S) :
    (ρ.comp (φ.comp Polynomial.C)).FormallyUnramified := by
  letI : Algebra A B := (φ.comp Polynomial.C).toAlgebra
  let φ' : Polynomial A →ₐ[A] B := { φ with commutes' := fun r => rfl }
  haveI := etale_localization_away_of_ker_eq_span hm hmu φ' hφ hker
  letI : Algebra B S := ρ.toAlgebra
  letI : Algebra A S := (ρ.comp (φ.comp Polynomial.C)).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower A B S := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl
  let e : Localization.Away (φ Polynomial.X) ≃ₐ[B] S :=
    IsLocalization.algEquiv (Submonoid.powers (φ Polynomial.X)) _ _
  haveI : Algebra.FormallyUnramified A (Localization.Away (φ' Polynomial.X)) := inferInstance
  exact Algebra.FormallyUnramified.of_equiv (e.restrictScalars A)

/-- **Off the branch divisor.** At a point `z` of the cyclic cover over `x ∉ D`, the maximal
ideal of `𝒪_{Z,z}` is generated by that of `𝒪_{X,x}`, and the two local rings have the same
dimension: the cover is étale there. -/
private lemma map_maximalIdeal_and_ringKrullDim_of_notMem (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hD : Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) (z : cyclicCover N m σ)
    (hz : ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z ∉ (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support) :
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z))).map
        ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).stalkMap z).hom =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) ∧
    ringKrullDim ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) =
      ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)) := by
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by omega
  obtain ⟨-, hsm, hfin, hflat, -⟩ :=
    ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne
  set p := ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ with hp
  haveI : IsAffineHom p := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType p :=
    ((IsFinite.iff_isIntegralHom_and_locallyOfFiniteType p).mp hfin).2
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, g, φ, hφs, hφC, hker, hIU⟩ := exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ (p z)
  set t := φ Polynomial.X
  have hV : IsAffineOpen (p ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := U.2.preimage p
  have hgx : IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ U.1 (p z) hxU g) := by
    have h := (Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mpr hz
    rw [IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ (p z) U hxU, hIU, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton,
      Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top] at h
    exact h
  have hzV : z ∈ (cyclicCover N m σ).basicOpen t := by
    have h1 : p z ∈ X.basicOpen g := (X.mem_basicOpen g (p z) hxU).mpr hgx
    have h2 : z ∈ p ⁻¹ᵁ X.basicOpen g := h1
    rwa [Scheme.preimage_basicOpen, show (p.app U.1) g = φ (Polynomial.C g) from
      (RingHom.congr_fun hφC g).symm, map_C_eq_pow hker, Scheme.basicOpen_pow _ _ hm0] at h2
  set V' := (cyclicCover N m σ).basicOpen t
  have e : V' ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 := (cyclicCover N m σ).basicOpen_le t
  haveI : IsAffine U.1.toScheme := U.2
  haveI : IsAffine V'.toScheme := hV.basicOpen t
  have hmu : IsUnit (m : Γ(X, U.1)) := by
    let ρ : k →+* Γ(X, U.1) := (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op).hom.comp
      ((f.app ⊤).hom.comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv.hom)
    have h : IsUnit (m : k) := (Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 (by omega)).isUnit
    exact map_natCast ρ m ▸ h.map ρ
  have hFU : FormallyUnramified (p.resLE U.1 V' e) := by
    rw [HasRingHomProperty.iff_of_isAffine (P := @FormallyUnramified), Scheme.Hom.appTop,
      Scheme.Hom.resLE_app_top, CommRingCat.hom_comp,
      RingHom.FormallyUnramified.respectsIso.cancel_left_isIso, CommRingCat.hom_comp,
      RingHom.FormallyUnramified.respectsIso.cancel_right_isIso, Scheme.Hom.appLE,
      CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← hφC]
    exact formallyUnramified_of_isLocalization_away hm0 hmu φ hφs hker _
      (hV.isLocalization_basicOpen t)
  have hunr : (p.stalkMap z).hom.FormallyUnramified := by
    have := FormallyUnramified.stalkMap (p.resLE U.1 V' e) ⟨z, hzV⟩
    exact (RingHom.FormallyUnramified.respectsIso.arrow_mk_iso_iff
      (p.resLEStalkMap e ⟨z, hzV⟩)).mp this
  have hft : (p.stalkMap z).hom.EssFiniteType := LocallyOfFiniteType.stalkMap p z
  have hfl : (p.stalkMap z).hom.Flat := Flat.stalkMap p z
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian (cyclicCover N m σ) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (p ≫ f)
  letI : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk (p z)) ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) :=
    (p.stalkMap z).hom.toAlgebra
  haveI : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk (p z)) ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsLocalHom (p.stalkMap z).hom)
  haveI : Algebra.EssFiniteType (X.presheaf.stalk (p z)) ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) :=
    hft
  haveI : Algebra.FormallyUnramified (X.presheaf.stalk (p z))
      ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) := hunr
  haveI : Module.Flat (X.presheaf.stalk (p z)) ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) := hfl
  have hmax : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (p z))).map
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk (p z)) ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.map_maximalIdeal
  refine ⟨hmax, ?_⟩
  rw [ringKrullDim_eq_add_ringKrullDim_closedFibre _ _ hfl]
  have h0 : ringKrullDim (ClosedFibre (X.presheaf.stalk (p z))
      ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z)) = 0 := by
    unfold ClosedFibre
    rw [hmax]
    exact ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_isField (Ideal.Quotient.maximal_ideal_iff_isField_quotient _ |>.mp
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _))
  rw [h0, add_zero]

/-- The reduced inverse image of the branch divisor maps isomorphically onto it. -/
private lemma isIso_subschemeMap_radical {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hD : IsSmoothScheme ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hle : zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ ≤
      ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical.map
        (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)) :
    IsIso (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap _ _ (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) hle) := by
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by omega
  haveI : IsAffineHom (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  haveI hDred : IsReduced (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subscheme :=
    MMP.Resolution.Aux.isReduced_subscheme_of_isSmoothScheme f _ hD
  set p := ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ
  set I := zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ
  set R := (I.comap p).radical with hR
  choose U hxU g φ hsurj hC hker hIU using exists_cyclicCover_chart N m σ
  let V : X → (cyclicCover N m σ).affineOpens := fun x => ⟨p ⁻¹ᵁ (U x).1, (U x).2.preimage p⟩
  have hcomap : ∀ x, (I.comap p).ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {φ x Polynomial.X ^ m} := fun x => by
    rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I p (U x) (V x) le_rfl,
      Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app, hIU x, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, ← hC x,
      RingHom.comp_apply, map_C_eq_pow (hker x)]
  have hrad : ∀ x, (Ideal.span {g x}).IsRadical := fun x =>
    hIU x ▸ isRadical_ideal_of_isReduced I (U x)
  have hRV : ∀ x, R.ideal (V x) = Ideal.span {φ x Polynomial.X} := fun x => by
    rw [hR, Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal, hcomap,
      radical_span_pow hm0 (hsurj x) (hker x) (hrad x)]
  exact isIso_subschemeMap_of_charts p I hle hm0 U hxU g φ hsurj hC hker hIU hRV

/-- An isomorphism of stalks along an equality of points carries the stalks of an ideal sheaf
to each other. -/
private lemma comap_stalkCongr_stalk {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData) {a b : Y}
    (h : Inseparable a b) :
    Ideal.comap (Y.presheaf.stalkCongr h).hom.hom (IdealSheafData.stalk I b) =
      IdealSheafData.stalk I a := by
  rw [Stacks.Chow.idealStalk_eq_map_stalkSpecializes I h.ge]
  exact Ideal.comap_map_of_bijective _
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (Y.presheaf.stalkCongr h).hom)

/-- If `p` restricts to an isomorphism `V(R) ≅ V(I)`, then at a point `w` of `V(R)` the composite
`𝒪_{X,p(w)} → 𝒪_{Z,w} → 𝒪_{V(R),w}` is surjective with kernel the stalk of `I`. -/
private lemma surjective_and_ker_stalkMap_comp {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (p : Z ⟶ X)
    (R : Z.IdealSheafData) (I : X.IdealSheafData) (hle : I ≤ R.map p)
    [IsIso (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap R I p hle)] (w : R.subscheme) :
    Function.Surjective ((R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom.comp (p.stalkMap (R.subschemeι w)).hom) ∧
      RingHom.ker ((R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom.comp (p.stalkMap (R.subschemeι w)).hom) =
        IdealSheafData.stalk I (p (R.subschemeι w)) := by
  set G := Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap R I p hle
  have hsq : G ≫ I.subschemeι = R.subschemeι ≫ p :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι R I p hle
  have hpt : (R.subschemeι ≫ p) w = (G ≫ I.subschemeι) w := by rw [hsq]
  set c := (X.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hpt)).hom
  have h2 : (R.subschemeι ≫ p).stalkMap w = c ≫ (G ≫ I.subschemeι).stalkMap w :=
    Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_congr_hom _ _ hsq.symm w
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp, Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp] at h2
  have key : (R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom.comp (p.stalkMap (R.subschemeι w)).hom =
      ((G.stalkMap w).hom.comp (I.subschemeι.stalkMap (G w)).hom).comp c.hom :=
    congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom h2
  rw [key]
  haveI : IsIso (G.stalkMap w) := ((isIso_iff_isIso_stalkMap G).mp inferInstance).2 w
  have hGi := ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (G.stalkMap w)
  refine ⟨(hGi.2.comp (I.subschemeι.stalkMap_surjective (G w))).comp
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso c).2, ?_⟩
  refine (RingHom.comap_ker _ _).symm.trans ?_
  rw [RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _ hGi.1, IdealSheafData.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι_eq_stalk]
  exact comap_stalkCongr_stalk I (Inseparable.of_eq hpt)

/-- **Over the branch divisor.** At a point `z` of the cyclic cover over `x ∈ D`, the reduced
inverse image `R` of `D` has a local equation `t ∈ 𝔪_z`, every element of `𝔪_z` is the image of
an element of `𝔪_x` modulo `t`, the equations of `D` at `x` become multiples of `t`, and
`dim 𝒪_{Z,z} = dim 𝒪_{D,x} + 1`: the subscheme `R` maps isomorphically onto `D`. -/
private lemma exists_local_equation_of_mem (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hD : Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ)) (z : cyclicCover N m σ)
    (hz : ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z ∈ (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support) :
    ∃ t : (cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z,
      IdealSheafData.stalk ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical z =
        Ideal.span {t} ∧ t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ ∧
      (∀ y ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z),
        ∃ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)),
          y - ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).stalkMap z).hom a ∈ Ideal.span {t}) ∧
      (∀ a ∈ IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z),
        ((ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ).stalkMap z).hom a ∈ Ideal.span {t}) ∧
      ringKrullDim ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z) =
        ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z) ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)) + 1 := by
  obtain ⟨hvar, hsm, hfin, hflat, -⟩ :=
    ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne
  haveI : IsIntegral (cyclicCover N m σ) := hvar.toIsIntegral
  haveI := AlgebraicGeometry.instLocallyOfFinitePresentationOfSmooth _ (hf := hD)
  have hbr := ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow f
    ((isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance) N m hm σ hσ ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hD) hDne
  haveI hRc := hbr.2.1
  have hle : zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ ≤
      ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical.map
        (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le.2 (Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_radical _)
  haveI := isIso_subschemeMap_radical f N m hm σ ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hD) hle
  haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) :=
    ((IsFinite.iff_isIntegralHom_and_locallyOfFiniteType _).mp hfin).2
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian (cyclicCover N m σ) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f)
  set p := ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ
  set I := zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ
  set R := (I.comap p).radical
  have hzR : z ∈ R.support := by
    rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_radical, MMP.Resolution.mem_support_comap_iff]
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ : z ∈ Set.range R.subschemeι := by rwa [R.range_subschemeι]
  obtain ⟨t, ht0, hRt⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_singleton_ne_zero R (R.subschemeι w)
  obtain ⟨hψs, hψk⟩ := surjective_and_ker_stalkMap_comp p R I hle w
  have hπk : RingHom.ker (R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom = Ideal.span {t} :=
    (IdealSheafData.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι_eq_stalk R w).trans hRt
  have hπs : Function.Surjective (R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom :=
    R.subschemeι.stalkMap_surjective w
  have hne : IdealSheafData.stalk R (R.subschemeι w) ≠ ⊤ := fun htop =>
    (Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mp htop hzR
  have htm : t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ :=
    IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hne (by rw [hRt]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self t)
  refine ⟨t, hRt, htm, fun y hy => ?_, fun a ha => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hψs ((R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom y)
    refine ⟨a, ?_, ?_⟩
    · by_contra hna
      have hu : IsUnit a := by
        by_contra hu'; exact hna ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mpr hu')
      have : IsUnit ((R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom y) := ha ▸ hu.map _
      exact (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp hy
        (isUnit_of_map_unit (R.subschemeι.stalkMap w).hom y this)
    · rw [← hπk, RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, ← RingHom.comp_apply, ha, sub_self]
  · rwa [← hπk, RingHom.mem_ker, ← RingHom.comp_apply, ← RingHom.mem_ker, hψk]
  · haveI := isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field (p ≫ f) (R.subschemeι w)
    haveI := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk (R.subschemeι w))
    let e1 := (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hπk.symm).trans (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hπs)
    let e2 := (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hψk.symm).trans (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hψs)
    rw [← ringKrullDim_quotient_span_singleton_succ_eq_ringKrullDim_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero ht0) htm, ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (e1.trans e2.symm)]

/-- **The local computation of Claim 2.65.** At every point `z` of the cover, over `x ∈ X`, the
divisors `p⁻¹(D)_red` and `p⁻¹(F j)` are cut out by products of pairwise disjoint sets of members of
one regular system of parameters of `𝒪_{Z,z}`: off `D` the pull-back of adapted parameters at
`x`; over `D`, the same with the equation of `D` replaced by that of `p⁻¹(D)_red`. -/
private lemma exists_params_cyclicCover (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hD : Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ))
    {ι : Type*} (F : ι → X.IdealSheafData) (z : cyclicCover N m σ) {n : ℕ}
    (v : Fin n → X.presheaf.stalk (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)) (S : Option ι → Finset (Fin n))
    (hv : IsRegularSystemOfParameters v) (hdisj : ∀ o o', o ≠ o' → Disjoint (S o) (S o'))
    (hS : ∀ o, IdealSheafData.stalk ((o.elim (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) F : X.IdealSheafData))
      (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z) = Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S o, v i}) :
    ∃ w : Fin n → (cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk z, IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧
      ∀ o, IdealSheafData.stalk ((o.elim
        ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical
        fun j => (F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ) : (cyclicCover N m σ).IdealSheafData))
          z = Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S o, w i} := by
  classical
  revert v S hv hdisj hS
  set p := ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ with hp
  intro v S hv hdisj hS
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  set φ := (p.stalkMap z).hom
  have hSj : ∀ j, IdealSheafData.stalk ((F j).comap p) z =
      Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S (some j), φ (v i)} := by
    intro j
    rw [IdealSheafData.stalk_comap, show IdealSheafData.stalk (F j) (p z) = _ from hS (some j),
      Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_prod]
  by_cases hx : p z ∈ (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).support
  · have hsmD := (isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hD
    have hDreg := MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk f _ hsmD hx
    have hDprime : (IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (p z)).IsPrime := by
      have := IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain
        (X.presheaf.stalk (p z) ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (p z))
      exact (Ideal.Quotient.isDomain_iff_prime _).mp this
    have hS0 : IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (p z) =
        Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S none, v i} := hS none
    obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := exists_eq_singleton_of_isPrime hv (hS0 ▸ hDprime)
    obtain ⟨t, hRt, htm, hgen, hDt, hdim⟩ :=
      exists_local_equation_of_mem k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne z hx
    have hvi₀ : φ (v i₀) ∈ Ideal.span {t} := by
      refine hDt _ ?_
      rw [hS0, hi₀, Finset.prod_singleton]
      exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    haveI : IsLocalHom φ := inferInstanceAs (IsLocalHom (p.stalkMap z).hom)
    have hw := isRegularSystemOfParameters_update φ hv i₀ htm hgen hvi₀
      (by rw [hdim, hS0, hi₀, Finset.prod_singleton])
    refine ⟨_, hw, fun o => ?_⟩
    cases o with
    | none =>
      change IdealSheafData.stalk ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap p).radical z = _
      rw [hRt, hi₀, Finset.prod_singleton, Function.update_self]
    | some j =>
      change IdealSheafData.stalk ((F j).comap p) z = _
      rw [hSj j]
      refine congrArg (fun r => Ideal.span {r}) (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_)
      have hne : i ≠ i₀ := fun h => Finset.disjoint_left.mp (hdisj (some j) none (by simp)) hi
        (by rw [hi₀, h]; exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _)
      rw [Function.update_of_ne hne]; rfl
  · obtain ⟨hmax, hdim⟩ := map_maximalIdeal_and_ringKrullDim_of_notMem k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne z hx
    have hw := isRegularSystemOfParameters_comp_of_map_maximalIdeal φ hv hmax hdim
    have hS0 : S none = ∅ := by
      by_contra hne
      have h := hS none
      change IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) (p z) = _ at h
      rw [(Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mpr hx] at h
      exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp
        (h ▸ (Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).mpr
          (prod_mem_maximalIdeal hv (Finset.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.mpr hne))))
    refine ⟨_, hw, fun o => ?_⟩
    cases o with
    | none =>
      change IdealSheafData.stalk ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap p).radical z = _
      rw [hS0, Finset.prod_empty, Ideal.span_singleton_one]
      refine (Stacks.Divisors.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mpr ?_
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_radical, MMP.Resolution.mem_support_comap_iff]
    | some j => exact hSj j

/-- **Pullback of an snc divisor along a ramified cyclic cover.** Let `f : X ⟶ Spec k` be a smooth
variety over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, `N = L⁻¹` an invertible sheaf,
`m ≥ 2` and `σ = ⟨·, s⟩ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X` non-zero with zero scheme `D` smooth over `k` and
non-empty, and `p : Z ⟶ X` the ramified cyclic cover. Let `F j`, `j ∈ ι`, be finitely many
effective Cartier divisors on `X` such that the divisor `B = D + ∑ⱼ F j` is snc with all
coefficients `1`. Then each `(F j).comap p` is an effective Cartier divisor, smooth whenever
`F j` is, and the divisor
`E = p⁻¹(D)_red + ∑ⱼ (F j).comap p` on `Z` is snc over `k` with all coefficients `1`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_cyclic_cover_snc_pullback"]
public theorem isSNC_ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_of_isSNC
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [IsVariety k f] [Smooth f] (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 0) (hD : Smooth ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hDne : Nonempty (zeroScheme N m σ))
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (F : ι → X.IdealSheafData)
    [∀ j, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (F j)]
    (B : Divisor X)
    (hB : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor X, B.coeff P =
      ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
        (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸
          IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) +
      ∑ j, ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
        (X.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk (F j) P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ))
    (hsnc : B.IsSNC f) (hB1 : ∀ P ∈ B.support, B.coeff P = 1) :
    (∀ j, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor ((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ))) ∧
      (∀ j, Smooth ((F j).subschemeι ≫ f) →
        Smooth (((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).subschemeι ≫
          ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f)) ∧
      ∃ E : Divisor (cyclicCover N m σ),
        (∀ P : PrimeDivisor (cyclicCover N m σ), E.coeff P =
          ((Module.length ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
            ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸
              IdealSheafData.stalk
                ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical
                P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) +
          ∑ j, ((Module.length ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
            ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸
              IdealSheafData.stalk ((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ))
                P.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ)) ∧
        E.IsSNC (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) ∧ ∀ P ∈ E.support, E.coeff P = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨hvar, hsm, -, hflat, -⟩ :=
    ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne
  have hF : ∀ j, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      ((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)) := fun j =>
    Stacks.Divisors.isPullbackDefined_of_flat _ (F j) inferInstance
  haveI := AlgebraicGeometry.instLocallyOfFinitePresentationOfSmooth _ (hf := hD)
  have hG₀ : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical :=
    (ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow f
      ((isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance) N m hm σ hσ
      ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hD) hDne).2.1
  let G : Option ι → (cyclicCover N m σ).IdealSheafData := fun o => o.elim
    ((zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).radical
    fun j => (F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)
  have hGc : ∀ o, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (G o) := fun o => by
    cases o with
    | none => exact hG₀
    | some j => exact hF j
  haveI : IsIntegral X := (inferInstance : IsVariety k f).toIsIntegral
  haveI := isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ hσ
  let H : Option ι → X.IdealSheafData := fun o => o.elim (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) F
  haveI : ∀ o, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (H o) := fun o => by
    cases o with
    | none => exact this
    | some j => exact inferInstanceAs (Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (F j))
  have hbase : ∀ x, AdaptedParams H x := adaptedParams_of_isSNC f H B
    (fun P => by rw [hB P, Fintype.sum_option]; rfl) hsnc hB1
  refine ⟨hF, fun j hFs => ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- a smooth `F j` is cut out at each of its points by one member of the parameters
    haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType (((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).subschemeι ≫
        ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) := locallyOfFiniteType_comp _ _
    haveI : LocallyOfFinitePresentation (((F j).comap (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ)).subschemeι ≫
        ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) :=
      (LocallyOfFinitePresentation.iff_locallyOfFiniteType).mpr inferInstance
    refine (isSmoothScheme_iff _).mp
      (MMP.Resolution.isSmoothScheme_subscheme_of_stalk_eq_span_parameter
        (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) _ fun z hz => ?_)
    obtain ⟨n, v, S, hv, hdisj, hS⟩ := hbase (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwS⟩ := exists_params_cyclicCover k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne F z v S hv hdisj hS
    have hx : ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z ∈ (F j).support :=
      (MMP.Resolution.mem_support_comap_iff _ _ _).mp hz
    have hreg := MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_stalk f (F j)
      ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hFs) hx
    have hprime : (IdealSheafData.stalk (F j) (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)).IsPrime :=
      (Ideal.Quotient.isDomain_iff_prime _).mp (IsRegularLocalRing.isDomain _)
    have hSj : IdealSheafData.stalk (F j) (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z) =
        Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ S (some j), v i} := hS (some j)
    rw [hSj] at hprime
    haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_eq_singleton_of_isPrime hv hprime
    refine ⟨n, w, i, hw, ?_⟩
    have := hwS (some j)
    rwa [hi, Finset.prod_singleton] at this
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := exists_divisor_coeff_eq_sum_length (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) G
  refine ⟨E, fun P => by rw [hE P, Fintype.sum_option]; rfl, ?_⟩
  refine isSNC_of_forall_adaptedParams (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ ≫ f) G E hE fun z => ?_
  obtain ⟨n, v, S, hv, hdisj, hS⟩ := hbase (ramifiedCyclicCover N m σ z)
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwS⟩ := exists_params_cyclicCover k f N m hm σ hσ hD hDne F z v S hv hdisj hS
  exact ⟨n, w, S, hw, hdisj, hwS⟩

section CoveringTrick

open MMP.Threefold.Resolution (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant')
open MMP.Flips (primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support eq_of_genericPoint_mem_primeDivisor_support)

/-- A divisor on a normal locally Noetherian scheme is its own pull-back along the identity. -/
public theorem divisor_isPullback_id {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (D : Divisor X)
    (hD : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X, (𝟙 X) (componentGenericPoint X C) ∉ D.supp) :
    D.IsPullback (𝟙 X) hD D := by
  intro U φ hφ E hE
  have hηU : componentGenericPoint X E.component ∈ U := E.map_componentGenericPoint_mem (𝟙 X) hE
  have hW : componentGenericPoint X E.component ∈ E.component.1 :=
    (isGenericPoint_componentGenericPoint X E.component).mem
  let a := Units.map (RationalFunctions.component X E.component).toMonoidHom φ
  have ha : (stalkToRationalFunctions X hW).hom a = (φ : RationalFunctions X) E.component := by
    simp [stalkToRationalFunctions, a, RationalFunctions.component]
  rw [pullbackComponent_eq hD hφ hηU hW a ha, hφ E hE, PrimeDivisor.ord_eq_ordUnit]
  congr 1
  ext
  simp [a]
  rfl

/-- A `ℚ`-divisor is its own pull-back along the identity. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_id {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (M : QDivisor X)
    (hM : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X, (𝟙 X) (componentGenericPoint X C) ∉ M.supp) :
    M.IsPullback (𝟙 X) hM M :=
  fun _ _ D hD _ => ⟨D, hD, divisor_isPullback_id D _⟩

/-- In an irreducible space, every point lies in every irreducible component. -/
public theorem mem_irreducibleComponent_of_irreducibleSpace {T : Type*} [TopologicalSpace T]
    [IrreducibleSpace T] (W : irreducibleComponents T) (t : T) : t ∈ W.1 := by
  rw [W.2.eq_of_le (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ T) (Set.subset_univ _)]
  trivial

/-- Pull-back of `ℚ`-divisors along a dominant composite `q ≫ p` from an irreducible scheme to
an integral one is the composite of the pull-backs. -/
public theorem covering_trick_comp
    {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [IrreducibleSpace Z] [IsLocallyNoetherian Z] [IsNormal Z]
    (p : Y ⟶ X) (q : Z ⟶ Y) [IsDominant (q ≫ p)]
    {M : QDivisor X} {MY : QDivisor Y} {MZ : QDivisor Z}
    {hM : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Y, p (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ M.supp}
    {hMY : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Z, q (componentGenericPoint Z C) ∉ MY.supp}
    (h₁ : M.IsPullback p hM MY) (h₂ : MY.IsPullback q hMY MZ) :
    ∃ hM' : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Z, (q ≫ p) (componentGenericPoint Z C) ∉ M.supp,
      M.IsPullback (q ≫ p) hM' MZ := by
  refine ⟨map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ M,
    fun m hm D hD hDc => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨D', hD', hpb⟩ := h₁ m hm D hD hDc
  obtain ⟨D'', hD'', hpb'⟩ := h₂ m hm D' hD' (hpb.isCartier hDc)
  exact ⟨D'', hD'', MMP.ProgramBaseChange.divisor_isPullback_comp rfl hpb hpb' _⟩

/-- **Numerical equivalence pulls back.** If `D₁ ≡ D₂` on `W` and `u : V ⟶ W` is a morphism of
normal varieties over `k`, then `u^*D₁ ≡ u^*D₂`: on a curve `C ⊆ V` both sides vanish when
`u(C)` is a point, and are `deg(C → u(C))` times `(D₁ · u(C)) = (D₂ · u(C))` otherwise. -/
public theorem numericallyEquivalent_of_isPullback (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {V W : Scheme.{u}} (sV : V ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sW : W ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sV] [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sW]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] (u : V ⟶ W) (hu : u ≫ sW = sV)
    {D₁ D₂ : QDivisor W} (h : D₁.NumericallyEquivalent k sW D₂)
    {hD₁ : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D₁.supp}
    {hD₂ : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D₂.supp}
    {D₁' D₂' : QDivisor V} (h₁ : D₁.IsPullback u hD₁ D₁') (h₂ : D₂.IsPullback u hD₂ D₂') :
    D₁'.NumericallyEquivalent k sV D₂' := by
  obtain ⟨q₁, q₂, hC⟩ := h
  refine ⟨h₁.isQCartier q₁, h₂.isQCartier q₂, fun C i _ hCi _ hC1 => ?_⟩
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (i ≫ sV) := AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety.mk
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve k (i ≫ sV) := ⟨hC1⟩
  by_cases hpt : ∃ w : W, Set.range (i ≫ u) = {w}
  · rw [intersectionNumber_pullback_eq_zero k sV sW u hu i q₁ h₁ hpt,
      intersectionNumber_pullback_eq_zero k sV sW u hu i q₂ h₂ hpt]
  · haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsCurve k ((i ≫ u) ≫ sW) := by
      rw [Category.assoc, hu]; infer_instance
    haveI : IsProper ((i ≫ u) ≫ sW) := by rw [Category.assoc, hu]; infer_instance
    have hcurve := isCurve_imageι_comp sW (i ≫ u) hpt
    rw [intersectionNumber_pullback_eq_degreeOver_mul k sV sW u hu i q₁ h₁ hcurve,
      intersectionNumber_pullback_eq_degreeOver_mul k sV sW u hu i q₂ h₂ hcurve]
    haveI : IsProper (i ≫ u) := IsProper.of_comp (i ≫ u) sW
    haveI : IsProper ((i ≫ u).imageι ≫ sW) := isProper_imageι_comp (i ≫ u) sW
    haveI : IsIntegral (i ≫ u).image := hcurve.toIsIntegral
    rw [hC _ (i ≫ u).imageι hcurve.topologicalKrullDim_eq_one]

/-- Numerical equivalence is compatible with adding a `ℚ`-Cartier `ℚ`-divisor. -/
public theorem numericallyEquivalent_add_right (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [QuasiCompact sX] [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    {D₁ D₂ : QDivisor X} (h : D₁.NumericallyEquivalent k sX D₂) {E : QDivisor X}
    (hE : E.IsQCartier) : (D₁ + E).NumericallyEquivalent k sX (D₂ + E) := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h⟩ := h
  refine ⟨h₁.add hE, h₂.add hE, fun C i _ _ _ hC => ?_⟩
  rw [QDivisor.intersectionNumber_add' k sX i hC.le D₁ E h₁ hE,
    QDivisor.intersectionNumber_add' k sX i hC.le D₂ E h₂ hE, h C i hC]

/-- **Additivity of the pull-back of `ℚ`-Cartier `ℚ`-divisors** along a dominant morphism from an
irreducible scheme: `u^*(D + E) = u^*D + u^*E`. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_add {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] [CompactSpace V]
    (u : V ⟶ W) [IsDominant u] {D E : QDivisor W} (hDq : D.IsQCartier) (hEq : E.IsQCartier)
    {hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D.supp}
    {hE : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ E.supp}
    (hDE : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ (D + E).supp)
    {D' E' : QDivisor V} (h₁ : D.IsPullback u hD D') (h₂ : E.IsPullback u hE E') :
    (D + E).IsPullback u hDE (D' + E') := by
  have hgen : ∀ G : Divisor W, ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V,
      u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ G.supp :=
    fun G => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u G
  obtain ⟨D₀, D₀', hD₀c, hD₀B, hD₀, hD₀', hp₀⟩ := h₁.exists_cartierIndex hDq
  obtain ⟨E₀, E₀', hE₀c, hE₀B, hE₀, hE₀', hq₀⟩ := h₂.exists_cartierIndex hEq
  set a : ℕ := D.cartierIndex hDq
  set b : ℕ := E.cartierIndex hEq
  have ha : 0 < a := QDivisor.cartierIndex_pos hDq
  have hb : 0 < b := QDivisor.cartierIndex_pos hEq
  intro m hm G hG hGc
  obtain ⟨G', hG'⟩ := hGc.exists_isPullback (hgen G)
  refine ⟨G', ?_, hG'⟩
  have key : ((a * b : ℕ) : ℤ) • G = (m : ℤ) • ((b : ℤ) • D₀ + (a : ℤ) • E₀) := by
    apply Divisor.toQDivisor_injective
    rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, hG, hD₀, hE₀, smul_smul, smul_add,
      smul_smul, smul_smul, smul_add, smul_smul, smul_smul]
    congr 2 <;> push_cast <;> ring
  have h1 := hG'.zsmul hGc ((a * b : ℕ) : ℤ) (hgen _)
  have h2 := ((((hp₀.zsmul hD₀c (b : ℤ) (hgen _)).add (hD₀c.zsmul _) (hE₀c.zsmul _) (hgen _)
    (hq₀.zsmul hE₀c (a : ℤ) (hgen _))).zsmul ((hD₀c.zsmul _).add (hE₀c.zsmul _)) (m : ℤ)
    (hgen _)).of_eq key.symm (hB₂ := hgen _))
  have h3 := congrArg Divisor.toQDivisor (h1.eq (hGc.zsmul _) h2)
  rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, hD₀', hE₀'] at h3
  refine Finsupp.ext fun P => ?_
  have h4 := congrArg (fun F : QDivisor V => F P) h3
  simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, zsmul_eq_mul] at h4 ⊢
  have hab : ((a * b : ℕ) : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by positivity
  have hab' : (((a * b : ℕ) : ℤ) : ℚ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hab
  apply mul_left_cancel₀ hab'
  rw [h4]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- The pull-back predicate for `ℚ`-divisors transported along equalities of the divisors. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_congr {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian V]
    [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] {u : V ⟶ W} {D D' : QDivisor W}
    {E E' : QDivisor V} {hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D.supp}
    (hD' : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D'.supp)
    (h : D.IsPullback u hD E) (h₁ : D = D') (h₂ : E = E') : D'.IsPullback u hD' E' := by
  subst h₁ h₂
  exact h

/-- `G` partitions the components of `Δ` with coefficient `a` into groups of pairwise disjoint
components, all groups non-empty; when `Δ` is snc, the sum of the components in one group is a
smooth reduced divisor. -/
@[expose] public def IsLevelPartition {X : Scheme.{u}} (Δ : QDivisor X) (a : ℚ) {s : ℕ}
    (G : Fin s → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) : Prop :=
  (∀ P, Δ.coeff P = a ↔ ∃ i, P ∈ G i) ∧ (∀ i j P, P ∈ G i → P ∈ G j → i = j) ∧
    (∀ i, ∀ P ∈ G i, ∀ Q ∈ G i, P ≠ Q → Disjoint P.support Q.support) ∧ ∀ i, (G i).Nonempty

/-- The groups of a level partition at a non-zero level consist of components of `Δ`. -/
public theorem IsLevelPartition.mem_support {X : Scheme.{u}} {Δ : QDivisor X} {a : ℚ} {s : ℕ}
    {G : Fin s → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)} (hG : IsLevelPartition Δ a G) (ha : a ≠ 0)
    {i : Fin s} {P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X} (hP : P ∈ G i) : P ∈ Δ.support :=
  Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr fun h0 => ha (((hG.1 P).mpr ⟨i, hP⟩).symm.trans h0)

/-- The reduced divisor underlying an snc `ℚ`-divisor is snc. -/
public theorem isSNC_sum_single_support {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Y} {Δ : QDivisor X}
    (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs.IsSNC f (∑ P ∈ Δ.support, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X) :=
  hΔ.of_support_subset fun Q hQ => by
    classical
    obtain ⟨P, hP, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp (Finsupp.support_finset_sum hQ)
    rw [Finsupp.support_single_ne_zero _ one_ne_zero, Finset.mem_singleton] at hQP
    exact hQP ▸ hP

/-- A `ℚ`-divisor pulls back to `D'` as soon as one positive multiple `n D` is a Cartier divisor
pulling back to `n D'`, along a dominant morphism from an irreducible scheme to a scheme all of
whose divisors are Cartier. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_of_nsmul {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] [CompactSpace V]
    (u : V ⟶ W) [IsDominant u] (hcart : ∀ G : Divisor W, G.IsCartier) {D : QDivisor W}
    {D' : QDivisor V} {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) {D₀ : Divisor W} {D₀' : Divisor V}
    (hD₀ : Divisor.toQDivisor D₀ = (n : ℤ) • D) (hD₀' : Divisor.toQDivisor D₀' = (n : ℤ) • D')
    {hB : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D₀.supp}
    (hp : D₀.IsPullback u hB D₀')
    (hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D.supp) :
    D.IsPullback u hD D' := by
  have hgen : ∀ G : Divisor W, ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V,
      u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ G.supp :=
    fun G => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u G
  intro m hm G hG _
  obtain ⟨G', hG'⟩ := (hcart G).exists_isPullback (hgen G)
  refine ⟨G', ?_, hG'⟩
  have key : (n : ℤ) • G = (m : ℤ) • D₀ := by
    apply Divisor.toQDivisor_injective
    rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, hG, hD₀, smul_smul, smul_smul, mul_comm]
  have h1 := hG'.zsmul (hcart G) (n : ℤ) (hgen _)
  have h2 := (hp.zsmul (hcart D₀) (m : ℤ) (hgen _)).of_eq key.symm (hB₂ := hgen _)
  have h3 := congrArg Divisor.toQDivisor (h1.eq (hcart _) h2)
  rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, hD₀', smul_smul] at h3
  refine Finsupp.ext fun P => ?_
  have h4 := congrArg (fun F : QDivisor V => F P) h3
  simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, zsmul_eq_mul] at h4 ⊢
  have hn' : ((n : ℤ) : ℚ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hn.ne'
  apply mul_left_cancel₀ hn'
  rw [h4]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- `num(c) D = den(c) (c D)` for a divisor `D` and `c ∈ ℚ`. -/
public theorem toQDivisor_num_smul {X : Scheme.{u}} (c : ℚ) (D : Divisor X) :
    Divisor.toQDivisor (c.num • D) = (c.den : ℤ) • (c • Divisor.toQDivisor D) := by
  rw [map_zsmul]
  refine Finsupp.ext fun Q => ?_
  simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, zsmul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
  have := Rat.mul_den_eq_num c
  push_cast
  linear_combination (-(Divisor.toQDivisor D Q)) * this

/-- `f^*(c P) = c f^*P` for a prime divisor `P` and `c ∈ ℚ`. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_smul_single {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] [CompactSpace V]
    (u : V ⟶ W) [IsDominant u] (hcart : ∀ G : Divisor W, G.IsCartier)
    (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W) {E : Divisor V}
    {hB : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V,
      u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))}
    (h : Divisor.IsPullback u (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) hB E) (c : ℚ)
    (hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V,
      u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ (c • Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single P 1)).supp) :
    (c • Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))).IsPullback u hD
      (c • Divisor.toQDivisor E) := by
  have hgen : ∀ G : Divisor W, ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V,
      u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ G.supp :=
    fun G => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u G
  refine qDivisor_isPullback_of_nsmul u hcart c.den_pos (D₀ := c.num • Finsupp.single P 1)
    (D₀' := c.num • E) (toQDivisor_num_smul c _) (toQDivisor_num_smul c E)
    (h.zsmul (hcart _) c.num (hgen _)) hD

/-- `f^*(∑ c_P P) = ∑ c_P f^*P` over a finite set of prime divisors. -/
public theorem qDivisor_isPullback_sum_smul {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] [CompactSpace V]
    (u : V ⟶ W) [IsDominant u] (hcart : ∀ G : Divisor W, G.IsCartier)
    (hq : ∀ G : QDivisor W, G.IsQCartier) (S : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W))
    (c : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W → ℚ) (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W → Divisor V)
    (h : ∀ P ∈ S, Divisor.IsPullback u (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _) (E P))
    (hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉
      (∑ P ∈ S, c P • Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))).supp) :
    (∑ P ∈ S, c P • Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))).IsPullback u hD
      (∑ P ∈ S, c P • Divisor.toQDivisor (E P)) := by
  classical
  induction S using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
    simp only [Finset.sum_empty]
    intro m hm G hG hGc
    refine ⟨0, by simp, ?_⟩
    have hG0 : G = 0 := Divisor.toQDivisor_injective (by rw [hG]; simp)
    subst hG0
    exact Divisor.isPullback_zero _
  | insert P S hPS ih =>
    simp only [Finset.sum_insert hPS]
    exact qDivisor_isPullback_add u (hq _) (hq _)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _)
      (qDivisor_isPullback_smul_single u hcart P (h P (Finset.mem_insert_self P S)) (c P)
        (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _))
      (ih (fun Q hQ => h Q (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hQ))
        (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _))

/-- The pull-back predicate for divisors transported along an equality of pull-backs. -/
public theorem divisor_isPullback_congr {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian V]
    [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W] {u : V ⟶ W} {D : Divisor W}
    {E E' : Divisor V} {hD : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents V, u (componentGenericPoint V Z) ∉ D.supp}
    (h : D.IsPullback u hD E) (h₂ : E = E') : D.IsPullback u hD E' := by
  subst h₂
  exact h

/-- **`H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` is a retract of `H^i(Y, 𝒪(-π^*B))`** for a finite surjective morphism
`π : Y ⟶ X` of normal varieties over `k` and a Cartier divisor `B` on `X`. -/
public theorem nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_divisorialSheaf_neg (k : Type u) [Field k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (π : Y ⟶ X)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k f] [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (π ≫ f)]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    [CompactSpace Y] [IsFinite π] [Surjective π] {B : Divisor X} (hBc : B.IsCartier)
    {hB : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents Y, π (componentGenericPoint Y Z) ∉ B.supp}
    {B' : Divisor Y} (h : B.IsPullback π hB B') (i : ℕ) :
    Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
      (cohomologyOverField k (π ≫ f) (-B').divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  haveI : IsIntegral Y := (inferInstance : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (π ≫ f)).toIsIntegral
  have hBn : ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents Y, π (componentGenericPoint Y Z) ∉ ((-1 : ℤ) • B).supp :=
    fun Z hZ => hB Z (by
      rwa [← Divisor.supp_toQDivisor, map_zsmul, QDivisor.supp_zsmul (by norm_num),
        Divisor.supp_toQDivisor] at hZ)
  have hneg : (-B).IsPullback π (fun Z => by rw [← neg_one_zsmul]; exact hBn Z) (-B') :=
    divisor_isPullback_congr ((h.zsmul hBc (-1) hBn).of_eq (neg_one_zsmul B))
      (neg_one_zsmul B')
  obtain ⟨R⟩ := MMP.Mori.nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_pullback_of_isFinite k f (π ≫ f)
    π rfl ((-B).divisorialSheaf) i
  exact ⟨R.trans ((cohomologyOverFieldFunctor k (π ≫ f) i).mapIso
    (hneg.divisorialSheafIso (hBc := hBc.neg)).symm).retract⟩

/-- A `ℚ`-divisor is the sum of its coefficients times its prime components. -/
public theorem qDivisor_eq_sum_smul_single {X : Scheme.{u}} (Δ : QDivisor X) :
    Δ = ∑ P ∈ Δ.support, Δ P • Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) := by
  classical
  refine Finsupp.ext fun Q => ?_
  rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]
  change Δ Q = ∑ P ∈ Δ.support, Δ P * ((Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) Q : ℤ) : ℚ)
  by_cases hQ : Q ∈ Δ.support
  · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single Q (fun P _ hPQ => by simp [Finsupp.single_apply, hPQ])
      (fun h => absurd hQ h)]
    simp
  · rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hQ]
    refine (Finset.sum_eq_zero fun P hP => ?_).symm
    have : P ≠ Q := fun h => hQ (h ▸ hP)
    simp [Finsupp.single_apply, this]

/-- The value of `∑ c_P E_P` at a component of one `E_{P₀}`, the `E_P` being reduced with
pairwise disjoint supports. -/
public theorem sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply {Y : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type*}
    (S : Finset ι) (c : ι → ℚ) (E : ι → Divisor Y) (hred : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, E P Q = 0 ∨ E P Q = 1)
    (hdisj : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → Disjoint (E P).support (E P').support)
    {P₀ : ι} (hP₀ : P₀ ∈ S) {Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (hQ : Q ∈ (E P₀).support) :
    (∑ P ∈ S, c P • Divisor.toQDivisor (E P)) Q = c P₀ := by
  classical
  rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]
  change ∑ P ∈ S, c P * ((E P Q : ℤ) : ℚ) = c P₀
  have h1 : E P₀ Q = 1 := (hred P₀ hP₀ Q).resolve_left (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ)
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_single P₀ (fun P hP hne => by
      rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp (Finset.disjoint_right.mp (hdisj P hP P₀ hP₀ hne) hQ)]
      simp) (fun h => absurd hP₀ h), h1]
  simp

/-- `∑ c_P E_P` vanishes away from the supports of the `E_P`. -/
public theorem sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply_of_notMem {Y : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type*}
    (S : Finset ι) (c : ι → ℚ) (E : ι → Divisor Y) {Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y}
    (hQ : ∀ P ∈ S, Q ∉ (E P).support) :
    (∑ P ∈ S, c P • Divisor.toQDivisor (E P)) Q = 0 := by
  rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun P hP => ?_
  change c P * ((E P Q : ℤ) : ℚ) = 0
  rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp (hQ P hP)]
  simp

/-- The value of `∑ E_P` at a component of one `E_{P₀}`. -/
public theorem sum_apply_of_mem_support {Y : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type*}
    (S : Finset ι) (E : ι → Divisor Y) (hred : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, E P Q = 0 ∨ E P Q = 1)
    (hdisj : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → Disjoint (E P).support (E P').support)
    {P₀ : ι} (hP₀ : P₀ ∈ S) {Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (hQ : Q ∈ (E P₀).support) :
    (∑ P ∈ S, E P) Q = 1 := by
  classical
  rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply, Finset.sum_eq_single P₀ (fun P hP hne =>
      Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp (Finset.disjoint_right.mp (hdisj P hP P₀ hP₀ hne) hQ))
      (fun h => absurd hP₀ h)]
  exact (hred P₀ hP₀ Q).resolve_left (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ)

/-- The quotient of a ring by the unit ideal has length `0`. -/
public theorem length_quotient_top_toNat (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    ((Module.length R (R ⧸ (⊤ : Ideal R))).toNat : ℤ) = 0 := by
  rw [length_quotient_top]; rfl

open Classical in
/-- The colength of the ideal of a prime divisor `P` at the generic point of a prime divisor `Q`
is `1` if `Q = P` and `0` otherwise. -/
public theorem length_stalk_idealSheaf {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (P Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (hP : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor P.idealSheaf) :
    ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
        IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) =
      if Q = P then 1 else 0 := by
  split_ifs with h
  · subst h
    rw [MMP.Threefold.Resolution.stalk_idealSheaf_genericPoint_eq_maximalIdeal Q hP]
    have := Q.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
    rw [Module.length_eq_one_iff.mpr ?_]
    · rfl
    exact isSimpleModule_iff_isCoatom.mpr (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).out
  · rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.stalkIdeal_eq_stalk,
      P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal_eq_top_of_notMem_support
      fun hmem => h (eq_of_genericPoint_mem_primeDivisor_support hmem)]
    exact length_quotient_top_toNat _

/-- On a locally Noetherian normal scheme, the order of vanishing along a prime divisor `Q` of a
nonzero element `t` of `𝒪_{X,Q}` is `length(𝒪_{X,Q}/(t))`. -/
public theorem valuation_toComponent_eq_length {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) {t : Q.localRing} (ht : t ≠ 0) :
    Q.valuation (Q.toComponent.hom t) =
      WithZero.exp ((Module.length Q.localRing (Q.localRing ⧸ Ideal.span {t})).toNat : ℤ) := by
  let := Q.toComponent.hom.toAlgebra
  have := isFractionRing_stalkToRationalFunctions Q.genericPoint_mem_component
  have : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 Q.localRing := krullDimLE_of_coheight_le Q.coheight_genericPoint.le
  have := Q.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  change Ring.ordFrac Q.localRing (IsLocalization.algEquiv (nonZeroDivisors Q.localRing) _
    (FractionRing Q.localRing) (algebraMap Q.localRing _ t)) = _
  rw [AlgEquiv.commutes, Ring.ordFrac_eq_ord _ ht]
  have hnz : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Q.localRing := mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero ht
  rw [Ring.ordMonoidWithZeroHom_eq_coe _ hnz (n := (Ring.ord Q.localRing t).toNat)
    (ENat.coe_toNat (Ring.ord_ne_top hnz)).symm]
  rfl

/-- The ideal of every prime divisor is locally generated by one regular function which is a
local equation of it. -/
@[expose] public def HasPrincipalLocalEquations (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [IsNormal Y] : Prop :=
  ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y) (x : Y), ∃ U : Y.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : Y.Opens) ∧
    ∃ (g : Γ(Y, U)) (φ : (RationalFunctions Y)ˣ),
      (∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents Y) (hZ : componentGenericPoint Y Z ∈ (U : Y.Opens)),
        (φ : RationalFunctions Y) Z = Y.presheaf.germ U _ hZ g) ∧
      Divisor.IsLocalEquation (Finsupp.single P 1) U φ ∧
      P.idealSheaf.ideal U = Ideal.span {g}

/-- **The inverse image of a prime divisor is its pull-back.** If the ideal of every prime
divisor of `X` is locally principal, generated by a local equation, then for `g : Y ⟶ X` and a
prime divisor `P` of `X`, `g^*P` has coefficient `length(𝒪_{Y,Q}/(g⁻¹ I_P)_Q)` at `Q`. -/
public theorem isPullback_single_of_comap {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y]
    (hsm : HasPrincipalLocalEquations X) (g : Y ⟶ X) (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)
    (hgen : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Y,
      g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)))
    (E : Divisor Y)
    (hE : ∀ Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y, E Q = ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
        IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ)) :
    Divisor.IsPullback g (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) hgen E := by
  haveI : IsNoetherian Y := ⟨⟩
  refine Divisor.IsPullback.of_forall_exists fun Q => ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hyU, s, φ, hgerm, hloc, hideal⟩ := hsm P (g Q.genericPoint)
  have hQU : Q.genericPoint ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens) := hyU
  have hE' : (Q.support ∩ g ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens)).Nonempty := (Q.genericPoint_mem_iff _).mp hQU
  refine ⟨U, φ, hloc, hE', ?_⟩
  have hst : ∀ (x : X) (hx : x ∈ (U : X.Opens)),
      P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal x = Ideal.span {(X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom s} := by
    intro x hx
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.stalkIdeal_eq_stalk,
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ x U hx, hideal, Ideal.map_span,
      Set.image_singleton]
  set t : Q.localRing := (g.stalkMap Q.genericPoint).hom ((X.presheaf.germ U _ hyU).hom s)
    with ht
  have hcomap : IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) Q.genericPoint = Ideal.span {t} := by
    rw [MMP.stalk_comap_eq_span P.idealSheaf g U hideal hQU,
      ht, Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply]
  change E Q = _
  rw [hE Q, hcomap]
  change (((Module.length Q.localRing (Q.localRing ⧸ Ideal.span {t})).toNat : ℕ) : ℤ) = _
  set z := componentGenericPoint Y Q.component with hz
  have hZ : g z ∈ (U : X.Opens) := Q.map_componentGenericPoint_mem g hE'
  have hzP : g z ∉ P.support := by
    intro hmem
    refine hgen Q.component ?_
    rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.mem_supp_iff]
    exact ⟨P, by simp [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_apply], hmem⟩
  have hunit : IsUnit ((X.presheaf.germ U (g z) hZ).hom s) := by
    rw [← Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top, ← hst _ hZ]
    exact P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal_eq_top_of_notMem_support hzP
  set W := MMP.Mori.pointComponent (g z)
  have hW : g z ∈ W.1 := MMP.Mori.mem_pointComponent _
  have hWU : componentGenericPoint X W ∈ (U : X.Opens) :=
    ((isGenericPoint_componentGenericPoint X W).specializes hW).mem_open U.1.isOpen hZ
  have ha : (MMP.Mori.stalkToRationalFunctions X hW).hom hunit.unit =
      (φ : RationalFunctions X) W := by
    rw [hgerm W hWU, IsUnit.unit_spec]
    exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply ..
  rw [MMP.Mori.pullbackComponent_eq _ hloc _ hW hunit.unit ha]
  set v := Units.map (g.stalkMap z).hom.toMonoidHom hunit.unit
  have hu : (v : Y.presheaf.stalk z) = Q.toComponent.hom t := by
    change (g.stalkMap z).hom ((X.presheaf.germ U (g z) hZ).hom s) =
      (Y.presheaf.stalkSpecializes _).hom
        ((g.stalkMap Q.genericPoint).hom ((X.presheaf.germ U _ hyU).hom s))
    rw [Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply, Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply]
    exact (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply ..).symm
  have ht0 : t ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have : (v : Y.presheaf.stalk z) = 0 := by rw [hu, h0, map_zero]
    exact v.ne_zero this
  have h1 := Q.valuation_eq_exp_ordUnit v
  rw [hu, valuation_toComponent_eq_length Q ht0] at h1
  rw [← WithZero.exp_injective h1]

/-- The stalk of an effective Cartier divisor is generated by one non-zero-divisor. -/
public theorem exists_stalk_eq_span_mem_nonZeroDivisors {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) (y : Y) :
    ∃ t ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Y.presheaf.stalk y), IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {t} := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, s, hs, hspan⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor I hI y
  refine ⟨_, Stacks.Divisors.germ_mem_nonZeroDivisors hW hs _ hxW, ?_⟩
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I _ ⟨W, hW⟩ hxW, hspan, Ideal.map_span,
    Set.image_singleton]

/-- At each point of a smooth effective Cartier divisor on a smooth scheme over a field, its
ideal is generated by one member of a regular system of parameters. -/
public theorem exists_regularParameter_of_smooth {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Smooth sY] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I) (hZ : Smooth (I.subschemeι ≫ sY)) :
    ∀ y ∈ I.support, ∃ (m : ℕ) (w : Fin m → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin m),
      MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {w j} := by
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ : y ∈ Set.range I.subschemeι := by
    rwa [I.range_subschemeι]
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hst⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_mem_nonZeroDivisors I hI (I.subschemeι z)
  have hR := isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field sY (I.subschemeι z)
  haveI : IsNoetherianRing (Y.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι z)) := hR.toIsNoetherian
  have htm : t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι z)) := by
    by_contra h
    have hu : IsUnit t := by simpa using h
    have htop : IdealSheafData.stalk I (I.subschemeι z) = ⊤ := by
      rwa [hst, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top]
    exact (IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I _).mp htop hy
  have hdim := ringKrullDim_quotient_span_singleton_succ_eq_ringKrullDim_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors
    ht htm
  haveI := hZ
  haveI := isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_smooth_over_field (I.subschemeι ≫ sY) z
  have hreg : IsRegularLocalRing (Y.presheaf.stalk (I.subschemeι z) ⧸ Ideal.span {t}) := by
    rw [← hst]
    exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv (IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotEquiv I z).symm
  have hr : Set.range ![t] = {t} := by ext; simp [eq_comm]
  obtain ⟨m, t', hw⟩ := (MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_add_eq_iff
    ![t]).mp ⟨by rw [hr]; exact hreg, by rw [hr]; exact_mod_cast hdim⟩
  exact ⟨1 + m, Fin.append ![t] t', Fin.castAdd m 0, hw, by simp [hst]⟩

/-- For a divisor `I` cut out by regular parameters, a prime divisor whose generic point lies in
the support of `I` has support the connected component of `I.support` through that point. -/
public theorem support_eq_connectedComponentIn {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hI : ∀ y ∈ I.support, ∃ (m : ℕ) (w : Fin m → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin m),
      MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {w j})
    (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y) (hQ : Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support) :
    Q.support = connectedComponentIn (I.support : Set Y) Q.genericPoint := by
  obtain ⟨Q', hQ'⟩ := MMP.Mori.exists_primeDivisor_support_eq_connectedComponentIn I hI hQ
  obtain rfl := eq_of_genericPoint_mem_primeDivisor_support
    (show Q.genericPoint ∈ Q'.support from hQ' ▸ mem_connectedComponentIn hQ)
  exact hQ'

/-- Every point of a divisor cut out by regular parameters lies on a prime divisor whose generic
point lies in the divisor. -/
public theorem exists_primeDivisor_of_regularParameter {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hI : ∀ y ∈ I.support, ∃ (m : ℕ) (w : Fin m → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin m),
      MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {w j})
    {y : Y} (hy : y ∈ I.support) :
    ∃ Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y, Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support ∧ y ∈ Q.support := by
  obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ := MMP.Mori.exists_primeDivisor_support_eq_connectedComponentIn I hI hy
  refine ⟨Q, connectedComponentIn_subset _ y ?_, hQ ▸ mem_connectedComponentIn hy⟩
  rw [← hQ]
  exact primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support Q

/-- Two distinct prime divisors whose generic points lie in the support of a divisor cut out by
regular parameters are disjoint. -/
public theorem disjoint_support_of_regularParameter {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace Y] (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hI : ∀ y ∈ I.support, ∃ (m : ℕ) (w : Fin m → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin m),
      MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I y = Ideal.span {w j})
    {Q Q' : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (hQ : Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support)
    (hQ' : Q'.genericPoint ∈ I.support) (hne : Q ≠ Q') : Disjoint Q.support Q'.support := by
  refine Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun y hy hy' => hne (eq_of_genericPoint_mem_primeDivisor_support ?_)
  rw [support_eq_connectedComponentIn I hI Q hQ] at hy
  rw [support_eq_connectedComponentIn I hI Q' hQ'] at hy'
  rw [support_eq_connectedComponentIn I hI Q' hQ', connectedComponentIn_eq hy',
    ← connectedComponentIn_eq hy]
  exact mem_connectedComponentIn hQ

/-- A prime divisor whose generic point lies in a closed subscheme lies in it. -/
public theorem support_subset_of_genericPoint_mem {Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    {Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y} (h : Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support) :
    Q.support ⊆ (I.support : Set Y) := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]
  exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr h) I.support.isClosed

/-- For an effective Cartier divisor `I` on a locally Noetherian normal scheme, the colength of
`I` at the generic point of a prime divisor `Q` is non-zero exactly when that generic point lies
in the support of `I`. -/
public theorem length_stalk_ne_zero_iff {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    (I : Y.IdealSheafData) (hI : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I)
    (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y) :
    (Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint)).toNat ≠ 0 ↔
      Q.genericPoint ∈ I.support := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hnot
    apply h
    rw [(IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I _).mpr hnot]
    exact_mod_cast length_quotient_top_toNat _
  · intro hmem
    obtain ⟨t, ht, hst⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_mem_nonZeroDivisors I hI Q.genericPoint
    have : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 Q.localRing := krullDimLE_of_coheight_le Q.coheight_genericPoint.le
    have hfin : IsFiniteLength (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ Ideal.span {t}) :=
      isFiniteLength_quotient_span_singleton _ ht
    have hne : IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint ≠ ⊤ :=
      fun h => ((IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I _).mp h) hmem
    rw [hst] at hne ⊢
    have : Nontrivial (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ Ideal.span {t}) :=
      Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
    rw [Ne, ENat.toNat_eq_zero, not_or]
    exact ⟨fun h0 => (not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial.mpr inferInstance)
      (Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mp h0), Module.length_ne_top_iff.mpr hfin⟩

/-- Tensor powers of isomorphic modules are isomorphic. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def tensorPowCongr {Y : Scheme.{u}} {A B : Y.Modules} (e : A ≅ B) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, MMP.Intersection.Scheme.Modules.tensorPow A n ≅
      MMP.Intersection.Scheme.Modules.tensorPow B n
  | 0 => Iso.refl _
  | n + 1 => MonoidalCategory.tensorIso (tensorPowCongr e n) e

/-- `𝒪_Y(D)^{⊗ n} ≅ 𝒪_Y(n D)` for a Cartier divisor `D`. -/
public theorem nonempty_tensorPow_divisorialSheaf_iso {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y]
    [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y] (D : Divisor Y) (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor Y, D.IsCartier) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, Nonempty (MMP.Intersection.Scheme.Modules.tensorPow D.divisorialSheaf n ≅
      ((n : ℤ) • D).divisorialSheaf)
  | 0 => ⟨(Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso).symm ≪≫ eqToIso (by rw [Nat.cast_zero, zero_smul])⟩
  | n + 1 => by
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_tensorPow_divisorialSheaf_iso D hcart n
    exact ⟨MonoidalCategory.tensorIso e (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
      (hcart _).divisorialSheafTensorIso (hcart D) ≪≫
      eqToIso (by congr 1; push_cast; rw [add_smul, one_smul])⟩

/-- `g^*(∑_{P ∈ T} P) = ∑_{P ∈ T} g^*P` along a dominant morphism from an irreducible scheme to a
scheme all of whose divisors are Cartier. -/
public theorem divisor_isPullback_sum_single {V W : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace V]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian V] [IsNormal V] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] [IsNormal W]
    (u : V ⟶ W) [IsDominant u] (hcart : ∀ G : Divisor W, G.IsCartier)
    (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W)) (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor W → Divisor V)
    (h : ∀ P ∈ T, Divisor.IsPullback u (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _) (E P)) :
    Divisor.IsPullback u (∑ P ∈ T, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' u _)
      (∑ P ∈ T, E P) := by
  classical
  induction T using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => exact Divisor.isPullback_zero _
  | insert P T hPT ih =>
    simp only [Finset.sum_insert hPT]
    exact Divisor.IsPullback.add (hcart _) (hcart _) _ (h P (Finset.mem_insert_self P T))
      (ih fun Q hQ => h Q (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hQ))

/-- The coefficients of the reduced sum of a finite set of prime divisors. -/
public theorem sum_single_one_apply {X : Scheme.{u}} [DecidableEq (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)]
    (A : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    (∑ P ∈ A, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X) Q = if Q ∈ A then 1 else 0 := by
  simp [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]

/-- The reduced sum of a finite set of prime divisors has coefficient `1` along its components. -/
public theorem coeff_sum_single_one_of_mem_support {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (A : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) :
    ∀ Q ∈ (∑ P ∈ A, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X).support,
      (∑ P ∈ A, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X).coeff Q = 1 := by
  classical
  intro Q hQ
  have h := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ
  change (∑ P ∈ A, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X) Q = 1
  rw [sum_single_one_apply] at h ⊢
  split_ifs at h ⊢ <;> simp_all

/-- Each member of a finite set of prime divisors is a component of their reduced sum. -/
public theorem mem_support_sum_single_one {X : Scheme.{u}} {A : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)}
    {P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X} (hP : P ∈ A) :
    P ∈ (∑ P ∈ A, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X).support := by
  classical
  exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr (by rw [sum_single_one_apply, if_pos hP]; exact one_ne_zero)

/-- A finite cover of a projective variety by a variety is a projective variety. -/
public theorem isProjectiveVariety_comp_of_isFinite {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [hpX : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k f] (g : Y ⟶ X)
    [IsFinite g] (hvar : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (g ≫ f)) :
    MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (g ≫ f) := by
  obtain ⟨L, _, hL⟩ := exists_isAmple_of_isProjectiveMorphism f
    (Stacks.Ample.unitModule (Spec (.of k))) (Stacks.Ample.isAmple_unitModule_of_isAffine _)
    hpX.isProjective
  exact (AlgebraicGeometry.isProjectiveVariety_iff k (g ≫ f)).mpr
    ⟨hvar, (isProjectiveMorphism_of_isFinite g L hL).comp hpX.isProjective⟩

/-- **The Bloch–Gieseker cover, for divisors.** Let `X` be a smooth projective variety, `S` a
finite set of prime divisors whose sum is snc, `T ⊆ S` and `m > 0`. There are a finite surjective
`g : Y ⟶ X` from a smooth projective variety and a divisor `D` on `Y` such that: each `P ∈ S`
pulls back to a non-zero reduced divisor `E_P = g⁻¹ P`, the `E_P` have pairwise disjoint
supports, two distinct components of `E_P` and `E_{P'}` are disjoint when `P = P'` (`g⁻¹ P` is
smooth) or `P ∩ P' = ∅`, `∑ E_P` is snc, and `∑_{P ∈ T} E_P ∼ m D`. This is
`MMP.Mori.exists_isFinite_surjective_pullback_iso_tensorPow_of_isSNC` for `𝒪(∑_{P ∈ T} P)`,
`m` and the ideal sheaves of the `P ∈ S`, translated to divisors. -/
public theorem exists_bloch_gieseker_cover_divisors
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (S T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) (hTS : T ⊆ S)
    (hS : DivisorWithCoeffs.IsSNC f (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X))
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) :
    ∃ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite g) (_ : Surjective g)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (g ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (g ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian Y) (_ : IsNormal Y) (_ : CompactSpace Y)
      (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → Divisor Y) (D : Divisor Y)
      (hgen : ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (C : irreducibleComponents Y),
        g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))),
      (∀ P ∈ S, Divisor.IsPullback g (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) (hgen P) (E P)) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, E P ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ Q, E P Q = 0 ∨ E P Q = 1) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → Disjoint (E P).support (E P').support) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, (P = P' ∨ Disjoint P.support P'.support) →
        ∀ Q ∈ (E P).support, ∀ Q' ∈ (E P').support, Q ≠ Q' → Disjoint Q.support Q'.support) ∧
      DivisorWithCoeffs.IsSNC (g ≫ f) (∑ P ∈ S, E P) ∧
      Divisor.LinearlyEquivalent (∑ P ∈ T, E P) ((m : ℤ) • D) := by
  classical
  haveI : IsQuasiProjectiveVariety k f := IsProjectiveVariety.isQuasiProjectiveVariety k f
  haveI : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
  haveI : IsSmoothVariety k f := (isSmoothVariety_iff k f).mpr ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  have hsmX : IsSmoothScheme f := (isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance
  obtain ⟨hcart, hloc, -⟩ := MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety k f
  have hECD : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X,
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor P.idealSheaf :=
    MMP.Threefold.Resolution.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_idealSheaf_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  set D₀ : Divisor X := ∑ P ∈ T, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) with hD₀
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      D₀.divisorialSheaf := (hcart D₀).isInvertibleModule_divisorialSheaf
  haveI : ∀ j : S, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (j.1.idealSheaf) := fun j => hECD j.1
  have hDc : ∀ Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X,
      (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X).coeff Q =
        ∑ j : S, ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
          (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
            IdealSheafData.stalk (j.1.idealSheaf) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
    intro Q
    simp_rw [length_stalk_idealSheaf _ Q (hECD _)]
    rw [Finset.sum_coe_sort S (fun P => if Q = P then (1 : ℤ) else 0)]
    change _ = ∑ P ∈ S, if Q = P then (1 : ℤ) else 0
    rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq]
    exact sum_single_one_apply S Q
  obtain ⟨Y, sY, g, hvar, hsmY, hgs, hfin, hsurj, ⟨L', hL', ⟨eL⟩⟩, hcomapC, hsmooth, E, hE,
    hEsnc, hE1⟩ :=
    MMP.Mori.exists_isFinite_surjective_pullback_iso_tensorPow_of_isSNC k f D₀.divisorialSheaf m hm
      (fun j : S => j.1.idealSheaf) (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) hDc hS
      (coeff_sum_single_one_of_mem_support S)
  subst hgs
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (g ≫ f) := hvar
  haveI : Smooth (g ≫ f) := hsmY
  haveI : IsFinite g := hfin
  haveI : Surjective g := hsurj
  haveI : IsSmoothVariety k (g ≫ f) := (isSmoothVariety_iff k _).mpr ⟨hvar, hsmY⟩
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (g ≫ f)
  haveI : IsNormal Y := isNormal_of_smooth_over_field (g ≫ f)
  haveI : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (g ≫ f)
  haveI : IsIntegral Y := hvar.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsNoetherian Y := ⟨⟩
  obtain ⟨hcartY, -, -, -, hinvY, -⟩ :=
    MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety k (g ≫ f)
  have hgen : ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (C : irreducibleComponents Y),
      g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) :=
    fun P => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g _
  -- the colengths `ℓ P Q` of `g⁻¹ P` along the prime divisors `Q` of `Y`
  set ℓ : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y → ℤ := fun P Q =>
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint) (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) with hℓ
  have hEℓ : ∀ Q, E Q = ∑ P ∈ S, ℓ P Q := fun Q => by
    rw [← Finset.sum_coe_sort S]; exact hE Q
  have hE01 : ∀ Q, E Q = 0 ∨ E Q = 1 := fun Q => by
    by_cases hQ : Q ∈ E.support
    · exact Or.inr (hE1 Q hQ)
    · exact Or.inl (Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hQ)
  have hℓ0 : ∀ P Q, 0 ≤ ℓ P Q := fun P Q => Int.natCast_nonneg _
  have hℓle : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, ℓ P Q ≤ E Q := fun P hP Q => by
    rw [hEℓ]; exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun P _ => hℓ0 P Q) hP
  have hℓ01 : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, ℓ P Q = 0 ∨ ℓ P Q = 1 := fun P hP Q => by
    have := hℓle P hP Q; have := hℓ0 P Q; rcases hE01 Q with h | h <;> omega
  have hℓdisj : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → ∀ Q, ℓ P Q = 0 ∨ ℓ P' Q = 0 := by
    intro P hP P' hP' hne Q
    have hsub : ({P, P'} : Finset _) ⊆ S := by
      intro x hx; rw [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hx
      rcases hx with rfl | rfl <;> assumption
    have h2 := Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg hsub (fun P _ _ => hℓ0 P Q)
    rw [Finset.sum_pair hne, ← hEℓ] at h2
    have := hℓ0 P Q; have := hℓ0 P' Q; rcases hE01 Q with h | h <;> omega
  have hℓsupp : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, ℓ P Q ≠ 0 → Q ∈ E.support := fun P hP Q hQ =>
    Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr (by have := hℓle P hP Q; have := hℓ0 P Q; omega)
  let EP : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → Divisor Y := fun P =>
    if hP : P ∈ S then Finsupp.onFinset E.support (fun Q => ℓ P Q) (hℓsupp P hP) else 0
  have hEP : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, EP P Q = ℓ P Q := fun P hP Q => by
    simp only [EP, dif_pos hP, Finsupp.onFinset_apply]
  have hreg : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ y ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support, ∃ (n : ℕ)
      (w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin n), MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧
        IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) y = Ideal.span {w j} :=
    fun P hP => exists_regularParameter_of_smooth (g ≫ f) _ (hcomapC ⟨P, hP⟩)
      (hsmooth ⟨P, hP⟩ ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mp (hS.1 P (mem_support_sum_single_one hP))))
  have hmemsupp : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, Q ∈ (EP P).support ↔
      Q.genericPoint ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support := by
    intro P hP Q
    rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, hEP P hP Q, ← length_stalk_ne_zero_iff _ (hcomapC ⟨P, hP⟩) Q]
    simp only [hℓ, ne_eq, Nat.cast_eq_zero]
  have hsub : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q ∈ (EP P).support, Q.support ⊆ g ⁻¹' P.support :=
    fun P hP Q hQ y hy => by
      have := support_subset_of_genericPoint_mem _ ((hmemsupp P hP Q).mp hQ) hy
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap] at this
  have hsumE : ∑ P ∈ S, EP P = E := Finsupp.ext fun Q => by
    rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply, hEℓ]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun P hP => hEP P hP Q
  have hpb : Divisor.IsPullback g D₀
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g _)
      (∑ P ∈ T, EP P) :=
    divisor_isPullback_sum_single g hcart T EP (fun P hP =>
      isPullback_single_of_comap hloc g P _ (EP P) (fun Q => hEP P (hTS hP) Q))
  obtain ⟨D', ⟨eD'⟩⟩ := hinvY L' hL'
  obtain ⟨eT⟩ := nonempty_tensorPow_divisorialSheaf_iso D' hcartY m
  refine ⟨Y, g, hfin, hsurj, isProjectiveVariety_comp_of_isFinite f g ‹_›, hsmY, inferInstance,
    inferInstance, inferInstance, EP, D',
    hgen, fun P hP => isPullback_single_of_comap hloc g P (hgen P) (EP P) (fun Q => hEP P hP Q),
    fun P hP => ⟨?_, fun Q => by rw [hEP P hP Q]; exact hℓ01 P hP Q⟩, ?_, ?_,
    by rw [hsumE]; exact hEsnc, ?_⟩
  · intro h0
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hsurj.surj P.genericPoint
    obtain ⟨Q, hηQ, -⟩ := exists_primeDivisor_of_regularParameter _ (hreg P hP)
      (show y ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support by
        rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
        change g y ∈ P.support
        rw [show g y = P.genericPoint from hy]
        exact primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support P)
    simpa [h0] using (hmemsupp P hP Q).mpr hηQ
  · intro P hP P' hP' hne
    refine Finset.disjoint_left.mpr fun Q hQ hQ' => ?_
    rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, hEP P hP Q] at hQ
    rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, hEP P' hP' Q] at hQ'
    rcases hℓdisj P hP P' hP' hne Q with h | h
    · exact hQ h
    · exact hQ' h
  · intro P hP P' hP' hPP Q hQ Q' hQ' hne
    rcases hPP with rfl | hdisj
    · exact disjoint_support_of_regularParameter _ (hreg P hP) ((hmemsupp P hP Q).mp hQ)
        ((hmemsupp P hP' Q').mp hQ') hne
    · exact (hdisj.preimage g).mono (hsub P hP Q hQ) (hsub P' hP' Q' hQ')
  · exact MMP.Flips.linearlyEquivalent_of_divisorialSheaf_iso
      (hpb.divisorialSheafIso (hBc := hcart D₀) ≪≫ eL ≪≫ tensorPowCongr eD'.symm m ≪≫ eT)

/-- **The Bloch–Gieseker stage.** With `Δ`, `a` and the partition `G` as in
`exists_cover_clearing_group`, and `D₀` the smooth reduced sum of the first group, the
Bloch–Gieseker cover for `𝒪(D₀)`, the exponent `m` (the denominator of `a`) and the family of
prime components of `Δ` gives a finite surjective `p₁ : X₁ ⟶ X` from a smooth projective
variety with `p₁^*Δ = Δ₁` snc with coefficients in `[0, 1)` among those of `Δ`; the pull-backs
of the groups are again groups of pairwise disjoint components (each `p₁⁻¹ P` is smooth), and
`p₁^* D₀` is linearly equivalent to `m D` for a divisor `D` on `X₁`. -/
public theorem exists_bloch_gieseker_stage
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (Δ : QDivisor X) (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (hΔ01 : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    {a : ℚ} (ha : a ≠ 0) {s : ℕ} (G : Fin (s + 1) → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hG : IsLevelPartition Δ a G) :
    ∃ (X₁ : Scheme.{u}) (p : X₁ ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₁) (_ : IsNormal X₁) (_ : CompactSpace X₁)
      (Δ₁ : QDivisor X₁) (G₁ : Fin (s + 1) → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₁)) (D : Divisor X₁)
      (hΔp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₁, p (componentGenericPoint X₁ C) ∉ Δ.supp),
      Δ.IsPullback p hΔp Δ₁ ∧ Δ₁.IsSNC (p ≫ f) ∧
      (∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₁, 0 ≤ Δ₁.coeff P ∧ Δ₁.coeff P < 1) ∧
      Δ₁.frange ⊆ Δ.frange ∧ IsLevelPartition Δ₁ a G₁ ∧
      Divisor.LinearlyEquivalent (∑ P ∈ G₁ 0, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) ((a.den : ℤ) • D) := by
  classical
  have hsmX : IsSmoothScheme f := (isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance
  have hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  have hq : ∀ D : QDivisor X, D.IsQCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  have hTS' : ∀ i, ∀ P ∈ G i, P ∈ Δ.support := fun _ _ => hG.mem_support ha
  have hTS : G 0 ⊆ Δ.support := fun _ => hG.mem_support ha
  have hS := isSNC_sum_single_support hΔ
  obtain ⟨Y, g, _, _, hproj, hsm, _, _, _, E, D, hgen, hpb, hred, hdisj, hdisjQ, hsnc, hlin⟩ :=
    exists_bloch_gieseker_cover_divisors k f Δ.support (G 0) hTS hS a.den a.den_pos
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (g ≫ f) := hproj
  set S := Δ.support
  set Δ₁ : QDivisor Y := ∑ P ∈ S, Δ P • Divisor.toQDivisor (E P) with hΔ₁
  have key : ∀ Q, (∃ P ∈ S, Q ∈ (E P).support ∧ Δ₁ Q = Δ P) ∨
      ((∀ P ∈ S, Q ∉ (E P).support) ∧ Δ₁ Q = 0) := by
    intro Q
    by_cases h : ∃ P ∈ S, Q ∈ (E P).support
    · obtain ⟨P, hP, hQ⟩ := h
      exact Or.inl ⟨P, hP, hQ, sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply S _ E (fun P hP => (hred P hP).2) hdisj
        hP hQ⟩
    · push Not at h
      exact Or.inr ⟨h, sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply_of_notMem S _ E h⟩
  have hred' : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, E P Q = 0 ∨ E P Q = 1 := fun P hP => (hred P hP).2
  have huniq : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, ∀ Q, Q ∈ (E P).support → Q ∈ (E P').support → P = P' :=
    fun P hP P' hP' Q h h' => by
      by_contra hne
      exact Finset.disjoint_left.mp (hdisj P hP P' hP' hne) h h'
  have hpΔ : Δ.IsPullback g
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g Δ) Δ₁ :=
    qDivisor_isPullback_congr _ (qDivisor_isPullback_sum_smul g hcart hq S (fun P => Δ P) E hpb
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g _))
      (qDivisor_eq_sum_smul_single Δ).symm rfl
  refine ⟨Y, g, inferInstance, inferInstance, hproj, hsm, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    inferInstance, Δ₁, fun i => (G i).biUnion fun P => (E P).support, D, _, hpΔ, ?_, ?_, ?_,
    ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · -- snc
    refine hsnc.of_support_subset fun Q hQ => ?_
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, hQP, -⟩ | ⟨-, h0⟩
    · exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr (by
        rw [sum_apply_of_mem_support S E hred' hdisj hP hQP]; exact one_ne_zero)
    · exact absurd h0 (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ)
  · intro Q
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, -, -, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
    · change 0 ≤ Δ₁ Q ∧ Δ₁ Q < 1
      rw [h]; exact hΔ01 P
    · change 0 ≤ Δ₁ Q ∧ Δ₁ Q < 1
      rw [h]; norm_num
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨hx0, Q, rfl⟩ := Finsupp.mem_frange.mp hx
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, -, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
    · rw [h]; exact Finsupp.mem_frange.mpr ⟨Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hP, P, rfl⟩
    · exact absurd h hx0
  · intro Q
    constructor
    · intro hQ
      rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, hQP, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
      · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := (hG.1 P).mp ((show Δ₁ Q = Δ.coeff P from h).symm.trans hQ)
        exact ⟨i, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨P, hi, hQP⟩⟩
      · exact absurd ((show Δ₁ Q = a from hQ).symm.trans h) ha
    · rintro ⟨i, hi⟩
      obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hi
      have hPS : P ∈ S := hTS' i P hPi
      change Δ₁ Q = a
      rw [sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply S _ E hred' hdisj hPS hQP]
      exact (hG.1 P).mpr ⟨i, hPi⟩
  · intro i j Q hi hj
    obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hi
    obtain ⟨P', hPj, hQP'⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hj
    have := huniq P (hTS' i P hPi) P' (hTS' j P' hPj) Q hQP hQP'
    subst this
    exact hG.2.1 i j P hPi hPj
  · intro i Q hQ Q' hQ' hne
    obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hQ
    obtain ⟨P', hPi', hQP'⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hQ'
    refine hdisjQ P (hTS' i P hPi) P' (hTS' i P' hPi') ?_ Q hQP Q' hQP' hne
    by_cases hPP : P = P'
    · exact Or.inl hPP
    · exact Or.inr (hG.2.2.1 i P hPi P' hPi' hPP)
  · intro i
    obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := hG.2.2.2 i
    obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.mpr (hred P (hTS' i P hP)).1
    exact ⟨Q, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨P, hP, hQ⟩⟩
  · refine (congrArg (fun F : Divisor Y => F.LinearlyEquivalent ((a.den : ℤ) • D)) ?_).mpr hlin
    refine Finsupp.ext fun Q => ?_
    dsimp only
    rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]
    by_cases hQ : ∃ P ∈ G 0, Q ∈ (E P).support
    · obtain ⟨P, hP, hQP⟩ := hQ
      have hQ0 : Q ∈ (G 0).biUnion fun P => (E P).support := Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨P, hP, hQP⟩
      rw [Finset.sum_eq_single Q (fun Q' _ hne => by simp [Finsupp.single_apply, hne])
        (fun h => absurd hQ0 h), Finsupp.single_eq_same,
        sum_apply_of_mem_support (G 0) E (fun P hP => hred' P (hTS hP))
          (fun P hP P' hP' => hdisj P (hTS hP) P' (hTS hP')) hP hQP]
    · push Not at hQ
      have hQ0 : Q ∉ (G 0).biUnion fun P => (E P).support := fun h => by
        obtain ⟨P, hP, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp h
        exact hQ P hP hQP
      rw [Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun Q' hQ' => by
        rw [Finsupp.single_apply, if_neg]; rintro rfl; exact hQ0 hQ'), Finsupp.finset_sum_apply,
        Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun P hP => Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp (hQ P hP))]

section CyclicCoverRetract

/-! ### The summands `Symᵇ N` of `p_* 𝒪_Z` for a cyclic cover, and the cohomology clause -/

open Opposite

/-- `𝒪(E)^{⊗ n} ≅ 𝒪(n E)` for the Stacks tensor power and a Cartier divisor `E`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def tensorPowerDivisorialSheafIso {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (E : Divisor X)
    (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, SheafOfModules.tensorPower (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) (Osharp := X.sheaf)
      E.divisorialSheaf n ≅ ((n : ℤ) • E).divisorialSheaf
  | 0 => (Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso).symm ≪≫ eqToIso (by rw [Nat.cast_zero, zero_smul])
  | 1 => eqToIso (by rw [Nat.cast_one, one_smul]; rfl)
  | n + 2 => ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.sheaf).obj E.divisorialSheaf).mapIso
      (tensorPowerDivisorialSheafIso E hcart (n + 1)) ≪≫
      (hcart E).divisorialSheafTensorIso (hcart _) ≪≫
      eqToIso (by congr 1; push_cast; rw [add_smul, add_smul, two_smul, one_smul]; abel)

/-- `Symⁿ 𝒪(E) ≅ 𝒪(n E)` for a Cartier divisor `E`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def symPieceDivisorialSheafIso {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (E : Divisor X)
    (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      E.divisorialSheaf] (n : ℕ) :
    (cyclicCoverSituation E.divisorialSheaf).symmetricAlgebra.piece (n : ℤ) ≅
      ((n : ℤ) • E).divisorialSheaf :=
  (cyclicCoverSituation E.divisorialSheaf).symmetricPieceIsoTensorPower n ≪≫
    tensorPowerDivisorialSheafIso E hcart n

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]
    (m : ℕ) (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

/-- `p_* 𝒪_Z` for the cyclic cover. -/
public noncomputable abbrev cyclicCoverPushUnit : X.Modules :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ)).obj (SheafOfModules.unit _)

public theorem cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl_map (i : ℕ) {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ i W'
        (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op x) =
      (cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).preimage_mono h)).op
        (cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ i W x) := by
  unfold cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl
  rw [← symSpecFunction_restrict]
  exact (((ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ _ _).symm.trans (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    ((cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.naturality
      (homOfLE ((symSpecToBase N).preimage_mono h)).op) (symSpecFunction N i W x)).symm).trans
    (ConcreteCategory.comp_apply _ _ _)).symm

/-- `ιᵢ` as a linear map on sections over `W`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverInclLinear (hm : 0 < m) (i : ℕ) (W : X.Opensᵒᵖ) :
    ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ)).val.obj W →ₗ[X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W]
      (cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ).val.obj W where
  toFun x := cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ i W.unop x
  map_add' x y := (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W.unop).2.1 i x y
  map_smul' r x := (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W.unop).2.2.1 i r x

/-- The inclusion `Symⁱ N ⟶ p_* 𝒪_Z` of sheaves of modules. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverInclHom (hm : 0 < m) (i : ℕ) :
    (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ) ⟶ cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ where
  val :=
    { app := fun W => ModuleCat.ofHom (R := X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W)
          (X := ↥(((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ)).val.obj W))
          (Y := ↥((cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ).val.obj W)) (cyclicCoverInclLinear N m σ hm i W)
      naturality := by
        intro W W' h
        ext x
        exact cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl_map N m σ i (leOfHom h.unop) x }

/-- The families `(xᵢ)_{i<m}` of sections over `W` of the pieces `Symⁱ N`, `i < m`. -/
public abbrev CyclicCoverPieces (W : X.Opens) : Type u :=
  (i : Fin m) → ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((i : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)

/-- The decomposition map `(xᵢ)_{i<m} ↦ ∑ᵢ ιᵢ(xᵢ)` over `W`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverDecompSum (W : X.Opens)
    (x : CyclicCoverPieces N m W) :
    Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ W) :=
  ∑ i : Fin m, cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ (i : ℕ) W (x i)

public theorem cyclicCoverDecompSum_add (hm : 0 < m) (W : X.Opens)
    (x y : CyclicCoverPieces N m W) :
    cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W (x + y) =
      cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W x + cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W y := by
  unfold cyclicCoverDecompSum
  rw [← Finset.sum_add_distrib]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W).2.1 i _ _

public theorem cyclicCoverDecompSum_smul (hm : 0 < m) (W : X.Opens)
    (r : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))
    (x : CyclicCoverPieces N m W) :
    cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W (r • x) =
      (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).app W r * cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W x := by
  unfold cyclicCoverDecompSum
  rw [Finset.mul_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W).2.2.1 i r _

public theorem cyclicCoverDecompSum_restrict {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (x : CyclicCoverPieces N m W) :
    cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W' (fun i =>
        ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((i : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.map
          (homOfLE h).op (x i)) =
      (cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).preimage_mono h)).op
        (cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W x) := by
  unfold cyclicCoverDecompSum
  rw [map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl_map N m σ i h (x i)

/-- The inverse of the decomposition over `W`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverDecompInv (hm : 0 < m) (W : X.Opens) :
    Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ W) ≃
      CyclicCoverPieces N m W :=
  (Equiv.ofBijective _ (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W).1).symm

public theorem cyclicCoverDecompSum_decompInv (hm : 0 < m) (W : X.Opens)
    (y : Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ W)) :
    cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W (cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W y) = y :=
  (Equiv.ofBijective _ (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W).1).apply_symm_apply y

public theorem cyclicCoverDecompInv_eq_iff (hm : 0 < m) (W : X.Opens)
    (y : Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ W))
    (x : CyclicCoverPieces N m W) :
    cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W y = x ↔ cyclicCoverDecompSum N m σ W x = y :=
  (Equiv.ofBijective _ (cyclicCoverAlgebra_decomposition N m hm σ W).1).symm_apply_eq.trans
    eq_comm

/-- The projection `p_* 𝒪_Z ⟶ Symᵇ N` onto the summand `b < m`, on sections over `W`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverProjLinear (hm : 0 < m) (b : Fin m) (W : X.Opensᵒᵖ) :
    (cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ).val.obj W →ₗ[X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W]
      ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((b : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.obj W where
  toFun y := cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop y b
  map_add' y y' := by
    have : cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop (y + y') =
        cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop y + cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop y' := by
      refine (cyclicCoverDecompInv_eq_iff N m σ hm W.unop _ _).mpr ?_
      exact (cyclicCoverDecompSum_add N m σ hm W.unop _ _).trans
        ((congrArg₂ (· + ·) (cyclicCoverDecompSum_decompInv N m σ hm W.unop y)
          (cyclicCoverDecompSum_decompInv N m σ hm W.unop y')).trans rfl)
    exact congrFun this b
  map_smul' r y := by
    have : cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop (r • y) =
        r • cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop y := by
      refine (cyclicCoverDecompInv_eq_iff N m σ hm W.unop _ _).mpr ?_
      exact (cyclicCoverDecompSum_smul N m σ hm W.unop r _).trans
        ((congrArg (_ * ·) (cyclicCoverDecompSum_decompInv N m σ hm W.unop y)).trans rfl)
    exact congrFun this b

/-- The projection `p_* 𝒪_Z ⟶ Symᵇ N` of sheaves of modules. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicCoverProjHom (hm : 0 < m) (b : Fin m) :
    cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ ⟶ (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((b : ℕ) : ℤ) where
  val :=
    { app := fun W => ModuleCat.ofHom (R := X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W)
          (X := ↥((cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ).val.obj W))
          (Y := ↥(((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((b : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.obj W))
          (cyclicCoverProjLinear N m σ hm b W)
      naturality := by
        intro W W' h
        ext y
        have hres : cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W'.unop
            ((cyclicCover N m σ).presheaf.map
              (homOfLE ((cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).preimage_mono (leOfHom h.unop))).op y) =
            fun i : Fin m => ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((i : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.map
              (homOfLE (leOfHom h.unop)).op (cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop y i) := by
          refine (cyclicCoverDecompInv_eq_iff N m σ hm W'.unop _ _).mpr ?_
          exact (cyclicCoverDecompSum_restrict N m σ (leOfHom h.unop) _).trans
            (congrArg _ (cyclicCoverDecompSum_decompInv N m σ hm W.unop y))
        exact (congrFun hres b).trans rfl }

/-- `ι_b ≫ π_b = 𝟙` for `b < m`. -/
public theorem cyclicCoverInclHom_projHom (hm : 0 < m) (b : Fin m) :
    cyclicCoverInclHom N m σ hm (b : ℕ) ≫ cyclicCoverProjHom N m σ hm b = 𝟙 _ := by
  classical
  ext W x
  change cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop (cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ (b : ℕ) W.unop x) b = x
  have : cyclicCoverDecompInv N m σ hm W.unop (cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ (b : ℕ) W.unop x) =
      Pi.single b x := by
    refine (cyclicCoverDecompInv_eq_iff N m σ hm W.unop _ _).mpr ?_
    unfold cyclicCoverDecompSum
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single b (fun i _ hi => by
      rw [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hi]
      exact (cyclicCoverInclLinear N m σ hm (i : ℕ) W).map_zero)
      (fun h => absurd (Finset.mem_univ b) h),
      Pi.single_eq_same]
  rw [this, Pi.single_eq_same]

open MonoidalCategory in
/-- **`H^i(X, M ⊗ Symᵇ N)` is a retract of `H^i(Z, G)`, `G ≅ p^* M`** for the cyclic cover
`p : Z ⟶ X`, `b < m` and `M` quasi-coherent. -/
public theorem nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_tensor_piece (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (hm : 0 < m) (b : Fin m) (M : X.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    (G : (cyclicCover N m σ).Modules) [G.IsQuasicoherent]
    (eG : (Scheme.Modules.pullback (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ)).obj M ≅ G) (i : ℕ) :
    letI : MonoidalCategory X.Modules := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.monoidalCategory
      X.presheaf (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X)
    Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f
        (M ⊗ (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((b : ℕ) : ℤ)) i)
      (cohomologyOverField k (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ≫ f) G i)) := by
  letI : MonoidalCategory X.Modules := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.monoidalCategory
    X.presheaf (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X)
  haveI := isAffineHom_cyclicCoverToBase N m σ
  obtain ⟨e, -⟩ := MMP.Modules.exists_pushforward_pullback_iso_tensor_unit
    (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ) M
  let W : Retract (M ⊗ (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece ((b : ℕ) : ℤ))
      (M ⊗ cyclicCoverPushUnit N m σ) :=
    { i := M ◁ cyclicCoverInclHom N m σ hm (b : ℕ)
      r := M ◁ cyclicCoverProjHom N m σ hm b
      retract := (MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp M _ _).symm.trans
        ((congrArg (M ◁ ·) (cyclicCoverInclHom_projHom N m σ hm b)).trans
          (MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_id M _)) }
  exact ⟨(((W.trans e.retract).trans
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ)).mapIso eG).retract).map
        (cohomologyOverFieldFunctor k f i)).trans
    (cohomologyOverFieldPushforwardIsoOfIsAffineHom k (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ) f _ i).symm.retract⟩

omit [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N] in
open MonoidalCategory in
/-- **The cohomology summand of a cyclic cover, for divisors.** For the cyclic cover
`p : Z ⟶ X` built from `N = 𝒪(-D)`, divisors `B`, `D` on `X` with pull-backs `B'`, `D''`, a
divisor `R ∼ D''` on `Z` and `b < m`, `H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` is a retract of
`H^i(Z, 𝒪(-(B' - b R)))`. -/
public theorem nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_cyclicCover_divisor (k : Type u) [Field k]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
    (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (D : Divisor X)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (-D).divisorialSheaf]
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation (-D).divisorialSheaf).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (hm : 0 < m)
    [IsLocallyNoetherian (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)]
    [IsNormal (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)]
    [CompactSpace (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)]
    [IsIntegral (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)]
    [IsDominant (cyclicCoverToBase (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)]
    {D'' R : Divisor (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)}
    (hD : D.IsPullback (cyclicCoverToBase (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _) D'')
    (hR : R.LinearlyEquivalent D'') (B : Divisor X)
    {B' : Divisor (cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)}
    (hB : B.IsPullback (cyclicCoverToBase (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _) B')
    (b : Fin m) (i : ℕ) :
    Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
      (cohomologyOverField k (cyclicCoverToBase (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ ≫ f)
        (-(B' - ((b : ℕ) : ℤ) • R)).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  letI : MonoidalCategory X.Modules := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.monoidalCategory
    X.presheaf (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isSheaf_structureRingPresheaf X)
  set p := cyclicCoverToBase (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ
  set c : ℤ := ((b : ℕ) : ℤ)
  -- `M = 𝒪(-B + c D)`
  have hpb : (-B + c • D).IsPullback p
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _)
      (-B' + c • D'') := by
    have hBn := (hB.zsmul (hcart B) (-1)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _)).of_eq
      (hB₂ := map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _)
      (neg_one_zsmul B)
    have hDc := hD.zsmul (hcart D) c
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' _ _)
    rw [neg_one_zsmul] at hBn
    exact Divisor.IsPullback.add (hcart _) (hcart _) _ hBn hDc
  have hlin : (-B' + c • D'').LinearlyEquivalent (-(B' - c • R)) := by
    rw [Divisor.linearlyEquivalent_iff_sub_mem_range]
    have h := (Divisor.linearlyEquivalent_iff_sub_mem_range.mp hR.symm)
    have : -B' + c • D'' - -(B' - c • R) = c • (D'' - R) := by
      rw [smul_sub]; abel
    rw [this]
    exact AddSubgroup.zsmul_mem _ h c
  let eM : (-B + c • D).divisorialSheaf ⊗
      (cyclicCoverSituation (-D).divisorialSheaf).symmetricAlgebra.piece c ≅
      (-B).divisorialSheaf :=
    whiskerLeftIso _ (symPieceDivisorialSheafIso (-D) hcart (b : ℕ)) ≪≫
      (hcart _).divisorialSheafTensorIso (hcart _) ≪≫
      eqToIso (by congr 1; rw [smul_neg]; abel)
  obtain ⟨Rt⟩ := nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_tensor_piece (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ k f hm b
    (-B + c • D).divisorialSheaf (-(B' - c • R)).divisorialSheaf
    ((hpb.divisorialSheafIso (hBc := hcart _)).symm ≪≫ hlin.divisorialSheafIso) i
  exact ⟨((cohomologyOverFieldFunctor k f i).mapIso eM).symm.retract.trans Rt⟩

/-- The section `σ : Symᵐ(𝒪(-D)) ⟶ 𝒪_X` of the cyclic cover branched along an effective `D₀ ∼ m D`:
`Symᵐ(𝒪(-D)) ≅ 𝒪(-m D) ≅ 𝒪(-D₀) ⊆ 𝒪_X`. -/
@[expose] public noncomputable def cyclicSection {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) (m : ℕ) (D D₀ : Divisor X)
    (hD₀ : 0 ≤ D₀) (hD : D₀.LinearlyEquivalent ((m : ℤ) • D))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (-D).divisorialSheaf] :
    (cyclicCoverSituation (-D).divisorialSheaf).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf :=
  (symPieceDivisorialSheafIso (-D) hcart m).hom ≫
    (show ((m : ℤ) • -D).LinearlyEquivalent (-D₀) by
      rw [smul_neg]; exact hD.neg.symm).divisorialSheafIso.hom ≫
    Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀) ≫ Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom

/-- The image of `cyclicSection` on sections over `U` is that of `𝒪(-D₀) ⊆ 𝒪_X`. -/
public theorem range_cyclicSection_app {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    [CompactSpace X] (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) (m : ℕ) (D D₀ : Divisor X)
    (hD₀ : 0 ≤ D₀) (hD : D₀.LinearlyEquivalent ((m : ℤ) • D))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (-D).divisorialSheaf] (U : X.Opens) :
    Set.range ((cyclicSection hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD).val.app (op U)) =
      Set.range ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀) ≫
        Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom).val.app (op U)) := by
  set e := symPieceDivisorialSheafIso (-D) hcart m ≪≫
    (show ((m : ℤ) • -D).LinearlyEquivalent (-D₀) by
      rw [smul_neg]; exact hD.neg.symm).divisorialSheafIso
  have hσ : cyclicSection hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD = e.hom ≫ (Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion
      (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀) ≫ Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom) :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
  rw [hσ]
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨e.inv.val.app (op U) x, ?_⟩
    have h := congrArg (fun φ : (-D₀).divisorialSheaf ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf =>
      φ.val.app (op U) x) (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc e (Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion
        (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀) ≫ Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom))
    simp only [SheafOfModules.comp_val, PresheafOfModules.comp_app, ModuleCat.comp_apply] at h ⊢
    exact h

end CyclicCoverRetract

/-! ### The zero scheme of `cyclicSection` and the branch divisor -/

/-- The colength of a principal ideal `(t)` of `𝒪_{X,Q}` is non-zero exactly when `t` is not a
unit. -/
public theorem length_quotient_span_ne_zero_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) {t : Q.localRing} (ht : t ≠ 0) :
    (Module.length Q.localRing (Q.localRing ⧸ Ideal.span {t})).toNat ≠ 0 ↔
      t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Q.localRing := by
  have : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 Q.localRing := krullDimLE_of_coheight_le Q.coheight_genericPoint.le
  have := Q.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
  have hnz : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Q.localRing := mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero ht
  have hfin : IsFiniteLength Q.localRing (Q.localRing ⧸ Ideal.span {t}) :=
    isFiniteLength_quotient_span_singleton _ hnz
  rw [Ne, ENat.toNat_eq_zero, not_or, Module.length_eq_zero_iff, not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial,
    Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff, Ne, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal,
    mem_nonunits_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, Module.length_ne_top_iff.mpr hfin⟩⟩

/-- `v_Q(t) ≥ 1` for `t ∈ 𝒪_{X,Q}` exactly when `t` lies in the maximal ideal. -/
public theorem ordGE_one_toComponent_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (t : Q.localRing) :
    Q.OrdGE 1 (Q.toComponent.hom t) ↔ t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Q.localRing := by
  by_cases ht : t = 0
  · subst ht
    simp only [map_zero, Submodule.zero_mem, iff_true]
    exact PrimeDivisor.OrdGE.zero _
  have hv := valuation_toComponent_eq_length Q ht
  have hne : Q.toComponent.hom t ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    rw [h0, map_zero] at hv
    exact WithZero.coe_ne_zero hv.symm
  rw [← length_quotient_span_ne_zero_iff Q ht]
  unfold PrimeDivisor.OrdGE
  rw [hv, WithZero.exp_le_exp]
  constructor
  · rintro (h | h)
    · exact absurd h hne
    · omega
  · intro h; right; omega

/-- A regular function on `U` is in the image of `𝒪(-D₀) ⊆ 𝒪(0) ≅ 𝒪_X` exactly when it is a section
of `𝒪(-D₀)`. -/
public theorem mem_range_inclusion_zeroIso_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] {D₀ : Divisor X} (hD₀ : 0 ≤ D₀) (U : X.Opens) (y : Γ(X, U)) :
    y ∈ Set.range ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀) ≫
        Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom).val.app (Opposite.op U)) ↔
      (-D₀).IsDivisorialSection U ((toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (Opposite.op U) y) := by
  set ι := Divisor.structureSheafToDivisorialSheaf (le_refl (0 : Divisor X))
  have key : ∀ z, ι.app U (Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom.app U z) = z := fun z =>
    congrArg (fun φ : (0 : Divisor X).divisorialSheaf ⟶ _ => φ.app U z) (IsIso.inv_hom_id ι)
  have key2 : ∀ r, Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom.app U (ι.app U r) = r := fun r =>
    congrArg (fun φ : _ ⟶ MMP.Mori.structureSheafModule X => φ.app U r) (IsIso.hom_inv_id ι)
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
    have h := congrArg Subtype.val (key ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion
      (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀)).app U x))
    have h' : (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (Opposite.op U)
        (Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom.app U
          ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀)).app U x)) = x.1 :=
      (Divisor.coe_structureSheafToDivisorialSheaf_app _ U _).symm.trans h
    change (-D₀).IsDivisorialSection U ((toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (Opposite.op U)
      (Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom.app U
        ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀)).app U x)))
    rw [h']
    exact x.2
  · intro h
    refine ⟨⟨_, h⟩, ?_⟩
    change Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso.hom.app U
      ((Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀)).app U ⟨_, h⟩) = y
    have : (Divisor.divisorialSheafInclusion (neg_nonpos.mpr hD₀)).app U ⟨_, h⟩ = ι.app U y :=
      Subtype.ext (by rw [Divisor.coe_divisorialSheafInclusion_app,
        Divisor.coe_structureSheafToDivisorialSheaf_app])
    rw [this]
    exact key2 y

open Classical in
/-- A regular function `y` on `U` is a section of `𝒪(-∑_{P ∈ T} P)` exactly when it vanishes at
the generic point of every `P ∈ T` lying in `U`. -/
public theorem isDivisorialSection_neg_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] {D₀ : Divisor X} (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hcoef : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, D₀.coeff E = if E ∈ T then 1 else 0)
    (U : X.Opens) (y : Γ(X, U)) :
    (-D₀).IsDivisorialSection U ((toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (Opposite.op U) y) ↔
      ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U → P.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen y := by
  have hgerm : ∀ (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (h : (E.support ∩ U).Nonempty),
      (toRationalFunctionsPresheaf X).app (Opposite.op U) y
        ⟨E.component, E.componentGenericPoint_mem_of_nonempty h⟩ =
      E.toComponent.hom (X.presheaf.germ U E.genericPoint (E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty h) y) :=
    fun E h => by
      rw [toRationalFunctionsPresheaf_app_apply]
      exact (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply ..).symm
  have hcneg : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, -(-D₀).coeff E = D₀.coeff E := fun E => by
    change -((-D₀) E) = D₀ E
    rw [Finsupp.neg_apply, neg_neg]
  have hunit : ∀ (E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (hη : E.genericPoint ∈ U),
      E.OrdGE 1 (E.toComponent.hom (X.presheaf.germ U E.genericPoint hη y)) ↔
        E.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen y := by
    intro E hη
    rw [ordGE_one_toComponent_iff, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff,
      Scheme.mem_basicOpen _ _ _ hη]
  constructor
  · intro h P hP hη
    have hne : (P.support ∩ U).Nonempty := (P.genericPoint_mem_iff U).mp hη
    have h1 := h P hne
    rw [hgerm P hne, hcneg, hcoef, if_pos hP] at h1
    exact (hunit P hη).mp h1
  · intro h E hE
    rw [hgerm E hE, hcneg, hcoef]
    split_ifs with hET
    · exact (hunit E _).mpr (h E hET (E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hE))
    · by_cases ht : X.presheaf.germ U E.genericPoint (E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hE) y = 0
      · rw [ht, map_zero]; exact PrimeDivisor.OrdGE.zero _
      · exact Or.inr (by rw [WithZero.exp_zero]; exact E.one_le_valuation_toComponent ht)

open Classical in
/-- **Sections of the zero scheme of `cyclicSection`.** For `D₀ = ∑_{P ∈ T} P`, a regular function
on an affine open `U` lies in the ideal of the zero scheme of `cyclicSection` exactly when it
vanishes at the generic point of every `P ∈ T` lying in `U`. -/
public theorem mem_zeroSchemeIdeal_cyclicSection_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) (m : ℕ) (D D₀ : Divisor X)
    (hD₀ : 0 ≤ D₀) (hD : D₀.LinearlyEquivalent ((m : ℤ) • D))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (-D).divisorialSheaf] (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hcoef : ∀ E : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, D₀.coeff E = if E ∈ T then 1 else 0)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (g : Γ(X, U)) :
    g ∈ (zeroSchemeIdeal (-D).divisorialSheaf m (cyclicSection hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD)).ideal U ↔
      ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U.1 → P.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen g := by
  rw [zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_eq_span_range]
  erw [range_cyclicSection_app hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD U.1]
  set J : Ideal Γ(X, U.1) := ⨅ P ∈ T, ⨅ (_ : P.genericPoint ∈ U.1), P.idealSheaf.ideal U with hJ
  have hJmem : ∀ y, y ∈ J ↔ ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U.1 → P.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen y := by
    intro y
    simp only [hJ, Submodule.mem_iInf, MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.mem_ideal_idealSheaf_iff]
    exact ⟨fun h P hP hη => h P hP hη hη, fun h P hP hη _ => h P hP hη⟩
  rw [← hJmem]
  suffices H : ∀ S : Set Γ(X, U.1), (∀ y, y ∈ S ↔ y ∈ J) → (g ∈ Ideal.span S ↔ g ∈ J) by
    refine H _ (fun y => ?_)
    rw [hJmem]
    constructor
    · intro hy
      exact (isDivisorialSection_neg_iff T hcoef U.1 y).mp
        ((mem_range_inclusion_zeroIso_iff hD₀ U.1 y).mp hy)
    · intro hy
      exact (mem_range_inclusion_zeroIso_iff hD₀ U.1 y).mpr
        ((isDivisorialSection_neg_iff T hcoef U.1 y).mpr hy)
  intro S hS
  rw [show S = (J : Set Γ(X, U.1)) from Set.ext hS, Ideal.span_eq]

/-- **The ideal of a disjoint union of prime divisors, near a point.** Let `I` be an ideal sheaf
whose sections on an affine open are the functions vanishing at the generic points of the members
of a finite set `T` of pairwise disjoint prime divisors. Near a point `x` of some `P ∈ T`, `I`
agrees with the ideal of `P` on an affine open; near a point outside the members of `T`, `I` is
the unit ideal on an affine open. -/
public theorem exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_of_forall_mem_ideal_iff {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hTdisj : ∀ P ∈ T, ∀ P' ∈ T, P ≠ P' → Disjoint P.support P'.support)
    (hI : ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (g : Γ(X, U)),
      g ∈ I.ideal U ↔ ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U.1 → P.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen g)
    (x : X) :
    (∃ P ∈ T, x ∈ P.support ∧ ∃ W : X.affineOpens, x ∈ W.1 ∧
        I.ideal W = P.idealSheaf.ideal W) ∨
      ((∀ P ∈ T, x ∉ P.support) ∧ ∃ W : X.affineOpens, x ∈ W.1 ∧ I.ideal W = ⊤) := by
  classical
  set C : Set X := ⋃ P ∈ T.filter (fun P => x ∉ P.support), P.support with hC
  have hCc : IsClosed C := by
    refine Set.Finite.isClosed_biUnion (Finset.finite_toSet _) fun P _ => ?_
    exact P.idealSheaf.support.isClosed
  have hxC : x ∈ Cᶜ := by
    simp only [hC, Set.mem_compl_iff, Set.mem_iUnion, Finset.mem_filter, not_exists, not_and]
    tauto
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, hUC⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show x ∈ (⟨Cᶜ, hCc.isOpen_compl⟩ : X.Opens) from hxC)
  have hmem : ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U → x ∈ P.support := by
    intro P hP hη
    by_contra hx
    have : P.genericPoint ∈ C := by
      simp only [hC, Set.mem_iUnion, Finset.mem_filter]
      refine ⟨P, ⟨hP, hx⟩, ?_⟩
      rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure]; exact subset_closure rfl
    exact hUC hη this
  by_cases hex : ∃ P ∈ T, x ∈ P.support
  · obtain ⟨P₀, hP₀, hxP₀⟩ := hex
    refine Or.inl ⟨P₀, hP₀, hxP₀, ⟨U, hU⟩, hxU, ?_⟩
    ext g
    rw [hI, MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.mem_ideal_idealSheaf_iff]
    constructor
    · exact fun h => h P₀ hP₀
    · intro h P hP hη
      by_cases hPP : P = P₀
      · subst hPP; exact h hη
      · exact absurd ⟨x, hmem P hP hη, hxP₀⟩
          (Set.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.mpr ((hTdisj P hP P₀ hP₀ hPP).inter_eq))
  · push Not at hex
    refine Or.inr ⟨hex, ⟨U, hU⟩, hxU, ?_⟩
    rw [eq_top_iff]
    intro g _
    rw [hI]
    exact fun P hP hη => absurd (hmem P hP hη) (hex P hP)

/-- **The stalks of the ideal of a disjoint union of prime divisors.** Let `I` be an ideal sheaf
whose sections on an affine open are the functions vanishing at the generic points of the members
of a finite set `T` of pairwise disjoint prime divisors. At a point `x` of some `P ∈ T` the stalk
of `I` is that of the ideal of `P`; away from the members of `T` it is the unit ideal. -/
public theorem stalk_eq_of_forall_mem_ideal_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hTdisj : ∀ P ∈ T, ∀ P' ∈ T, P ≠ P' → Disjoint P.support P'.support)
    (hI : ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (g : Γ(X, U)),
      g ∈ I.ideal U ↔ ∀ P ∈ T, P.genericPoint ∈ U.1 → P.genericPoint ∉ X.basicOpen g)
    (x : X) :
    (∃ P ∈ T, x ∈ P.support ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf x) ∨
      ((∀ P ∈ T, x ∉ P.support) ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = ⊤) := by
  rcases exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_of_forall_mem_ideal_iff I T hTdisj hI x with
    ⟨P, hP, hx, W, hxW, hW⟩ | ⟨hnot, W, hxW, hW⟩
  · refine Or.inl ⟨P, hP, hx, ?_⟩
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I x W hxW,
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ P.idealSheaf x W hxW, hW]
  · refine Or.inr ⟨hnot, ?_⟩
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I x W hxW, hW, Ideal.map_top]

/-- If two ideal sheaves agree on an affine open `W`, their inverse images along `g` have the same
stalks at the points of `g⁻¹ W`. -/
public theorem stalk_comap_eq_of_ideal_eq {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X)
    {I J : X.IdealSheafData} (W : X.affineOpens) (h : I.ideal W = J.ideal W) {y : Y}
    (hy : g y ∈ W.1) :
    IdealSheafData.stalk (I.comap g) y = IdealSheafData.stalk (J.comap g) y := by
  obtain ⟨U, hyU, hUW⟩ :=
    MMP.exists_affineOpens_le (U := g ⁻¹ᵁ W.1) hy
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ y U hyU,
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ y U hyU,
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I g W U hUW,
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE J g W U hUW, h]

/-- For an effective Cartier divisor `J` and a prime divisor `Q` of a locally Noetherian normal
scheme, the colength of `Jⁿ` at the generic point of `Q` is `n` times that of `J`. -/
public theorem length_stalk_pow {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    (J : Y.IdealSheafData) (hJ : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor J)
    (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y) (n : ℕ) :
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk J Q.genericPoint ^ n)).toNat : ℤ) =
      n * ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
        (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk J Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hst⟩ := exists_stalk_eq_span_mem_nonZeroDivisors J hJ Q.genericPoint
  rw [hst, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  have ht0 : (t : Q.localRing) ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero ht
  have htn0 : (t ^ n : Q.localRing) ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (pow_mem ht n)
  have h1 := valuation_toComponent_eq_length Q htn0
  rw [map_pow, map_pow, valuation_toComponent_eq_length Q ht0, ← WithZero.exp_nsmul] at h1
  have h2 := WithZero.exp_injective h1
  rw [nsmul_eq_mul] at h2
  exact h2.symm

open Classical in
/-- The colength at generic points of an ideal sheaf whose stalks are those of a disjoint union of
the prime divisors `P ∈ T`. -/
public theorem length_stalk_of_stalk_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hECD : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor P.idealSheaf)
    (hst : ∀ x : X,
      (∃ P ∈ T, x ∈ P.support ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf x) ∨
        ((∀ P ∈ T, x ∉ P.support) ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = ⊤))
    (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) :
    ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) =
      if Q ∈ T then 1 else 0 := by
  rcases hst Q.genericPoint with ⟨P, hP, hmem, heq⟩ | ⟨hnot, htop⟩
  · obtain rfl := eq_of_genericPoint_mem_primeDivisor_support hmem
    rw [heq, length_stalk_idealSheaf Q Q (hECD Q), if_pos rfl, if_pos hP]
  · rw [if_neg (fun hQ => hnot Q hQ (primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support Q)), htop]
    exact length_quotient_top_toNat _

/-- An ideal sheaf whose stalks are those of a disjoint union of smooth prime divisors cuts out a
smooth subscheme. -/
public theorem smooth_subschemeι_of_stalk_eq {k : Type u} [Field k] [PerfectField k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hsm : ∀ P ∈ T, Smooth (P.idealSheaf.subschemeι ≫ f))
    (hst : ∀ x : X,
      (∃ P ∈ T, x ∈ P.support ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf x) ∨
        ((∀ P ∈ T, x ∉ P.support) ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk I x = ⊤)) :
    Smooth (I.subschemeι ≫ f) := by
  rw [MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing_stalk]
  intro z
  have hz : I.subschemeι z ∈ I.support := by
    show I.subschemeι z ∈ (I.support : Set X)
    rw [← I.range_subschemeι]; exact ⟨z, rfl⟩
  rcases hst (I.subschemeι z) with ⟨P, hP, hmem, heq⟩ | ⟨-, htop⟩
  · obtain ⟨z', hz'⟩ : I.subschemeι z ∈ Set.range P.idealSheaf.subschemeι := by
      rwa [P.idealSheaf.range_subschemeι]
    haveI := hsm P hP
    have hreg := (MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.smooth_iff_forall_isRegularLocalRing_stalk
      (P.idealSheaf.subschemeι ≫ f)).mp inferInstance z'
    have key : ∀ (x : X) (_ : P.idealSheaf.subschemeι z' = x),
        IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk P.idealSheaf x) := by
      rintro x rfl
      haveI := hreg
      exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv
        (IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotEquiv P.idealSheaf z').symm
    haveI := key _ hz'
    exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv
      ((Ideal.quotEquivOfEq heq.symm).trans (IdealSheafData.subschemeStalkQuotEquiv I z))
  · exact absurd htop
      ((IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I _).not.mpr (not_not.mpr hz))

/-- The closed subscheme cut out by `I` is non-empty as soon as some stalk of `I` is proper. -/
public theorem nonempty_subscheme_of_stalk_ne_top {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X)
    (hx : IdealSheafData.stalk I x ≠ ⊤) : Nonempty I.subscheme := by
  have : x ∈ I.support := by
    by_contra h
    exact hx ((IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I x).mpr h)
  have h' : x ∈ (I.support : Set X) := this
  rw [← I.range_subschemeι] at h'
  obtain ⟨z, -⟩ := h'
  exact ⟨z⟩

/-- A section `σ` whose zero scheme has a unit stalk somewhere is non-zero. -/
public theorem ne_zero_of_stalk_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_top {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N] (m : ℕ)
    (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) (x : X)
    (hx : IdealSheafData.stalk (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ) x = ⊤) : σ ≠ 0 := by
  rintro rfl
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, -⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens
    (show x ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
  have hbot : (zeroSchemeIdeal N m 0).ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = ⊥ := by
    rw [zeroSchemeIdeal_ideal_eq_span_range, Ideal.span_eq_bot]
    rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
    rfl
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ x ⟨V, hV⟩ hxV, hbot, Ideal.map_bot]
    at hx
  exact (bot_ne_top : (⊥ : Ideal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) ≠ ⊤) hx

/-- `𝒪(D) ≅ 𝒪(-D)^∨` on a scheme all of whose divisors are Cartier (Tag 0B8K, through
`𝒪(-D) ⊗ 𝒪(D) ≅ 𝒪(0) ≅ 𝒪_X`). -/
public theorem nonempty_divisorialSheaf_iso_dualSheaf_neg {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier) (D : Divisor X) :
    Nonempty (D.divisorialSheaf ≅ Stacks.SheafOfModules.dualSheaf X.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property (-D).divisorialSheaf) :=
  ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorInverseIsoDualSheaf _ _ (-D).divisorialSheaf
    D.divisorialSheaf ((hcart (-D)).divisorialSheafTensorIso (hcart D) ≪≫
      eqToIso (by rw [neg_add_cancel]) ≪≫ Divisor.divisorialSheafZeroIso)⟩

/-- **The divisorial sheaf of the Weil divisor of an effective Cartier divisor.** If the
coefficients of a Cartier divisor `R` are the colengths of an effective Cartier divisor `J` at the
generic points, then `𝒪(R) ≅ 𝒪(J)`. -/
public theorem nonempty_divisorialSheaf_iso_invertibleSheaf'_of_length {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y] (J : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor J) (R : Divisor Y) (hRc : R.IsCartier)
    (hR : ∀ Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y, R Q = ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
      (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk J Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ)) :
    Nonempty (R.divisorialSheaf ≅ (Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' J : Y.Modules)) := by
  refine MMP.Threefold.Resolution.nonempty_divisorialSheaf_iso_invertibleSheaf'_of_isLocalEquation
    J R (fun Q => by change 0 ≤ R Q; rw [hR]; exact Int.natCast_nonneg _) hRc fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, f, hf, hspan⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor J hJ x
  have ha : ∀ (Z : irreducibleComponents Y) (hZ : componentGenericPoint Y Z ∈ W),
      (Y.presheaf.germ W _ hZ).hom f ≠ 0 := fun Z hZ =>
    nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (Stacks.Divisors.germ_mem_nonZeroDivisors hW hf _ hZ)
  refine ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hxW, f, MMP.Threefold.Resolution.sectionUnit f ha, hspan, ?_,
    fun Z hZ => MMP.Threefold.Resolution.sectionUnit_apply _ _ Z hZ⟩
  intro E hE
  have hη : E.genericPoint ∈ W := E.genericPoint_mem_of_nonempty hE
  have ht0 : (Y.presheaf.germ W _ hη).hom f ≠ 0 :=
    nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (Stacks.Divisors.germ_mem_nonZeroDivisors hW hf _ hη)
  have h1 := E.valuation_component (MMP.Threefold.Resolution.sectionUnit f ha)
  rw [← MMP.Threefold.Resolution.toComponent_germ_eq_sectionUnit f ha E hη,
    valuation_toComponent_eq_length E ht0] at h1
  have hst : IdealSheafData.stalk J E.genericPoint =
      Ideal.span {(Y.presheaf.germ W _ hη).hom f} := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ J _ ⟨W, hW⟩ hη, hspan, Ideal.map_span,
      Set.image_singleton]
  change R E = _
  rw [hR, hst]
  exact WithZero.exp_injective h1

open Classical in
/-- **The cyclic cover, for divisors.** Let `X` be a smooth projective variety, `S` a finite set
of prime divisors whose sum is snc, `T ⊆ S` non-empty with pairwise disjoint members (so that
`D₀ = ∑_{P ∈ T} P` is smooth), `m ≥ 2` and `D₀ ∼ m D`. The cyclic cover `g : Y ⟶ X` of degree
`m` branched along `D₀` is finite surjective from a smooth projective variety, and there are
non-zero reduced divisors `F_P` (`P ∈ S`) with pairwise disjoint supports such that `g^*P = m F_P`
for `P ∈ T` and `g^*P = F_P` otherwise; two distinct components of `F_P`, `F_{P'}` (`P, P' ∉ T`)
are disjoint when `P = P'` (`g⁻¹ P` is smooth) or `P ∩ P' = ∅`; `∑ F_P` is snc; and for every
divisor `B` and `0 ≤ b < m`, `H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` is a retract of `H^i(Y, 𝒪(-(g^*B - b R)))`,
`R = ∑_{P ∈ T} F_P`, the summand `j = b` of `g_* 𝒪(-(g^*B - b R)) ≅ ⊕_{j < m} 𝒪(-B + (b - j) D)`.
This is `MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover` with the lemmas above on cyclic covers and
`MMP.Mori.isSNC_ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_of_isSNC`, translated to divisors. -/
public theorem exists_cyclic_cover_divisors
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X]
    (S T : Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X)) (hTS : T ⊆ S) (hT : T.Nonempty)
    (hS : DivisorWithCoeffs.IsSNC f (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X))
    (hTdisj : ∀ P ∈ T, ∀ P' ∈ T, P ≠ P' → Disjoint P.support P'.support)
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 ≤ m) (D : Divisor X)
    (hD : Divisor.LinearlyEquivalent (∑ P ∈ T, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) ((m : ℤ) • D)) :
    ∃ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite g) (_ : Surjective g)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (g ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (g ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian Y) (_ : IsNormal Y) (_ : CompactSpace Y)
      (F : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → Divisor Y)
      (hgen : ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (C : irreducibleComponents Y),
        g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ))),
      (∀ P ∈ S, Divisor.IsPullback g (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) (hgen P)
        ((if P ∈ T then (m : ℤ) else 1) • F P)) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, F P ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ Q, F P Q = 0 ∨ F P Q = 1) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → Disjoint (F P).support (F P').support) ∧
      (∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ∉ T → P' ∉ T → (P = P' ∨ Disjoint P.support P'.support) →
        ∀ Q ∈ (F P).support, ∀ Q' ∈ (F P').support, Q ≠ Q' → Disjoint Q.support Q'.support) ∧
      DivisorWithCoeffs.IsSNC (g ≫ f) (∑ P ∈ S, F P) ∧
      ∀ B : Divisor X, ∃ (hBp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Y,
          g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ B.supp) (B' : Divisor Y),
        B.IsPullback g hBp B' ∧ ∀ b : ℤ, 0 ≤ b → b < m → ∀ i : ℕ,
          Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
            (cohomologyOverField k (g ≫ f) (-(B' - b • ∑ P ∈ T, F P)).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  classical
  haveI : IsQuasiProjectiveVariety k f := IsProjectiveVariety.isQuasiProjectiveVariety k f
  haveI : IsSmoothVariety k f := (isSmoothVariety_iff k f).mpr ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  have hsmX : IsSmoothScheme f := (isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance
  obtain ⟨hcart, hloc, -⟩ := MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety k f
  have hECD : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X,
      Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor P.idealSheaf :=
    MMP.Threefold.Resolution.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_idealSheaf_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  set D₀ : Divisor X := ∑ P ∈ T, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) with hD₀def
  have hD₀ : 0 ≤ D₀ := fun Q => by
    change (0 : ℤ) ≤ D₀ Q
    rw [hD₀def, sum_single_one_apply]; split_ifs <;> norm_num
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (-D).divisorialSheaf := (hcart (-D)).isInvertibleModule_divisorialSheaf
  set σ := cyclicSection hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD with hσdef
  set I := zeroSchemeIdeal (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ with hIdef
  have hI := mem_zeroSchemeIdeal_cyclicSection_iff hcart m D D₀ hD₀ hD T
    (fun E => sum_single_one_apply T E)
  have hst := stalk_eq_of_forall_mem_ideal_iff I T hTdisj hI
  have hlen := length_stalk_of_stalk_eq I T hECD hst
  have hsmD : Smooth (I.subschemeι ≫ f) :=
    smooth_subschemeι_of_stalk_eq f I T
      (fun P hP => (isSmoothScheme_iff _).mp (hS.1 P (mem_support_sum_single_one (hTS hP)))) hst
  obtain ⟨P₀, hP₀⟩ := hT
  have hne : Nonempty (zeroScheme (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ) := by
    refine nonempty_subscheme_of_stalk_ne_top I P₀.genericPoint ?_
    rcases hst P₀.genericPoint with ⟨P, -, hmem, heq⟩ | ⟨hnot, -⟩
    · rw [heq]
      exact fun h => ((IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mp h) hmem
    · exact absurd (primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support P₀) (hnot P₀ hP₀)
  have hσ : σ ≠ 0 := by
    set x₀ := componentGenericPoint X (MMP.Mori.pointComponent P₀.genericPoint)
    have hx₀ := map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant'
      (𝟙 X) D₀ (MMP.Mori.pointComponent P₀.genericPoint)
    refine ne_zero_of_stalk_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_top _ m σ x₀ ?_
    rcases hst x₀ with ⟨P, hP, hmem, -⟩ | ⟨-, htop⟩
    · refine absurd ?_ hx₀
      rw [DivisorWithCoeffs.mem_supp_iff]
      exact ⟨P, by
        change D₀ P ≠ 0; rw [hD₀def, sum_single_one_apply, if_pos hP]; exact one_ne_zero, hmem⟩
    · exact htop
  have hm0 : 0 < m := by omega
  have hsmD' : IsSmoothScheme (I.subschemeι ≫ f) := (isSmoothScheme_iff _).mpr hsmD
  obtain ⟨hvarY, hsmY, hfin, -, hsurj⟩ :=
    ramifiedCyclicCover_isVariety_smooth_isFinite_flat_surjective k f (-D).divisorialSheaf m hm σ
      hσ hsmD hne
  obtain ⟨hJsm, hJ, hJpow⟩ := ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_eq_radical_pow f hsmX
    (-D).divisorialSheaf m hm σ hσ hsmD' hne
  obtain ⟨eJ⟩ := nonempty_invertibleSheaf_radical_comap_zeroSchemeIdeal_iso_pullback f hsmX
    (-D).divisorialSheaf m hm σ hσ hsmD' hne
  set Y := cyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ with hYdef
  set g := ramifiedCyclicCover (-D).divisorialSheaf m σ with hgdef
  set J := (I.comap g).radical with hJdef
  -- the prime components of `∑_{P ∈ S} P` off the branch divisor
  set U' := S.filter (· ∉ T) with hU'def
  have hU' : ∀ P, P ∈ U' ↔ P ∈ S ∧ P ∉ T := fun P => Finset.mem_filter
  haveI : ∀ j : U', Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (j.1.idealSheaf) :=
    fun j => hECD j.1
  have hBcoef : ∀ Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X,
      (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X).coeff Q =
        ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
          (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸ IdealSheafData.stalk I Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) +
        ∑ j : U', ((Module.length (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint)
          (X.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
            IdealSheafData.stalk (j.1.idealSheaf) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) := by
    intro Q
    rw [hlen Q]
    simp_rw [length_stalk_idealSheaf _ Q (hECD _)]
    rw [Finset.sum_coe_sort U' (fun P => if Q = P then (1 : ℤ) else 0)]
    change (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Divisor X) Q = _
    rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq, sum_single_one_apply S Q]
    by_cases hQT : Q ∈ T
    · simp [hQT, hTS hQT, hU']
    · by_cases hQS : Q ∈ S <;> simp [hQT, hQS, hU']
  obtain ⟨hcomapC, hsmooth, E, hE, hEsnc, hE1⟩ :=
    isSNC_ramifiedCyclicCover_comap_of_isSNC k f (-D).divisorialSheaf m hm σ hσ hsmD hne
      (fun j : U' => j.1.idealSheaf) (∑ P ∈ S, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) hBcoef hS
      (coeff_sum_single_one_of_mem_support S)
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (g ≫ f) := hvarY
  haveI : Smooth (g ≫ f) := hsmY
  haveI : IsFinite g := hfin
  haveI : Surjective g := hsurj
  haveI : IsSmoothVariety k (g ≫ f) := (isSmoothVariety_iff k _).mpr ⟨hvarY, hsmY⟩
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (g ≫ f)
  haveI : IsNormal Y := isNormal_of_smooth_over_field (g ≫ f)
  haveI : CompactSpace Y := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (g ≫ f)
  haveI : IsIntegral Y := hvarY.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsNoetherian Y := ⟨⟩
  obtain ⟨hcartY, -⟩ := MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartier_weil_dictionary_of_isSmoothVariety k (g ≫ f)
  have hgen : ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (C : irreducibleComponents Y),
      g (componentGenericPoint Y C) ∉ DivisorWithCoeffs.supp (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) :=
    fun P => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g _
  -- the colengths along the prime divisors `Q` of `Y` of `g⁻¹ P`, of `R = g⁻¹(D₀)_red` and of
  -- `g⁻¹ D₀`
  set ℓ : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y → ℤ := fun P Q =>
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint) (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) with hℓ
  set ℓJ : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y → ℤ := fun Q =>
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint) (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk J Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) with hℓJ
  set ℓI : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y → ℤ := fun Q =>
    ((Module.length (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint) (Y.presheaf.stalk Q.genericPoint ⧸
      IdealSheafData.stalk (I.comap g) Q.genericPoint)).toNat : ℤ) with hℓI
  have hEℓ : ∀ Q, E Q = ℓJ Q + ∑ P ∈ U', ℓ P Q := fun Q => by
    rw [← Finset.sum_coe_sort U']; exact hE Q
  have hE01 : ∀ Q, E Q = 0 ∨ E Q = 1 := fun Q => by
    by_cases hQ : Q ∈ E.support
    · exact Or.inr (hE1 Q hQ)
    · exact Or.inl (Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hQ)
  have hℓ0 : ∀ P Q, 0 ≤ ℓ P Q := fun P Q => Int.natCast_nonneg _
  have hℓJ0 : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ ℓJ Q := fun Q => Int.natCast_nonneg _
  have hmJ : ∀ Q, ℓI Q = m * ℓJ Q := fun Q => by
    simp only [hℓI, hℓJ]
    rw [hJpow, MMP.Resolution.Aux.stalk_pow, length_stalk_pow J hJ Q m]
  have hst' := exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_of_forall_mem_ideal_iff I T hTdisj hI
  have hcomapP : ∀ Q, ∀ P ∈ T, g Q.genericPoint ∈ P.support → ℓI Q = ℓ P Q := by
    intro Q P hP hx
    rcases hst' (g Q.genericPoint) with ⟨P', hP', hx', W, hxW, hW⟩ | ⟨hnot, -⟩
    · have hPP : P' = P := by
        by_contra hne
        exact Set.disjoint_left.mp (hTdisj P' hP' P hP hne) hx' hx
      subst hPP
      simp only [hℓI, hℓ]
      rw [stalk_comap_eq_of_ideal_eq g W hW hxW]
    · exact absurd hx (hnot P hP)
  have hcomapTop : ∀ Q, (∀ P ∈ T, g Q.genericPoint ∉ P.support) → ℓI Q = 0 := by
    intro Q hnot
    rcases hst' (g Q.genericPoint) with ⟨P', hP', hx', -⟩ | ⟨-, W, hxW, hW⟩
    · exact absurd hx' (hnot P' hP')
    · simp only [hℓI]
      rw [stalk_comap_eq_of_ideal_eq g W (J := ⊤) (by rw [hW]; simp) hxW,
        Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_top, MMP.Resolution.Aux.stalk_top]
      exact length_quotient_top_toNat _
  have hℓJ_zero : ∀ Q, ℓI Q = 0 → ℓJ Q = 0 := fun Q h => by
    have h' := hmJ Q
    rw [h] at h'
    exact (mul_eq_zero.mp h'.symm).resolve_left (by exact_mod_cast hm0.ne')
  have hℓnot : ∀ Q P, g Q.genericPoint ∉ P.support → ℓ P Q = 0 := by
    intro Q P hx
    simp only [hℓ]
    rw [(IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mpr (by
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap])]
    exact length_quotient_top_toNat _
  have hℓJE : ∀ Q, ℓJ Q ≤ E Q := fun Q => by
    rw [hEℓ]; have := Finset.sum_nonneg (fun P (_ : P ∈ U') => hℓ0 P Q); omega
  have hℓE : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ Q, ℓ P Q ≤ E Q := fun P hP Q => by
    rw [hEℓ]; have := Finset.single_le_sum (fun P _ => hℓ0 P Q) hP; have := hℓJ0 Q; omega
  have hFsupp1 : ∀ (P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (Q : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Y),
      (if g Q.genericPoint ∈ P.support then ℓJ Q else 0) ≠ 0 → Q ∈ E.support := by
    intro P Q h
    refine Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr fun h0 => h ?_
    have := hℓJE Q; have := hℓJ0 Q
    split_ifs <;> omega
  have hFsupp2 : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ Q, ℓ P Q ≠ 0 → Q ∈ E.support := fun P hP Q h =>
    Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr fun h0 => h (by have := hℓE P hP Q; have := hℓ0 P Q; omega)
  let F : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → Divisor Y := fun P =>
    if P ∈ T then Finsupp.onFinset E.support
      (fun Q => if g Q.genericPoint ∈ P.support then ℓJ Q else 0) (hFsupp1 P)
    else if hP' : P ∈ U' then Finsupp.onFinset E.support (ℓ P) (hFsupp2 P hP') else 0
  have hFT : ∀ P ∈ T, ∀ Q, F P Q = if g Q.genericPoint ∈ P.support then ℓJ Q else 0 :=
    fun P hP Q => by simp only [F, if_pos hP, Finsupp.onFinset_apply]
  have hFU : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ Q, F P Q = ℓ P Q := fun P hP Q => by
    simp only [F, if_neg ((hU' P).mp hP).2, dif_pos hP, Finsupp.onFinset_apply]
  have hsumT : ∀ Q, ∑ P ∈ T, F P Q = ℓJ Q := by
    intro Q
    by_cases hx : ∃ P ∈ T, g Q.genericPoint ∈ P.support
    · obtain ⟨P, hP, hxP⟩ := hx
      rw [Finset.sum_eq_single P (fun P' hP' hne => by
          rw [hFT P' hP', if_neg (fun h => Set.disjoint_left.mp (hTdisj P' hP' P hP hne) h hxP)])
        (fun h => absurd hP h), hFT P hP, if_pos hxP]
    · push Not at hx
      rw [Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun P hP => by rw [hFT P hP, if_neg (hx P hP)])]
      exact (hℓJ_zero Q (hcomapTop Q hx)).symm
  have hsumE' : ∀ Q, ∑ P ∈ S, F P Q = E Q := by
    intro Q
    rw [← Finset.sum_filter_add_sum_filter_not S (· ∈ T), Finset.filter_mem_eq_inter,
      Finset.inter_eq_right.mpr hTS, hsumT, hEℓ]
    congr 1
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun P hP => hFU P hP Q
  have hsumE : ∑ P ∈ S, F P = E := Finsupp.ext fun Q => by
    rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]; exact hsumE' Q
  have hR : ∀ Q, (∑ P ∈ T, F P) Q = ℓJ Q := fun Q => by
    rw [Finsupp.finset_sum_apply]; exact hsumT Q
  have hF0 : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, 0 ≤ F P Q := by
    intro P hP Q
    by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
    · rw [hFT P hPT]; split_ifs; exacts [hℓJ0 Q, le_rfl]
    · rw [hFU P ((hU' P).mpr ⟨hP, hPT⟩)]; exact hℓ0 P Q
  have hFle : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, F P Q ≤ E Q := fun P hP Q => by
    rw [← hsumE']; exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun P hP => hF0 P hP Q) hP
  have hF01 : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, F P Q = 0 ∨ F P Q = 1 := fun P hP Q => by
    have := hFle P hP Q; have := hF0 P hP Q; rcases hE01 Q with h | h <;> omega
  have hFdisj : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, P ≠ P' → ∀ Q, F P Q = 0 ∨ F P' Q = 0 := by
    intro P hP P' hP' hne Q
    have hsub : ({P, P'} : Finset _) ⊆ S := by
      intro x hx; rw [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hx
      rcases hx with rfl | rfl <;> assumption
    have h2 := Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg hsub (fun P hP _ => hF0 P hP Q)
    rw [Finset.sum_pair hne, hsumE'] at h2
    have := hF0 P hP Q; have := hF0 P' hP' Q; rcases hE01 Q with h | h <;> omega
  -- the components off the branch divisor
  have hreg : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ y ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support, ∃ (n : ℕ)
      (w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin n), MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧
        IdealSheafData.stalk (P.idealSheaf.comap g) y = Ideal.span {w j} :=
    fun P hP => exists_regularParameter_of_smooth (g ≫ f) _ (hcomapC ⟨P, hP⟩)
      (hsmooth ⟨P, hP⟩ ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mp
        (hS.1 P (mem_support_sum_single_one ((hU' P).mp hP).1))))
  have hmemsupp : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ Q, Q ∈ (F P).support ↔
      Q.genericPoint ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support := by
    intro P hP Q
    rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, hFU P hP Q, ← length_stalk_ne_zero_iff _ (hcomapC ⟨P, hP⟩) Q]
    simp only [hℓ, ne_eq, Nat.cast_eq_zero]
    exact Iff.rfl
  have hsub : ∀ P ∈ U', ∀ Q ∈ (F P).support, Q.support ⊆ g ⁻¹' P.support :=
    fun P hP Q hQ y hy => by
      have := support_subset_of_genericPoint_mem _ ((hmemsupp P hP Q).mp hQ) hy
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap] at this
  -- the branch divisor `J` is smooth, hence cut out by regular parameters
  have hregJ : ∀ y ∈ J.support, ∃ (n : ℕ) (w : Fin n → Y.presheaf.stalk y) (j : Fin n),
      MMP.Mori.IsRegularSystemOfParameters w ∧ IdealSheafData.stalk J y = Ideal.span {w j} :=
    exists_regularParameter_of_smooth (g ≫ f) J hJ ((isSmoothScheme_iff _).mp hJsm)
  have hFne : ∀ P ∈ S, F P ≠ 0 := by
    intro P hP h0
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hsurj.surj P.genericPoint
    by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
    · have hηI : P.genericPoint ∈ I.support := by
        by_contra hn
        have htop := (IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support I _).mpr hn
        rcases hst P.genericPoint with ⟨P', -, hmem, heq⟩ | ⟨hnot, -⟩
        · rw [heq] at htop
          exact ((IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mp htop) hmem
        · exact hnot P hPT (primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support P)
      have hyJ : y ∈ J.support := by
        by_contra hyn
        have htop := (IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support J y).mpr hyn
        have h' : IdealSheafData.stalk (I.comap g) y = ⊤ := by
          rw [hJpow, MMP.Resolution.Aux.stalk_pow, htop, Ideal.top_pow]
        refine (IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support _ _).mp h' ?_
        rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
        change g y ∈ I.support
        rw [show g y = P.genericPoint from hy]
        exact hηI
      obtain ⟨Q, hηQ, hyQ⟩ := exists_primeDivisor_of_regularParameter _ hregJ hyJ
      have hℓJQ : ℓJ Q ≠ 0 := by
        simp only [hℓJ, ne_eq, Nat.cast_eq_zero]
        exact (length_stalk_ne_zero_iff J hJ Q).mpr hηQ
      have hspec : Q.genericPoint ⤳ y := by
        rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure] at hyQ
        exact specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hyQ
      have hspec' : g Q.genericPoint ⤳ P.genericPoint := by
        rw [← show g y = P.genericPoint from hy]
        exact g.base.hom.map_specializes hspec
      have hx : ∃ P' ∈ T, g Q.genericPoint ∈ P'.support := by
        by_contra hx
        push Not at hx
        exact hℓJQ (hℓJ_zero Q (hcomapTop Q hx))
      obtain ⟨P', hP', hxP'⟩ := hx
      have hηP' : P.genericPoint ∈ P'.support :=
        hspec'.mem_closed P'.idealSheaf.support.isClosed hxP'
      have hPP : P' = P := by
        by_contra hne
        exact Set.disjoint_left.mp (hTdisj P' hP' P hPT hne) hηP'
          (primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support P)
      subst hPP
      have h1 : F P' Q = ℓJ Q := by rw [hFT P' hPT, if_pos hxP']
      rw [h0] at h1
      exact hℓJQ (by simpa using h1.symm)
    · have hPU : P ∈ U' := (hU' P).mpr ⟨hP, hPT⟩
      obtain ⟨Q, hηQ, -⟩ := exists_primeDivisor_of_regularParameter _ (hreg P hPU)
        (show y ∈ (P.idealSheaf.comap g).support by
          rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
          change g y ∈ P.support
          rw [show g y = P.genericPoint from hy]
          exact primeDivisor_genericPoint_mem_support P)
      simpa [h0] using (hmemsupp P hPU Q).mpr hηQ
  refine ⟨Y, g, hfin, hsurj, isProjectiveVariety_comp_of_isFinite f g ‹_›, hsmY, inferInstance,
    inferInstance, inferInstance, F, hgen,
    fun P hP => isPullback_single_of_comap hloc g P (hgen P) _ (fun Q => ?_),
    fun P hP => ⟨hFne P hP, hF01 P hP⟩, ?_, ?_, by rw [hsumE]; exact hEsnc, fun B => ?_⟩
  · -- `g^*P = m F_P` on the branch divisor, `F_P` off it
    change ((if P ∈ T then (m : ℤ) else 1) • F P) Q = ℓ P Q
    by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
    · rw [if_pos hPT, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, hFT P hPT]
      split_ifs with hx
      · rw [← hmJ, hcomapP Q P hPT hx]
      · rw [mul_zero, hℓnot Q P hx]
    · rw [if_neg hPT, one_smul, hFU P ((hU' P).mpr ⟨hP, hPT⟩)]
  · intro P hP P' hP' hne
    refine Finset.disjoint_left.mpr fun Q hQ hQ' => ?_
    rcases hFdisj P hP P' hP' hne Q with h | h
    · exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ h
    · exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ' h
  · intro P hP P' hP' hPT hP'T hPP Q hQ Q' hQ' hne
    have hPU : P ∈ U' := (hU' P).mpr ⟨hP, hPT⟩
    have hP'U : P' ∈ U' := (hU' P').mpr ⟨hP', hP'T⟩
    rcases hPP with rfl | hdisj
    · exact disjoint_support_of_regularParameter _ (hreg P hPU) ((hmemsupp P hPU Q).mp hQ)
        ((hmemsupp P hP'U Q').mp hQ') hne
    · exact (hdisj.preimage g).mono (hsub P hPU Q hQ) (hsub P' hP'U Q' hQ')
  · -- the cohomology clause
    have hBp := map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g B
    obtain ⟨B', hpB⟩ := (hcart B).exists_isPullback hBp
    refine ⟨hBp, B', hpB, fun b hb0 hbm i => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨D'', hpD⟩ := (hcart D).exists_isPullback
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g D)
    have hRlin : (∑ P ∈ T, F P).LinearlyEquivalent D'' := by
      obtain ⟨e1⟩ := nonempty_divisorialSheaf_iso_invertibleSheaf'_of_length J hJ _ (hcartY _) hR
      obtain ⟨e2⟩ := nonempty_divisorialSheaf_iso_dualSheaf_neg hcart D
      exact MMP.Flips.linearlyEquivalent_of_divisorialSheaf_iso (e1 ≪≫ eJ ≪≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pullback g).mapIso e2.symm ≪≫
        (hpD.divisorialSheafIso (hBc := hcart D)).symm)
    obtain ⟨r⟩ := nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_cyclicCover_divisor (m := m) k hcart f D σ
      hm0 hpD hRlin B hpB ⟨b.toNat, by omega⟩ i
    have hb : (((⟨b.toNat, by omega⟩ : Fin m) : ℕ) : ℤ) = b := Int.toNat_of_nonneg hb0
    rw [hb] at r
    exact ⟨r⟩

/-- **The cyclic cover stage.** With `Δ`, `a = b / m` and the partition `G` as in
`exists_cover_clearing_group`, suppose the smooth reduced sum `D₀` of the first group is
linearly equivalent to `m D`. The cyclic cover `p : X₂ ⟶ X` of degree `m` branched along `D₀`
(for the section of `𝒪(m D) ≅ 𝒪(D₀)` cutting out `D₀`) is finite surjective from a smooth
projective variety, `p^*D₀ = m R` with `R = p⁻¹(D₀)_red`, so `p^*Δ = Δ₂ + b R` with `Δ₂` snc
with coefficients in `[0, 1)` among those of `Δ`, the pull-backs of the remaining groups
partitioning its components with coefficient `a`; and `H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` is a retract of
`H^i(X₂, 𝒪(-(p^*B - b R)))`, the summand `j = b` of
`p_* 𝒪(-(p^*B - b R)) ≅ ⊕_{j < m} 𝒪(-B + (b - j) D)`. -/
public theorem exists_cyclic_cover_stage
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] [CompactSpace X] (Δ : QDivisor X) (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (hΔ01 : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    {a : ℚ} (ha : a ≠ 0) {s : ℕ} (G : Fin (s + 1) → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hG : IsLevelPartition Δ a G) (D : Divisor X)
    (hD : Divisor.LinearlyEquivalent (∑ P ∈ G 0, Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) ((a.den : ℤ) • D)) :
    ∃ (X₂ : Scheme.{u}) (p : X₂ ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₂) (_ : IsNormal X₂)
      (R : Divisor X₂) (Δ₂ : QDivisor X₂) (G₂ : Fin s → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂))
      (hΔp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂, p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ Δ.supp),
      Δ.IsPullback p hΔp (Δ₂ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor R) ∧ Δ₂.IsSNC (p ≫ f) ∧
      (∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂, 0 ≤ Δ₂.coeff P ∧ Δ₂.coeff P < 1) ∧
      Δ₂.frange ⊆ Δ.frange ∧ IsLevelPartition Δ₂ a G₂ ∧
      ∀ B : Divisor X, ∃ (hBp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂,
          p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ B.supp) (B' : Divisor X₂),
        B.IsPullback p hBp B' ∧
        ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
          (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-(B' - a.num • R)).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  classical
  have hsmX : IsSmoothScheme f := (isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance
  have hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X, D.IsCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  have hq : ∀ D : QDivisor X, D.IsQCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  have hTS' : ∀ i, ∀ P ∈ G i, P ∈ Δ.support := fun _ _ => hG.mem_support ha
  have hTS : G 0 ⊆ Δ.support := fun _ => hG.mem_support ha
  have hS := isSNC_sum_single_support hΔ
  -- `0 < a < 1`, so `0 < b < m` and `2 ≤ m`
  obtain ⟨P₀, hP₀⟩ := hG.2.2.2 0
  have haP₀ : Δ.coeff P₀ = a := (hG.1 P₀).mpr ⟨0, hP₀⟩
  have ha0 : 0 < a := lt_of_le_of_ne (haP₀ ▸ (hΔ01 P₀).1) (Ne.symm ha)
  have ha1 : a < 1 := haP₀ ▸ (hΔ01 P₀).2
  have hnum0 : 0 < a.num := Rat.num_pos.mpr ha0
  have hnumden : a.num < a.den := by
    have : (a.num : ℚ) < a.den := by
      rw [← Rat.mul_den_eq_num a]
      exact (mul_lt_iff_lt_one_left (by exact_mod_cast a.den_pos)).mpr ha1
    exact_mod_cast this
  have hm : 2 ≤ a.den := by omega
  obtain ⟨Y, g, _, _, hproj, hsm, _, _, _, F, hgen, hpb, hred, hdisj, hdisjQ, hsnc, hcoh⟩ :=
    exists_cyclic_cover_divisors k f Δ.support (G 0) hTS ⟨P₀, hP₀⟩ hS (hG.2.2.1 0) a.den hm D hD
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (g ≫ f) := hproj
  set S := Δ.support
  set T := G 0
  set c' : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X → ℚ := fun P => if P ∈ T then 0 else Δ P with hc'
  set Δ₂ : QDivisor Y := ∑ P ∈ S, c' P • Divisor.toQDivisor (F P) with hΔ₂
  have hred' : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ Q, F P Q = 0 ∨ F P Q = 1 := fun P hP => (hred P hP).2
  have key : ∀ Q, (∃ P ∈ S, Q ∈ (F P).support ∧ Δ₂ Q = c' P) ∨
      ((∀ P ∈ S, Q ∉ (F P).support) ∧ Δ₂ Q = 0) := by
    intro Q
    by_cases h : ∃ P ∈ S, Q ∈ (F P).support
    · obtain ⟨P, hP, hQ⟩ := h
      exact Or.inl ⟨P, hP, hQ, sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply S _ F hred' hdisj hP hQ⟩
    · push Not at h
      exact Or.inr ⟨h, sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply_of_notMem S _ F h⟩
  have huniq : ∀ P ∈ S, ∀ P' ∈ S, ∀ Q, Q ∈ (F P).support → Q ∈ (F P').support → P = P' :=
    fun P hP P' hP' Q h h' => by
      by_contra hne
      exact Finset.disjoint_left.mp (hdisj P hP P' hP' hne) h h'
  have hnotT : ∀ (i : Fin s), ∀ P ∈ G i.succ, P ∉ T := fun i P hP hPT =>
    Fin.succ_ne_zero i (hG.2.1 _ _ P hP hPT)
  have hterm : ∀ P ∈ S, Δ P • Divisor.toQDivisor ((if P ∈ T then (a.den : ℤ) else 1) • F P) =
      c' P • Divisor.toQDivisor (F P) +
        (if P ∈ T then a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor (F P) else 0) := by
    intro P _
    by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
    · have hΔP : Δ P = a := (hG.1 P).mpr ⟨0, hPT⟩
      simp only [hc', if_pos hPT, zero_smul, zero_add, map_zsmul, hΔP]
      rw [← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℚ, ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℚ, smul_smul]
      congr 1
      push_cast
      exact Rat.mul_den_eq_num a
    · simp [hc', hPT]
  have heq : ∑ P ∈ S, Δ P • Divisor.toQDivisor ((if P ∈ T then (a.den : ℤ) else 1) • F P) =
      Δ₂ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor (∑ P ∈ T, F P) := by
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hterm, Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.sum_filter,
      Finset.filter_mem_eq_inter, Finset.inter_eq_right.mpr hTS, map_sum, Finset.smul_sum]
  have hpΔ : Δ.IsPullback g
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g Δ)
      (Δ₂ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor (∑ P ∈ T, F P)) :=
    qDivisor_isPullback_congr _ (qDivisor_isPullback_sum_smul g hcart hq S (fun P => Δ P)
      (fun P => (if P ∈ T then (a.den : ℤ) else 1) • F P) hpb
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' g _))
      (qDivisor_eq_sum_smul_single Δ).symm heq
  refine ⟨Y, g, inferInstance, inferInstance, hproj, hsm, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    ∑ P ∈ T, F P, Δ₂, fun i => (G i.succ).biUnion fun P => (F P).support, _, hpΔ, ?_, ?_, ?_,
    ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩, fun B => ?_⟩
  · refine hsnc.of_support_subset fun Q hQ => ?_
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, hQP, -⟩ | ⟨-, h0⟩
    · exact Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr (by
        rw [sum_apply_of_mem_support S F hred' hdisj hP hQP]; exact one_ne_zero)
    · exact absurd h0 (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hQ)
  · intro Q
    change 0 ≤ Δ₂ Q ∧ Δ₂ Q < 1
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, -, -, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
    · rw [h]
      by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
      · simp only [hc', if_pos hPT]; norm_num
      · simp only [hc', if_neg hPT]; exact hΔ01 P
    · rw [h]; norm_num
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨hx0, Q, rfl⟩ := Finsupp.mem_frange.mp hx
    rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, -, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
    · by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
      · exact absurd (h.trans (by simp only [hc', if_pos hPT])) hx0
      · rw [h]; simp only [hc', if_neg hPT]
        exact Finsupp.mem_frange.mpr ⟨Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mp hP, P, rfl⟩
    · exact absurd h hx0
  · intro Q
    constructor
    · intro hQ
      rcases key Q with ⟨P, hP, hQP, h⟩ | ⟨-, h⟩
      · have hval : c' P = a := h.symm.trans hQ
        by_cases hPT : P ∈ T
        · simp only [hc', if_pos hPT] at hval; exact absurd hval.symm ha
        · simp only [hc', if_neg hPT] at hval
          obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := (hG.1 P).mp hval
          have hj0 : j ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hPT (by subst h0; exact hj)
          obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := Fin.exists_succ_eq.mpr hj0
          exact ⟨i, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨P, hj, hQP⟩⟩
      · exact absurd ((show Δ₂ Q = a from hQ).symm.trans h) ha
    · rintro ⟨i, hi⟩
      obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hi
      have hPS : P ∈ S := hTS' _ P hPi
      change Δ₂ Q = a
      rw [sum_smul_toQDivisor_apply S _ F hred' hdisj hPS hQP]
      simp only [hc', if_neg (hnotT i P hPi)]
      exact (hG.1 P).mpr ⟨i.succ, hPi⟩
  · intro i j Q hi hj
    obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hi
    obtain ⟨P', hPj, hQP'⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hj
    have := huniq P (hTS' _ P hPi) P' (hTS' _ P' hPj) Q hQP hQP'
    subst this
    exact Fin.succ_injective _ (hG.2.1 _ _ P hPi hPj)
  · intro i Q hQ Q' hQ' hne
    obtain ⟨P, hPi, hQP⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hQ
    obtain ⟨P', hPi', hQP'⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hQ'
    refine hdisjQ P (hTS' _ P hPi) P' (hTS' _ P' hPi') (hnotT i P hPi) (hnotT i P' hPi') ?_
      Q hQP Q' hQP' hne
    by_cases hPP : P = P'
    · exact Or.inl hPP
    · exact Or.inr (hG.2.2.1 _ P hPi P' hPi' hPP)
  · intro i
    obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := hG.2.2.2 i.succ
    obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.mpr (hred P (hTS' _ P hP)).1
    exact ⟨Q, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨P, hP, hQ⟩⟩
  · obtain ⟨hBp, B', hpB, hr⟩ := hcoh B
    exact ⟨hBp, B', hpB, fun i => hr a.num hnum0.le (by exact_mod_cast hnumden) i⟩

/-- **The two covers for one group.** Let `Δ` be an snc `ℚ`-divisor on the smooth projective
variety `X` with coefficients in `[0, 1)`, `a = b / m` a non-zero coefficient, and `G` a partition
of the components with coefficient `a` into groups of pairwise disjoint components. Let `D₀` be
the (smooth, reduced) sum of the first group. A Bloch–Gieseker cover `p₁` making `𝒪(D₀)` an
`m`-th power `𝒪(m D)`, followed by the cyclic cover `p₂` branched along the smooth divisor
`p₁⁻¹ D₀`, gives `p = p₁ p₂ : X₂ ⟶ X` finite surjective from a smooth projective variety and the
reduced divisor `R = p⁻¹(D₀)_red` with `p^*Δ = Δ₂ + b R`. Here `Δ₂` is snc with coefficients in
`[0, 1)` among those of `Δ`, and the pull-backs of the remaining groups partition its components
with coefficient `a`. For every divisor `B` on `X`, `H^i(X, 𝒪(-B))` is a retract of
`H^i(X₂, 𝒪(-(p^*B - b R)))`, the summand `j = b` of
`p₂_* 𝒪(-(p^*B - bR)) = ⊕_{j < m} 𝒪(-p₁^*B + (b - j) D)`. -/
public theorem exists_cover_clearing_group
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (Δ : QDivisor X) (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (hΔ01 : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    {a : ℚ} (ha : a ≠ 0) {s : ℕ} (G : Fin (s + 1) → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (hG : IsLevelPartition Δ a G) :
    ∃ (X₂ : Scheme.{u}) (p : X₂ ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₂) (_ : IsNormal X₂)
      (R : Divisor X₂) (Δ₂ : QDivisor X₂) (G₂ : Fin s → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂))
      (hΔp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂, p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ Δ.supp),
      Δ.IsPullback p hΔp (Δ₂ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor R) ∧ Δ₂.IsSNC (p ≫ f) ∧
      (∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂, 0 ≤ Δ₂.coeff P ∧ Δ₂.coeff P < 1) ∧
      Δ₂.frange ⊆ Δ.frange ∧ IsLevelPartition Δ₂ a G₂ ∧
      ∀ B : Divisor X, ∃ (hBp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂,
          p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ B.supp) (B' : Divisor X₂),
        B.IsPullback p hBp B' ∧
        ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
          (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-(B' - a.num • R)).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  obtain ⟨X₁, p, _, _, hproj, hsm, _, _, _, Δ₁, G₁, D, hΔp, hpΔ, hΔ₁, hΔ₁01, hsub, hG₁,
    hD⟩ := exists_bloch_gieseker_stage k f Δ hΔ hΔ01 ha G hG
  have hcoh : ∀ B : Divisor X, ∃ (hBp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₁,
      p (componentGenericPoint X₁ C) ∉ B.supp) (B' : Divisor X₁), B.IsPullback p hBp B' ∧
      ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
        (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-B').divisorialSheaf i)) := by
    intro B
    haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f) := hproj
    haveI : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace f
    have hBc : B.IsCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme
      ((isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance) B
    have hBp := map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' p B
    obtain ⟨B', hpB⟩ := hBc.exists_isPullback hBp
    exact ⟨hBp, B', hpB, nonempty_retract_cohomologyOverField_divisorialSheaf_neg k f p hBc hpB⟩
  obtain ⟨X₂, q, _, _, hproj₂, hsm₂, _, _, R, Δ₂, G₂, hΔq, hqΔ, hΔ₂, hΔ₂01, hsub₂, hG₂,
    hcoh₂⟩ := exists_cyclic_cover_stage k (p ≫ f) Δ₁ hΔ₁ hΔ₁01 ha G₁ hG₁ D hD
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f) := hproj
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (q ≫ p ≫ f) := hproj₂
  obtain ⟨hM', hcomp⟩ := covering_trick_comp p q hpΔ hqΔ
  refine ⟨X₂, q ≫ p, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_, ?_, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    R, Δ₂, G₂, hM', hcomp, ?_, hΔ₂01, hsub₂.trans hsub, hG₂, fun B => ?_⟩
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hproj₂
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hsm₂
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hΔ₂
  · obtain ⟨hBp, B₁, hpB, hret⟩ := hcoh B
    obtain ⟨hBq, B₂, hqB, hret₂⟩ := hcoh₂ B₁
    refine ⟨map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant'
      (q ≫ p) B, B₂, MMP.ProgramBaseChange.divisor_isPullback_comp rfl hpB hqB _, fun i => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨r₁⟩ := hret i
    obtain ⟨r₂⟩ := hret₂ i
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    exact ⟨r₁.trans r₂⟩

/-- **Clearing one coefficient**, by induction on the number of groups of a partition of the
components with that coefficient into groups of pairwise disjoint components. -/
public theorem exists_cover_clearing_partition (s : ℕ) :
    ∀ (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (Δ : QDivisor X) (_ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (_ : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    {a : ℚ} (_ : a ≠ 0) (G : Fin s → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X))
    (_ : IsLevelPartition Δ a G),
    ∃ (X₂ : Scheme.{u}) (p : X₂ ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₂) (_ : IsNormal X₂)
      (R : Divisor X₂) (Δ₂ : QDivisor X₂)
      (hΔp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂, p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ Δ.supp),
      Δ.IsPullback p hΔp (Δ₂ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor R) ∧ Δ₂.IsSNC (p ≫ f) ∧
      (∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂, 0 ≤ Δ₂.coeff P ∧ Δ₂.coeff P < 1) ∧
      Δ₂.frange ⊆ Δ.frange.erase a ∧
      ∀ B : Divisor X, ∃ (hBp : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂,
          p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ B.supp) (B' : Divisor X₂),
        B.IsPullback p hBp B' ∧
        ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
          (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-(B' - a.num • R)).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  induction s with
  | zero =>
    intro k _ _ _ X f _ _ _ _ Δ hΔ hΔ01 a ha G hG
    have e0 : Δ + a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor (0 : Divisor X) = Δ := by simp
    have hgΔ : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X, (𝟙 X) (componentGenericPoint X C) ∉ Δ.supp :=
      fun C => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant'
        (𝟙 X) Δ C
    refine ⟨X, 𝟙 X, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_, ?_, inferInstance, inferInstance, 0, Δ,
      hgΔ, qDivisor_isPullback_congr hgΔ (qDivisor_isPullback_id Δ hgΔ) rfl e0.symm, ?_, hΔ01, ?_,
      fun B => ⟨fun C => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant'
        (𝟙 X) B C, B, divisor_isPullback_id B _, fun i => ?_⟩⟩
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp] using ‹MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f›
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp] using ‹Smooth f›
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp] using hΔ
    · intro x hx
      refine Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨?_, hx⟩
      rintro rfl
      obtain ⟨-, P, hP⟩ := Finsupp.mem_frange.mp hx
      obtain ⟨i, -⟩ := (hG.1 P).mp hP
      exact i.elim0
    · simp only [Category.id_comp, smul_zero, sub_zero]
      exact ⟨Retract.refl _⟩
  | succ s ih =>
    intro k _ _ _ X f _ _ _ _ Δ hΔ hΔ01 a ha G hG
    obtain ⟨X₂, p, _, _, hproj, hsm, _, _, R, Δ₂, G₂, hΔp, hpΔ, hΔ₂, hΔ₂01, hsub, hG₂, hcoh⟩ :=
      exists_cover_clearing_group k f Δ hΔ hΔ01 ha G hG
    obtain ⟨X₃, q, _, _, hproj₃, hsm₃, _, _, R', Δ₃, hΔq, hqΔ, hΔ₃, hΔ₃01, hsub₃, hcoh₃⟩ :=
      ih k (p ≫ f) Δ₂ hΔ₂ hΔ₂01 ha G₂ hG₂
    haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f) := hproj
    haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (q ≫ p ≫ f) := hproj₃
    haveI : CompactSpace X₃ := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (q ≫ p ≫ f)
    have hsmX₂ : IsSmoothScheme (p ≫ f) := (isSmoothScheme_iff (p ≫ f)).mpr hsm
    have hcart : ∀ D : Divisor X₂, D.IsCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX₂
    have hq₂ : ∀ D : QDivisor X₂, D.IsQCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX₂
    obtain ⟨Rq, hRq⟩ := (hcart R).exists_isPullback (f := q)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q R)
    have hbR : (a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor R).IsPullback q
        (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _)
        (a.num • Divisor.toQDivisor Rq) :=
      qDivisor_isPullback_congr _ (QDivisor.isPullback_toQDivisor (hcart _)
        (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _)
        (hRq.zsmul (hcart R) a.num
          (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _)))
        (map_zsmul _ _ _) (map_zsmul _ _ _)
    have hq := qDivisor_isPullback_add q (hq₂ Δ₂) (hq₂ _)
      (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _) hqΔ hbR
    obtain ⟨hM', hcomp⟩ := covering_trick_comp p q hpΔ hq
    refine ⟨X₃, q ≫ p, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_, ?_, inferInstance, inferInstance,
      R' + Rq, Δ₃, hM', qDivisor_isPullback_congr _ hcomp rfl
        (by rw [map_add, smul_add, add_assoc]), ?_, hΔ₃01,
      hsub₃.trans (Finset.erase_subset_erase a hsub), fun B => ?_⟩
    · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hproj₃
    · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hsm₃
    · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hΔ₃
    · obtain ⟨hBp, B', hpB, hret⟩ := hcoh B
      obtain ⟨hBq, B'', hqB, hret₃⟩ := hcoh₃ (B' - a.num • R)
      have h1 : B'.IsPullback q
          (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q B')
          (B'' + a.num • Rq) :=
        (Divisor.IsPullback.add (hcart _) (hcart _)
          (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _) hqB
          (hRq.zsmul (hcart R) a.num
            (map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' q _))
          ).of_eq (sub_add_cancel B' (a.num • R))
      refine ⟨map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant'
        (q ≫ p) B, B'' + a.num • Rq,
        MMP.ProgramBaseChange.divisor_isPullback_comp rfl hpB h1 _, fun i => ?_⟩
      have e : B'' + a.num • Rq - a.num • (R' + Rq) = B'' - a.num • R' := by
        rw [smul_add]; abel
      obtain ⟨r₁⟩ := hret i
      obtain ⟨r₂⟩ := hret₃ i
      rw [e]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      exact ⟨r₁.trans r₂⟩

/-- **One step of the covering trick.** For a non-zero coefficient `a = b / m` of `Δ`, the
components of `Δ` with coefficient `a`, taken one at a time, are removed by a Bloch–Gieseker cover
followed by a cyclic cover (`exists_cover_clearing_partition`). This keeps all hypotheses, lowers
the number of distinct coefficients, and keeps the cohomology of `𝒪(-B)` as a retract. -/
public theorem covering_trick_step
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (B : Divisor X) (M Δ : QDivisor X) (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (hΔ01 : ∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    (hB : (Divisor.toQDivisor B).NumericallyEquivalent k f (M + Δ)) (hΔ0 : Δ ≠ 0) :
    ∃ (X₂ : Scheme.{u}) (p : X₂ ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₂) (_ : IsNormal X₂)
      (B₂ : Divisor X₂) (M₂ Δ₂ : QDivisor X₂)
      (hM : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents X₂, p (componentGenericPoint X₂ C) ∉ M.supp),
      M.IsPullback p hM M₂ ∧ Δ₂.IsSNC (p ≫ f) ∧
      (∀ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X₂, 0 ≤ Δ₂.coeff P ∧ Δ₂.coeff P < 1) ∧
      Δ₂.frange.card < Δ.frange.card ∧
      (Divisor.toQDivisor B₂).NumericallyEquivalent k (p ≫ f) (M₂ + Δ₂) ∧
      ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
        (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-B₂).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨P₀, hP₀⟩ : ∃ P, Δ P ≠ 0 := by
    by_contra! h
    exact hΔ0 (Finsupp.ext h)
  set a := Δ P₀
  have ha : a ∈ Δ.frange := Finsupp.mem_frange.mpr ⟨hP₀, P₀, rfl⟩
  -- the components with coefficient `a`, each in a group of its own
  set S := Δ.support.filter (fun P => Δ P = a)
  let e := S.equivFin
  let G : Fin S.card → Finset (MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor X) := fun i => {(e.symm i : S).1}
  have hG : IsLevelPartition Δ a G := by
    refine ⟨fun P => ⟨fun hP => ?_, ?_⟩, ?_, ?_, fun i => Finset.singleton_nonempty _⟩
    · have hPS : P ∈ S := Finset.mem_filter.mpr
        ⟨Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr (fun h0 => hP₀ (hP.symm.trans h0)), hP⟩
      exact ⟨e ⟨P, hPS⟩, by simp [G]⟩
    · rintro ⟨i, hi⟩
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hi
      subst hi
      exact (Finset.mem_filter.mp (e.symm i).2).2
    · intro i j P hi hj
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hi hj
      exact e.symm.injective (Subtype.ext (hi.symm.trans hj))
    · intro i P hP Q hQ hPQ
      rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hP hQ
      exact absurd (hP.trans hQ.symm) hPQ
  obtain ⟨X₂, p, _, _, hproj, hsm, _, _, R, Δ₂, hΔp, hpΔ, hΔ₂, hΔ₂01, hsub, hcoh⟩ :=
    exists_cover_clearing_partition S.card k f Δ hΔ hΔ01 hP₀ G hG
  set b := a.num
  obtain ⟨hBp, B', hpB, hret⟩ := hcoh B
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f) := hproj
  haveI : CompactSpace X₂ := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (p ≫ f)
  have hsmX : IsSmoothScheme f := (isSmoothScheme_iff f).mpr inferInstance
  have hsmX₂ : IsSmoothScheme (p ≫ f) := (isSmoothScheme_iff (p ≫ f)).mpr hsm
  have hq : ∀ D : QDivisor X, D.IsQCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX
  have hq₂ : ∀ D : QDivisor X₂, D.IsQCartier := MMP.Fourfold.isQCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX₂
  have hgen : ∀ G : QDivisor X, ∀ Z : irreducibleComponents X₂,
      p (componentGenericPoint X₂ Z) ∉ G.supp :=
    fun G => map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' p G
  set M₂ := QDivisor.pullback (f := p) M (hq M) (hgen M)
  have hpM : M.IsPullback p (hgen M) M₂ := QDivisor.isPullback_pullback (hq M) (hgen M)
  refine ⟨X₂, p, inferInstance, inferInstance, hproj, hsm, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    B' - b • R, M₂, Δ₂, hgen M, hpM, hΔ₂, hΔ₂01,
    lt_of_le_of_lt (Finset.card_le_card hsub) (Finset.card_lt_card (Finset.erase_ssubset ha)),
    ?_, hret⟩
  have hBQ : (Divisor.toQDivisor B).IsPullback p (hgen _) (Divisor.toQDivisor B') :=
    QDivisor.isPullback_toQDivisor
      (MMP.Fourfold.isCartier_of_isSmoothScheme hsmX B) (hgen _) hpB
  have hMΔ : (M + Δ).IsPullback p (hgen _) (M₂ + (Δ₂ + b • Divisor.toQDivisor R)) :=
    qDivisor_isPullback_add p (hq M) (hq Δ) (hgen _) hpM hpΔ
  have h1 := numericallyEquivalent_of_isPullback k (p ≫ f) f p rfl hB hBQ hMΔ
  have h2 := numericallyEquivalent_add_right k (p ≫ f) h1 (hq₂ (-(b • Divisor.toQDivisor R)))
  have e1 : Divisor.toQDivisor B' + -(b • Divisor.toQDivisor R) =
      Divisor.toQDivisor (B' - b • R) := by
    rw [map_sub, map_zsmul, sub_eq_add_neg]
  have e2 : M₂ + (Δ₂ + b • Divisor.toQDivisor R) + -(b • Divisor.toQDivisor R) = M₂ + Δ₂ := by
    abel
  rwa [e1, e2] at h2

/-- **The covering trick.** Let `f : X ⟶ Spec k` be a smooth projective variety over an
algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, `B` a divisor and `M`, `Δ` `ℚ`-divisors on `X`
with `Δ` snc, all coefficients of `Δ` in `[0, 1)`, and `B ≡ M + Δ`. Then there are a smooth
projective variety `p ≫ f : Z ⟶ Spec k`, with `p : Z ⟶ X` finite and surjective, and a divisor
`B_Z` on `Z` numerically equivalent to the pull-back `p^* M`, such that for every `i` the space
`H^i(X, 𝒪_X(-B))` is a retract of `H^i(Z, 𝒪_Z(-B_Z))`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km2c_covering_trick"]
public theorem exists_isFinite_retract_cohomologyOverField_divisorialSheaf_neg
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] [CharZero k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsProjectiveVariety k f] [Smooth f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] (B : Divisor X) (M Δ : QDivisor X) (hΔ : Δ.IsSNC f)
    (hΔ01 : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ Δ.coeff P ∧ Δ.coeff P < 1)
    (hB : (Divisor.toQDivisor B).NumericallyEquivalent k f (M + Δ)) :
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (p : Z ⟶ X) (_ : IsFinite p) (_ : Surjective p)
      (_ : IsProjectiveVariety k (p ≫ f)) (_ : Smooth (p ≫ f))
      (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian Z) (_ : IsNormal Z)
      (BZ : Divisor Z) (MZ : QDivisor Z)
      (hM : ∀ C : irreducibleComponents Z, p (componentGenericPoint Z C) ∉ M.supp),
      M.IsPullback p hM MZ ∧ (Divisor.toQDivisor BZ).NumericallyEquivalent k (p ≫ f) MZ ∧
      ∀ i : ℕ, Nonempty (Retract (cohomologyOverField k f (-B).divisorialSheaf i)
        (cohomologyOverField k (p ≫ f) (-BZ).divisorialSheaf i)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ : ∃ n, Δ.frange.card = n := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  induction n using Nat.strong_induction_on generalizing X with
  | _ n ih =>
  by_cases hΔ0 : Δ = 0
  · subst hΔ0
    have hM := map_componentGenericPoint_notMem_supp_of_isDominant' (𝟙 X) M
    refine ⟨X, 𝟙 X, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_, ?_, inferInstance, inferInstance, B, M, hM,
      qDivisor_isPullback_id M hM, ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp] using ‹IsProjectiveVariety k f›
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp] using ‹Smooth f›
    · simpa only [Category.id_comp, add_zero] using hB
    · simp only [Category.id_comp]
      exact ⟨Retract.refl _⟩
  obtain ⟨X₂, p, _, _, _, _, _, _, B₂, M₂, Δ₂, hM, hpM, hΔ₂, hΔ₂01, hcard, hB₂, hret⟩ :=
    covering_trick_step k f B M Δ hΔ hΔ01 hB hΔ0
  obtain ⟨Z, q, _, _, hZp, hZs, _, _, BZ, MZ, hMZ, hqM, hBZ, hretZ⟩ :=
    ih _ (hn ▸ hcard) (p ≫ f) B₂ M₂ Δ₂ hΔ₂ hΔ₂01 hB₂ rfl
  haveI : IrreducibleSpace Z := by
    haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveVariety k (q ≫ p ≫ f) := hZp
    infer_instance
  obtain ⟨hM', hcomp⟩ := covering_trick_comp p q hpM hqM
  refine ⟨Z, q ≫ p, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_, ?_, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    BZ, MZ, hM', hcomp, ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hZp
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hZs
  · simpa only [Category.assoc] using hBZ
  · obtain ⟨r⟩ := hret i
    obtain ⟨r'⟩ := hretZ i
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    exact ⟨r.trans r'⟩

end CoveringTrick

end MMP.Mori
